// Conținut editorial per plajă — traducere ENGLEZĂ (106 din 188, în lucru).
// Aceeași structură ca beach-content-data.js (română), cheile sunt numele
// EXACT din attractions-data.js. Se încarcă DOAR când pagina cere lang=uk,
// nu la fiecare cerere — vezi server.js, unde e cerut condiționat.
module.exports = {
  "Plaja Golden Beach Thassos": {
    scurt: "Golden Beach (or Chrysi Ammoudia) is the longest, most popular and spectacular beach on Thassos. Stretching for several kilometres in a huge bay surrounded by green mountains, it fully lives up to its name thanks to fine sand that glitters like gold under the sun. The water is crystal clear with an extremely gentle entry, making it a dream spot where kids can play safely and adults can relax without a care.",
    cumAjungi: "The beach practically links two important tourist villages, Skala Potamia and Skala Panagia. Local buses exist, but they run on a fixed schedule and get packed in high season. With a rental car you have the freedom to explore both ends of the bay, drop your heavy bags a few steps from your sunbed, and drive up in the evening to the traditional village of Panagia for dinner under the plane trees. Parking is generous along the whole beach, with both free public spots and dedicated beach-bar parking.",
    echipament: [{ titlu: "Snorkelling mask", text: "Where the beach meets the rocky edges of the bay, marine life is very active and the water is perfectly clear." }, { titlu: "Kite or sand-game gear", text: "The beach is so wide and open in places that you have plenty of space for relaxed activities without bothering anyone else." }, { titlu: "Water-resistant sunscreen", text: "The sea breeze here is deceptive and it's easy to get sunburnt while walking along the long shoreline." }],
    preturi: "A set of two sunbeds with an umbrella costs between €10-15, though most beach bars will give you the sunbeds for free with a minimum drink purchase of the same value (a beer, coffee, or juice). A gyros at the beachfront taverns runs around €4-5, and a full meal for two comes to about €30-40.",
    turisti: [{ titlu: "A kids' paradise", text: "Parents consistently praise how far out you have to walk before the water reaches your waist." }, { titlu: "A lively beachfront", text: "Tourists appreciate having everything within a minute's walk: supermarkets, showers, a changing cabin, and excellent tavernas." }],
    tips: [{ titlu: "Best time to go", text: "Head to the left end of the beach (Skala Panagia side) for even finer sand and a completely wave-free sea — the most sheltered corner of the whole bay." }],
  },
  "Plaja Saliara (Marble Beach) Thassos": {
    scurt: "Saliara is arguably the most exotic and unique beach on Thassos. Instead of classic sand, the whole beach is made of small, perfectly rounded white marble pebbles (sourced from the nearby quarry). Because of this white backdrop, the sea takes on such an intense electric turquoise that you'd swear you were in the Caribbean or the Maldives. It's an incredibly photogenic spot, though the pure white glare reflects the sun very strongly.",
    cumAjungi: "The beach is isolated and tucked away on the island's north-east coast, and public transport doesn't reach it at all. From the paved main road toward Makryammos, you'll need to cover about 4-5km of unpaved forest track. It's a dusty road, full of bumps and stones, which is why a car is absolutely necessary to get there safely and without rushing. The lower parking area is set right in the pine forest and is free.",
    echipament: [{ titlu: "Polarised sunglasses", text: "Light reflected off the white marble pebbles is blinding at midday. Without good sunglasses, it's hard to enjoy the view." }, { titlu: "Beach sandals or aqua shoes", text: "The marble pebbles get extremely hot under the blazing sun, and walking barefoot to the water can be a real challenge." }, { titlu: "Underwater camera or waterproof case", text: "Water clarity in this bay is legendary — perfect for underwater filming and photos." }],
    preturi: "The beach is run entirely by one exclusive beach bar, so prices run higher than the island average. Renting a set of two sunbeds with an umbrella starts at €25-35 (depending on the row), and most of the time that price covers access only, not drinks. A coffee or beer at the bar costs around €5-6.",
    turisti: [{ titlu: "Get ready for dust", text: "Every visitor warns that after the drive in, your car will be covered in a fine layer of white marble dust." }, { titlu: "Very crowded in season", text: "Thanks to its social-media fame, the beach fills up completely from the early morning hours." }],
    tips: [{ titlu: "Best time to go", text: "Arrive very early, ideally before 08:45. You'll get the best shaded parking spot, a front-row sunbed, and be able to take stunning photos before the bay fills with people." }],
  },
  "Plaja Navagio Zakynthos": {
    scurt: "Navagio Beach (Shipwreck Beach) is, without a doubt, the most famous and photographed beach in all of Greece. Tucked into an isolated bay on the north-west coast, it's surrounded by vertical white limestone cliffs over 200 metres tall. On the fine white-pebble shore rests the wreck of the Panagiotis, which ran aground in 1980. The water colour here is truly surreal — a milky, glowing, neon-intense blue, caused by underwater sulphur springs and dissolved limestone.",
    cumAjungi: "The only way to reach the lower Navagio beach is by sea. Even so, you definitely need a car to reach the ports the speedboats leave from (such as Porto Vromi, Agios Nikolaos, or Skinari). The mountain road to these ports is spectacular, full of hairpin turns and dramatic scenery. On top of that, having a car lets you later drive up to the clifftop viewpoint for the famous overhead photo. Parking at the ports is free, but spots are limited in August.",
    echipament: [{ titlu: "Sturdy beach sandals or aqua shoes", text: "The beach isn't fine sand but round white pebbles that get very hot in the sun and can be painful to walk on." }, { titlu: "A thin windbreaker jacket", text: "The speedboats taking you into the bay move fast, and you can get quite wet from the spray." }, { titlu: "Hat and sunglasses", text: "The white cliffs reflect sunlight like a giant mirror, and down on the beach there's absolutely no shade or facilities." }],
    preturi: "A speedboat excursion ticket (usually including a stop at the Blue Caves) costs €20-30 per person. Since this is a fully protected, wild beach, there are no shops, bars, or sunbeds down there. Your only expenses will be the boat ticket and any snacks bought at the port before setting off.",
    turisti: [{ titlu: "Check the access rules", text: "Visitors often warn that, due to the risk of rockfall from the cliffs, authorities sometimes ban landing on the sand — in which case boats just stop in the bay for swimming straight from the boat." }, { titlu: "The water colour is real", text: "Every visitor confirms that the bright blue shade isn't an editing trick — it looks exactly like the photos." }],
    tips: [{ titlu: "Best time to go", text: "Choose an early departure from Porto Vromi, around 08:30-09:00. You'll reach the bay before the big cruise boats bring in hundreds of tourists at once, giving you a chance to enjoy the place in peace." }],
  },
  "Plaja Porto Katsiki Lefkada": {
    scurt: "Leaving Zakynthos behind, we start exploring the famous island of Lefkada with its very emblem: Porto Katsiki. This is one of the most spectacular and dramatic beaches in the entire world. A long strip of snow-white pebbles is squeezed at the foot of a vertical, huge, imposing limestone cliff. The Ionian Sea here takes on a uniquely milky-blue colour, electric in its intensity, that seems almost unreal. The scenery has a wild grandeur that will take your breath away from the very first glance.",
    cumAjungi: "Porto Katsiki sits in the south-western corner of Lefkada. The road is fully paved but a genuine challenge — narrow, full of tight bends, hairpins and steep descents through mountain villages. Public buses don't run efficient routes here, so a rental car is essential to arrive safely. Up on the plateau above the cliff there are a few large private car parks (around €10/day). From the car park, you reach the beach by descending roughly 100 sturdy concrete steps.",
    echipament: [{ titlu: "Aqua shoes are a must", text: "The beach is made of round white pebbles that can be quite painful underfoot and get very hot. You'll walk over pebbles into the sea as well." }, { titlu: "Be careful in the water", text: "The sea drops off extremely quickly (just two steps from shore), and in the afternoon big waves and strong currents can form. Not a beach recommended for unsupervised kids." }, { titlu: "A backpack instead of hand luggage", text: "Going down — and especially back up — the 100 steps with heavy bags is tiring; a backpack keeps your hands free for the railing." }],
    preturi: "Renting a set of two sunbeds with an umbrella costs €25-35 a day, among the priciest on the island. The canteens and tavernas above the cliff have a clever system: you can order food (gyros, burgers, salads) and drinks by phone or app, and the waiters bring your order right down to your sunbed. A frappe costs €4, and a quick lunch runs around €10-14.",
    turisti: [{ titlu: "Don't sit right against the cliff", text: "Visitors and authorities consistently warn about the risk of rockfall from the vertical cliff face, so it's much safer to set up your umbrella or sunbed near the water's edge." }, { titlu: "The sunset is spectacular", text: "Everyone raves about the moment the evening sun paints the huge limestone cliff in warm shades of orange and gold." }],
    tips: [{ titlu: "Best time to go", text: "Arrive very early, ideally before 09:00. You'll get a spot in the first car park by the stairs, find the sea calm as a swimming pool, and be able to soak in the grandeur of the place before dozens of cruise boats bring in thousands of tourists from Nidri starting around 11:00." }],
  },
  "Plaja Simos Elafonisos": {
    scurt: "Simos Beach consistently ranks among Europe's most beautiful beaches, and it's a genuine wonder of nature. Located on the small island of Elafonisos off the southern Peloponnese, Simos is a huge figure-eight-shaped beach formed by two twin bays set back to back, separated by a long tongue of fine, powder-soft pinkish-white sand. The water is such a bright, clear light turquoise that the bay feels like a tropical swimming pool plucked straight out of the Caribbean.",
    cumAjungi: "To reach this paradise, you definitely need a car to drive to the small port of Pounta in southern Laconia — the mainland road is fully paved. From Pounta, a short local ferry (just a 10-minute crossing) carries cars directly to Elafonisos island. Once you disembark, it's only 4km more along a paved dune road to the huge car park behind Simos beach. A car is vital for hauling family luggage and umbrellas onto the island. Beach parking is free.",
    echipament: [{ titlu: "No water shoes needed", text: "The entire bay's seabed is covered exclusively with fine, soft, clean sand, so the risk of stepping on anything sharp is zero." }, { titlu: "Your own umbrella and mat", text: "Since the beach is huge and ecologically protected, the organised sections cover only limited areas, leaving the rest of the beach with unlimited space for those who want to settle right on the dunes." }, { titlu: "Good polarised sunglasses", text: "The white sand reflects the strong midday light intensely." }],
    preturi: "A ferry ticket for car and passengers costs around €15-20 one way. On the organised sections of the beach, a set of two sunbeds runs about €15-20 a day. A frappe costs €4, and behind the beach there's an excellent family-run taverna where a full lunch will cost you around €12-15 per person.",
    turisti: [{ titlu: "A tropical paradise in Europe", text: "Every visitor is blown away by the stunning water colour and the fine sand with its pink shimmer." }, { titlu: "You never feel crowded", text: "Tourists appreciate the beach's impressive size, giving you huge personal space even in August." }],
    tips: [{ titlu: "Best time to go", text: "Arrive at the beach around 09:15 in the morning. The bay is incredibly calm in the early part of the day. Walk the paths between the two twin bays to admire the large sand dunes and the rare plants protected by law." }],
  },
  "Plaja Elafonisi Chania": {
    scurt: "Elafonisi is a genuine wonder of nature and one of the most spectacular beaches in the entire Mediterranean. Set in the south-western corner of Crete, it's a huge exotic lagoon world-famous for its fine sand with pink hues, caused by millions of crushed seashells. The Libyan Sea here has an unreal electric-turquoise shade and is extremely warm. A thin strip of sand, covered by very shallow water, connects the mainland to a small ecologically protected island, creating the scenery of a perfect tropical pool.",
    cumAjungi: "The beach lies roughly 75km south-west of Chania. The long distance and mountainous terrain make public transport fairly rigid, with only one bus a day, which fills up completely. A rental car is absolutely necessary to travel comfortably and at your own pace. The road crosses the island through gorgeous mountain passes and is fully paved, though winding. Behind the dunes there's a huge parking area (part of it a paid municipal lot, around €5, and free ground areas), just a few minutes' walk from the water.",
    echipament: [{ titlu: "No water shoes needed", text: "The whole lagoon's seabed is covered exclusively with fine, soft, clean sand, with an extremely gentle, pleasant slope underfoot." }, { titlu: "Your own umbrella and a thick mat (optional)", text: "Although there's a large organised sunbed area, it fills up instantly. The rest of the beach and the island offer unlimited space for towels, but pitching your own umbrella on the protected island is not allowed." }, { titlu: "Good polarised sunglasses", text: "The pinkish-white sand reflects the strong midday light intensely." }],
    preturi: "In the organised areas, a set of two sunbeds with an umbrella costs around €15-20 a day. Behind the beach there are a few large kiosks where you can buy a frappe (€4), a large bottle of water (€1.50), or a quick sandwich (€6-8). Public toilets cost around €1.",
    turisti: [{ titlu: "A tropical paradise in Europe", text: "Every review praises the unique turquoise shades of the water and the pink sparkle of the sand at the water's edge." }, { titlu: "Gets seriously crowded by afternoon", text: "Visitors warn that from around 11:00, hundreds of tour buses arrive at once, and the beach becomes very busy." }],
    tips: [{ titlu: "Best time to go", text: "Arrive at the car park very early, ideally before 08:45. You'll find the lagoon perfectly still, flat as a mirror, and be able to wade across the shallow water to the island in complete peace. Be sure to cross past the island's dunes toward the open sea, where you'll find small, intimate coves of rare beauty." }],
  },
  "Laguna Balos Kissamos": {
    scurt: "Balos is one of the most famous, photographed, and spectacular locations in the entire world. Set in the north-western corner of Crete, Balos is an exotic lagoon with fine sand, distinctive pink hues (from millions of crushed shells), and extremely shallow, warm, calm water ranging from light green to electric blue. It's a genuine tropical paradise in the middle of the Mediterranean.",
    cumAjungi: "Getting to Balos is quite the adventure. You have two options: the ferry from Kissamos (which ties you to a fixed schedule) or driving. If you want full freedom, a car is the best option, but be warned — the last 8km are an unpaved forest and rock track, fairly rough going. From the upper car park, you'll need to hike down about 20-30 minutes in the sun. Having a car means you can rest as soon as you climb back up the trail. Parking is free or involves a small environmental fee (around €1-2).",
    echipament: [{ titlu: "Comfortable trainers", text: "These will come in very handy for the hike from the car park down to the beach, and especially for the climb back up." }, { titlu: "Sun hat and plenty of water", text: "There's no natural shade at all along the trail, and the Cretan sun is strong from early morning." }, { titlu: "No water shoes needed in the lagoon", text: "Inside the lagoon, the seabed is exclusively fine, soft sand that's very pleasant underfoot." }],
    preturi: "There's a small snack kiosk near the car park and a beach bar set up in season, but prices are steep. Water or a soft drink costs around €4-5. A set of two sunbeds with an umbrella rents for €20-30, and spots fill up instantly.",
    turisti: [{ titlu: "The view from above is breathtaking", text: "Everyone recommends taking photos from the trail before descending, since that's where the lagoon's colour contrast shows best." }, { titlu: "The drive is tough but worth it", text: "Visitors warn to drive very slowly on the unpaved section." }],
    tips: [{ titlu: "Best time to go", text: "Arrive at the car park before 09:00 in the morning. You'll avoid the crowds and find the lagoon calm, before the big cruise boats from Kissamos bring in hundreds of tourists at once around 11:30." }],
  },
  "Kleftiko Milos": {
    scurt: "Kleftiko isn't a traditional beach, but a monumental complex of volcanic rocks, white stone arches, and spectacular caves rising straight out of the Libyan Sea. In the past, this hidden spot served as a refuge and secret base for pirates who raided ships in the Mediterranean. The water is legendarily clear, in shades of milky turquoise and emerald, and it's considered the most spectacular snorkelling and diving spot on the whole island.",
    cumAjungi: "Kleftiko sits in the island's south-western corner and is reachable almost exclusively by sea, via organised boat trips. Even so, you'll need a car to reach the main port in Adamas or the southern departure bay (Provatas Beach), from where boats leave daily. The roads to the ports are paved and quick. There's also a tough overland trail down through the mountains to Kleftiko, but it requires a 4x4 and a long, unmarked, potentially dangerous hike under the sun.",
    echipament: [{ titlu: "Snorkel mask and tube are essential", text: "You'll swim right through the pirate caves and under the huge stone arches; underwater visibility is absolutely stunning." }, { titlu: "Waterproof action camera", text: "The underwater scenery and white rocks make for incredible footage you'll definitely want to capture." }, { titlu: "Water-resistant sunscreen", text: "You'll spend a lot of time swimming out in the open, straight off the boat." }],
    preturi: "A full-day boat or catamaran trip to Kleftiko (often including lunch on board, drinks, and snorkelling gear) costs €40-70 per person, depending on the type of vessel. Down at the cave complex itself, there are no shops or facilities of any kind on land.",
    turisti: [{ titlu: "Milos's number-one experience", text: "Every review agrees that a holiday on Milos isn't complete without a boat tour to Kleftiko." }, { titlu: "Swimming through the caves is magical", text: "Visitors are fascinated by how sunlight streams through the rock openings, shifting the water's colour underwater." }],
    tips: [{ titlu: "Best time to go", text: "Choose a tour on a smaller boat or small sailboat that departs early, around 08:30. Smaller vessels can go much deeper into the narrow caves, letting you explore spots the big cruise boats can't reach." }],
  },
  "Plaja Myrtiotissa Corfu": {
    scurt: "Myrtiotissa is often described as one of the most isolated, wild, and charming hidden beaches on Corfu. Squeezed between huge limestone cliffs covered in lush, deep-green vegetation, this small beach offers fine silvery sand and extremely clean, transparent water. The spot has kept a bohemian, laid-back feel, historically known on the island as a partly naturist area for those seeking a total connection with unspoiled nature.",
    cumAjungi: "The beach lies on the west coast, right between the villages of Pelekas and Vatos. Public transport is completely non-existent for this secluded spot. You absolutely need a car to cover the main road, followed by a particularly steep, narrow secondary descent full of tight bends. Our tip is to leave your car for free at the dirt car park by the historic Myrtiotissa Monastery (halfway down the slope) and walk the last 300 metres, rather than risk getting your car stuck on the very steep stretch near the sand.",
    echipament: [{ titlu: "Your own beach umbrella", text: "The commercially organised area is minimal or non-existent depending on the month. Most of the space is completely free for towels." }, { titlu: "Snorkelling mask", text: "The large rocks bordering the bay continue underwater, creating spectacular channels full of small fish, great for exploring." }, { titlu: "A light backpack for the hike", text: "It will keep your hands free during the steep walk down and back up to the car." }],
    preturi: "Beach access is free. There's a small beach kiosk where you can occasionally rent sunbeds for €10-12 a set, or buy water or a frappe for €3-4. Near the monastery up top there's a small family taverna where a Greek salad or a portion of souvlaki costs around €8-11.",
    turisti: [{ titlu: "A hidden gem", text: "Visitors praise the wild beauty of the greenery-covered cliffs and the stunning clarity of the water." }, { titlu: "The drive needs your full attention", text: "Many reviews warn that the final slope is one of the steepest on Corfu and recommend walking down if you don't have a powerful car." }],
    tips: [{ titlu: "Best time to go", text: "Visit in the morning, around 09:00-11:30. The sun lights the western bay directly then, making the water look completely transparent. While you're there, visit the historic 14th-century Myrtiotissa Monastery, a picturesque, peaceful spot with olive trees right above the sea." }],
  },
  "Plaja Lindos Lindos": {
    scurt: "Lindos Beach (also known as Megali Paralia) is one of the most spectacular, history-rich spots in Greece. Set in a perfectly sheltered natural bay, the beach sits right below the famous whitewashed village of Lindos and its ancient acropolis perched on the rock above. The sand is fine and golden, and the sea is incredibly warm, clean, and calm — so still it feels like a giant open-air swimming pool set against a backdrop of rare historic beauty.",
    cumAjungi: "Lindos sits on the east coast, about 50km south of Rhodes Town. Buses connect it to the capital, but in summer the journey is tiring and the schedule limits you. A rental car gives you total freedom and comfort on a fast, fully paved road. The big challenge in Lindos is parking: the village itself is pedestrian-only, so you leave the car up in the large hillside car parks (some free, others around €5-7), then walk down to the beach along a paved path.",
    echipament: [{ titlu: "No water shoes needed", text: "The whole bay's seabed is covered in soft, extremely fine sand, making it a pleasure to walk barefoot through the water." }, { titlu: "Sun hat and high SPF protection", text: "The bay is sheltered from the wind, which means midday temperatures can get very high and the heat is felt strongly." }, { titlu: "Comfortable clothes and walking shoes", text: "After a few hours on the beach, it's practically a must to climb the narrow streets of Lindos village or visit the ancient acropolis." }],
    preturi: "Renting a set of two sunbeds with an umbrella costs around €15-20 a day. Right behind the beach there are charming tavernas serving excellent food. A frappe costs €4, a cold beer is €4.50, and a full meal based on fresh fish or traditional dishes runs around €15-18 per person.",
    turisti: [{ titlu: "Great for little ones", text: "Parents consistently praise the extremely gentle entry into the water, which stays shallow and warm for a long stretch from the shore." }, { titlu: "A postcard-worthy view", text: "Every tourist is captivated by the sight of the acropolis dominating the sky right above the sunbeds." }],
    tips: [{ titlu: "Best time to go", text: "Arrive around 09:00 in the morning. You'll find parking much closer to the village and get the pick of the sunbeds. For even more peace and quiet, head to the next bay over, called Pallas Beach, in the same area, where the atmosphere is a touch more secluded." }],
  },
  "Plaja Gerakas Zakynthos": {
    scurt: "Set at the southern tip of the Vassilikos peninsula, Gerakas is considered one of the most beautiful, clean, and protected beaches on Zakynthos. It's a long, wide strip of warm golden sand, flanked by clay hills and unusual rock formations. The beach is part of the National Marine Park and is a preferred nesting site for the famous Caretta-Caretta sea turtles, which is why it has remained completely unspoilt — no modern buildings or noisy water sports allowed.",
    cumAjungi: "The beach lies about 18km south of Zakynthos Town. The road is fully paved, winds pleasantly through olive groves, and is a nice drive. Local buses run rarely and on a rigid schedule, hard to fit around a relaxed beach day. A rental car gets you there quickly, and you can leave it in a large, free public car park about 200m from the beach. From there, a wooden boardwalk built specifically to protect the turtle nests in the dunes leads down to the sea.",
    echipament: [{ titlu: "Your own beach umbrella", text: "There's a small area where park volunteers rent eco-friendly wooden umbrellas, but they run out fast. Bring your own, but note that pitching it in the sand is only allowed in marked zones, to avoid disturbing turtle eggs." }, { titlu: "No water shoes needed", text: "The seabed is covered entirely in fine, clean sand, and the entry into the water is extremely gentle." }, { titlu: "Swimming goggles", text: "The water is warm, calm, and very clear — great for long swims." }],
    preturi: "Renting a simple eco-friendly umbrella costs around €5-7 a day (there are no plastic sunbeds here, just small folding chairs or a towel on the sand). At the trailhead there's a turtle information centre and a few excellent tavernas. A warm meal with traditional dishes will cost around €12-15 per person.",
    turisti: [{ titlu: "Strict rules, but necessary ones", text: "Visitors mention that park volunteers give you a quick briefing on arrival and explain the rules (no pointed umbrellas outside the permitted zones, and no staying on the beach after sunset)." }, { titlu: "Total peace and quiet", text: "Widely praised for the lack of loud music and motorboats." }],
    tips: [{ titlu: "Best time to go", text: "Come in the morning around 09:00. You'll catch an incredibly calm atmosphere, and if you're lucky, you might see volunteers marking new turtle nests made overnight. Also, avoid touching or climbing the clay hills at the end of the beach — it's forbidden, as the structure is extremely fragile and can collapse." }],
  },
  "Plaja Laganas Zakynthos": {
    scurt: "Laganas Beach is the epicentre of fun, nightlife, and vibrant tourism on Zakynthos. Stretching an impressive 9km along a huge bay in the south of the island, it's made of fine sand and lined with an unbroken row of modern beach bars, clubs, hotels, and tavernas. It's the place where music pulses all day long and the atmosphere is always festive — a favourite destination for young travellers from across Europe.",
    cumAjungi: "Laganas is just 8km from the island's capital and very close to the airport. The road is straight, flat, and busy. Though the resort is fairly well connected by public transport, a rental car gives you a huge advantage: parking in the centre of Laganas is a nightmare due to the crowds. With a car, you can head toward the far end of the beach (the Kalamaki or Agios Sostis area), where you can park for free on dirt lots behind the bars and access a much airier part of the bay.",
    echipament: [{ titlu: "Budget for a boat rental", text: "Laganas is the island's best spot to rent a small motorboat (no licence needed) to go looking for Caretta-Caretta turtles or visit Marathonisi Island (Turtle Island)." }, { titlu: "Headphones (if you want peace and quiet)", text: "Being very commercial, the beach has bar speakers running constantly." }, { titlu: "No special footwear needed", text: "The entry into the water is extremely gentle, entirely over fine sand, staying shallow for a long stretch out." }],
    preturi: "With so much competition, prices are affordable. Most beach bars give you a free set of two sunbeds with an umbrella if you order drinks worth a minimum amount (around €10-15 total). A large cocktail costs €7-9, a frappe is €3.50, and a quick lunch (gyros or club sandwich) runs €5-8.",
    turisti: [{ titlu: "The perfect spot for partygoers", text: "Young travellers consistently praise the nightlife and the clubs just steps from the sand." }],
    tips: [{ titlu: "Best time to go", text: "If you want to experience the famous nightlife, come to the beach in the late afternoon, stay for a sunset cocktail, then move to the resort's main street, which becomes fully pedestrian and buzzing after 21:00." }],
  },
  "Plaja Banana Beach Zakynthos": {
    scurt: "Banana Beach is the largest and widest sandy beach on the whole island of Zakynthos. Set on the Vassilikos peninsula, this impressive beach offers an exotic setting with fine golden sand and clear water that turns spectacular shades of turquoise in the sun. It's a lively, fully organised spot where modern beachfront bars blend seamlessly with huge open space. If you want comfort, good music, and plenty of room, Banana Beach is the place.",
    cumAjungi: "The beach lies about 14km from Zakynthos Town. Although buses run toward Vassilikos, their schedule is unpredictable and drops you well short of the shore. A rental car is by far the best option. The access road is fully paved, and from the main road you drop straight into a huge dirt car park under trees, where you can leave your car completely free of charge. The large parking area means you'll never stress about finding a spot, whatever the time.",
    echipament: [{ titlu: "Budget for water sports", text: "Banana Beach is famous for having the island's largest and best-equipped water sports centre (parasailing, flyboarding, jet skis, or inflatable towables)." }, { titlu: "No water shoes needed", text: "The seabed is an unbroken stretch of fine sand, ideal for sensitive feet, with an extremely gentle entry." }, { titlu: "Polarised sunglasses", text: "The huge expanse of golden sand reflects the midday light strongly." }],
    preturi: "Renting a set of two sunbeds with an umbrella costs around €15-25, depending on the row and the beach bar. A frappe costs €4, a cocktail runs €9-11, and a quick club sandwich or burger at the cosy restaurants behind the beach costs €10-12.",
    turisti: [{ titlu: "You never feel crowded", text: "Tourists praise the beach's size — even on the busiest August days, there's enough personal space for everyone." }, { titlu: "Excellent service", text: "Reviews often mention the quality of bars like Casa Playa and the presence of clean showers and changing rooms." }],
    tips: [{ titlu: "Best time to go", text: "Arrive around 10:00 to grab a spot in the front row of sunbeds. If you catch a day with a light southerly breeze, the sea will have small, fun waves — great for jumping in." }],
  },
  "Plaja Egremni Lefkada": {
    scurt: "Egremni is Lefkada's other legendary beach, located north of Porto Katsiki. It's a huge, imposing stretch of white sand mixed with fine pebbles, nearly 3km long, guarded by a tall, steep limestone cliff. Many consider the sea colour here to be the most beautiful in all of Greece — an electric, milky, incredibly intense blue. Thanks to its massive size, Egremni keeps a much wilder, freer, and airier feel than Porto Katsiki.",
    cumAjungi: "Set on the south-west coast, Egremni was accessible only by boat for years after the 2015 earthquake destroyed its stairway. Today, both the road and the steps have been fully rebuilt! You definitely need a car — the road is paved up to a point, followed by a dirt stretch where you can leave your car on the roadside (or in an improvised car park for €5-10). From there, it's about a 1km walk on a car-free road, followed by a descent of over 400 metal steps suspended on the cliff.",
    echipament: [{ titlu: "Plenty of still water and snacks", text: "Climbing back up the 400 steps in the sun is a real physical test. Bring hydration reserves!" }, { titlu: "Aqua shoes", text: "Very useful for walking comfortably over the fine pebbles on the shore and in the water." }, { titlu: "Your own beach umbrella", text: "Most of this huge beach is completely wild and unorganised, with no natural shade at all." }],
    preturi: "Beach access is free. In high season, there's a small organised area with sunbeds near the stairs, where a set costs around €20-25. There's also a small caravan/kiosk at the base of the stairs selling cold water or juice for €3-4. All other parts of the 3km-long beach are free and open to everyone.",
    turisti: [{ titlu: "The effort is 100% worth it", text: "Every visitor mentions the road and the steps are exhausting on the way back, but the unreal water colour and lack of crowds make Egremni an unforgettable experience." }, { titlu: "A dramatic sea", text: "Visitors note that waves can get quite large and powerful in the afternoon." }],
    tips: [{ titlu: "Best time to go", text: "Come in the morning, around 09:00. You'll go down the steps in shade (the huge cliff blocks the sun in the early morning) and enjoy the beach in much cooler conditions before the day's heat sets in." }],
  },
  "Plaja Kathisma Lefkada": {
    scurt: "Kathisma is the most cosmopolitan, vibrant, and longest organised beach on the island's west coast. It's a huge stretch of fine sand mixed with white pebbles, lapped by an electric-turquoise Ionian Sea. Unlike the wild beaches nearby, Kathisma is a haven of comfort: packed with modern beach bars, stylish beachfront pools, restaurants, and excellent water sports facilities.",
    cumAjungi: "The beach lies about 15km south of Lefkada Town. A rental car is by far the best option, as the road is fully paved, wide, and descends right down to the sand. The huge advantage is that you can park directly behind the beach — there's a large free public car park along the road, plus paid private ones offered by the bars (around €5-10).",
    echipament: [{ titlu: "No water shoes needed on the sandy sections", text: "The sand is very pleasant across most of the beach, though pebbles can appear right at the water's edge." }, { titlu: "Budget for a paragliding flight", text: "Kathisma is famous for tandem paragliding flights that take off from the mountain behind and land right on the beach." }, { titlu: "Be very careful in the sea", text: "The sea drops off quickly, and waves here can get huge and quite rough in the second half of the day." }],
    preturi: "Renting a set of two sunbeds with an umbrella costs around €15-25, depending on the bar and how close you are to the water. A frappe costs €4, a cocktail is around €10, and a full meal at the large restaurants above the beach runs €15-20 per person.",
    turisti: [{ titlu: "Excellent facilities", text: "Everyone praises the showers, changing rooms, and general cleanliness of the beach." }, { titlu: "Postcard-worthy sunsets", text: "The west-facing orientation delivers a stunning show as the sun sinks into the sea." }],
    tips: [{ titlu: "Best time to go", text: "For more peace, head to the far right end of the beach (facing the sea), past the large rocks in the water. That area is completely free, much less crowded, and perfect for a towel straight on the sand." }],
  },
  "Plaja Vai Lasithi": {
    scurt: "Vai Beach (officially known as Finikodasos) is one of Crete's most famous and spectacular destinations, offering scenery unique in all of Europe. What makes it famous is the huge wild Cretan palm forest (Phoenix theophrasti) that grows naturally right behind the sand, spreading over more than 20 hectares. The beach itself is a gorgeous crescent of fine golden sand, washed by a warm, clear, brilliant turquoise sea. It's a true exotic paradise corner that will make you feel like you're on a tropical island.",
    cumAjungi: "Vai sits in the north-eastern corner of the island, about 24km from Sitia and 94km from Agios Nikolaos. Due to its remote location at the island's edge, public transport is extremely rare and impractical. A rental car is absolutely essential for covering the fast, paved road. The site has a huge public car park on dirt ground, with an environmental fee (around €3-5 a day). Car access is very easy, with parking just a minute's walk from the first palm trees.",
    echipament: [{ titlu: "No water shoes needed", text: "The seabed is clean, entirely fine and pleasant sand, with a gentle entry." }, { titlu: "A charged camera or phone", text: "A short walk up steps on the rock on the right side of the beach leads to a superb viewpoint, where you can take the famous overhead photo of the palm forest and turquoise sea." }, { titlu: "Good polarised sunglasses", text: "The golden sand and palm leaves reflect the midday sun strongly." }],
    preturi: "As a major top-tier tourist attraction, the beach is fully organised. Renting a set of two sunbeds with an umbrella costs around €15-25 a day, depending on the row. A large restaurant and snack bar operate right at the edge of the forest. A frappe costs €4, a beer is €4.50, and a quick lunch or a fresh salad runs €10-14.",
    turisti: [{ titlu: "An unreal tropical oasis", text: "Every visitor is amazed by the unique beauty of the palm forest reaching all the way to the sand." }, { titlu: "Gets crowded at midday", text: "Reviews often warn that from 11:00 onward, lots of cars and buses arrive and the beach becomes fairly busy." }],
    tips: [{ titlu: "Best time to go", text: "Arrive at the car park around 09:00 in the morning. You'll get a shaded parking spot under the trees, a front-row sunbed, and total quiet in the forest. A local tip: from the top of the viewpoint rock, the path continues down the other side to a second beach (Psili Ammos), which is completely wild, unorganised, and much quieter." }],
  },
  "Red Beach Heraklion": {
    scurt: "Red Beach (or Kokkini Ammos) is one of the most spectacular, isolated, and unusual beaches in Crete. Tucked into a picturesque bay just south of Matala, it will take your breath away with its dramatic setting: the sand is an intense reddish-copper colour, and the bay is flanked by steep ochre sandstone cliffs. The sea has rare clarity, taking on brilliant emerald-green shades against the red sand. It's a fully wild beach, famous for its free-spirited, unconventional vibe.",
    cumAjungi: "There's no direct road access to the beach, as it's protected by a rocky mountain. You'll need a car to reach Matala, where you can leave your vehicle in the large car park in the resort centre (around €3-5 a day). From there, the adventure begins on foot: a demanding 25-30 minute hike over the hill. The path starts behind the village, is steep, rocky, and only partly marked, requiring real effort, especially on the way back up.",
    echipament: [{ titlu: "Comfortable trainers", text: "The path over the hill is full of loose stones and stretches where you need to scramble slightly over rock. Avoid basic flip-flops for this trail entirely!" }, { titlu: "A backpack with plenty of still water", text: "Resources down in the bay are extremely limited, and the effort of the hike under a blazing sun will dehydrate you quickly." }, { titlu: "No water shoes needed", text: "Once you're down, the reddish sand is fine and soft, and the entry into the sea is clean, free of large stones." }],
    preturi: "Beach access is free. In high season, a local opens a small improvised wooden shack right on the sand (the famous Yannis Mojito bar), where you can buy cold drinks or his famous cocktails for €7-9. Occasionally there are a few rustic wooden sunbeds to rent for around €10-15 a set.",
    turisti: [{ titlu: "A completely different place", text: "Visitors are fascinated by the unique sand colour and the artwork carved by visitors into the rocks at the edge of the beach." }, { titlu: "The trail is tiring but worth it", text: "Every review warns that climbing back over the hill at midday is very hard due to the heat." }],
    tips: [{ titlu: "Best time to go", text: "Set off early in the morning, around 08:30. You'll cross the hill in pleasant temperatures while the path is still partly shaded, and reach the red beach in complete peace before other tourists arrive. Note that a good part of the beach is traditionally used by naturist visitors — the spot is known for tolerance and mutual respect." }],
  },
  "Plaja Falassarna Chania": {
    scurt: "Falassarna is one of Crete's largest, cleanest, and most acclaimed beaches, regularly awarded the prestigious Blue Flag. Set on the west coast, it's actually a series of 5 huge beaches, all covered in fine, light-golden sand with a pinkish shimmer. The sea has legendary clarity, in a deep turquoise colour. Thanks to its massive size, Falassarna offers a rare sense of open space and total freedom, making it the perfect beach for anyone who loves comfort and plenty of room.",
    cumAjungi: "The beach lies about 52km west of Chania and 15km from Kissamos. Although a few regional buses run, a rental car gives you total comfort, with a modern, fully paved, fast coastal road. A big advantage at Falassarna is parking: behind each stretch of beach there are huge public dirt lots where you can park completely free, just steps from the sand — one of the easiest access points on the island by car.",
    echipament: [{ titlu: "No water shoes needed", text: "The whole beach and seabed are made entirely of fine, pleasant sand, with zero risk of stepping on anything sharp." }, { titlu: "Budget for water sports or volleyball", text: "Falassarna is very well equipped, with beach volleyball nets and excellent centres for renting surfboards or jet skis." }, { titlu: "Good sunglasses", text: "The huge stretch of sand reflects the strong midday light intensely." }],
    preturi: "In the areas run by modern beachfront bars, renting a set of two sunbeds costs around €15-25 a day, depending on the row. A frappe costs €4, a cold beer is €4.50, and a full dinner at the excellent traditional tavernas on the hills behind the beach costs around €13-16 per person.",
    turisti: [{ titlu: "Huge space and comfort", text: "Every visitor praises the impressive width of the beach, mentioning you never feel crowded, even on the busiest August weekends." }, { titlu: "Watch out for waves", text: "Reviews mention that, being fully open to the west, in the second half of the day the wind can create big, fun waves — ideal for jumping." }],
    tips: [{ titlu: "Best time to go", text: "Stay on the beach or at a taverna on the hill until late. Falassarna offers one of the most spectacular, clean, and stunning sunsets in all of Crete, the sun sinking straight into the open sea. For more peace, choose the northern section called Small Beach, more sheltered by the rocks." }],
  },
  "Plaja Sarakiniko Milos": {
    scurt: "Sarakiniko is one of Greece's most famous and photographed beaches, with a landscape that looks like the surface of the moon. There's no classic sand here, just a spectacular expanse of pristine white volcanic rock, shaped by wind and waves into flowing forms and narrow canyons. The sea has a deep electric-blue shade in contrast to the blinding white of the rock. It's a place of raw beauty that will make you feel like you've landed on another planet.",
    cumAjungi: "The beach is on the north coast of Milos. Public transport reaches it rarely, and the rigid schedule will make you miss the best hours of the day. A rental car is absolutely necessary to explore this spectacular area at your own pace. The access road is fully paved, and you can park for free in a large dirt lot right above the rock formations. From there, it's only a 2-3 minute walk.",
    echipament: [{ titlu: "Good polarised sunglasses", text: "The white volcanic rock reflects sunlight extremely strongly, just like snow in winter." }, { titlu: "Your own umbrella or beach tent", text: "Sarakiniko is 100% public and unorganised. There are no sunbeds, bars, or natural shade." }, { titlu: "Grippy footwear (trainers)", text: "Although the rocks look smooth, walking in basic flip-flops on the polished, steep shapes can be slippery and dangerous." }],
    preturi: "Access to the rocks and parking are completely free. In high season, a food truck sets up in the parking area, where you can buy cold water or a frappe for €3.50-4. There are no other commercial costs down in the bay.",
    turisti: [{ titlu: "Magazine-worthy photos", text: "Everyone recommends exploring the small caves and tunnels carved into the white rock — incredibly photogenic spots." }, { titlu: "Cliff jumping", text: "The braver visitors praise the high points where you can jump straight into the deep, clean water." }],
    tips: [{ titlu: "Best time to go", text: "Arrive either at sunrise (for a mystical, totally empty atmosphere) or after 17:00. The warm sunset light paints the white rocks in pale shades of pink and gold, and if you stay after dark on full-moon nights, the scenery becomes truly otherworldly." }],
  },
  "Plaja Firiplaka Milos": {
    scurt: "Firiplaka is one of the longest, most comfortable, and spectacular beaches on Milos's southern coast. Unlike the tiny coves nearby, it offers a wide strip of fine, silvery sand, majestically flanked by huge volcanic rocks layered in warm shades of yellow, pink, and ochre. The sea is warm, rare in its transparency, and has a light turquoise shade — a gentle entry into the Libyan Sea, perfect for total relaxation.",
    cumAjungi: "The beach sits right next to Tsigrado beach, in the south of the island. Public transport is rare, with stops fairly far from the shore. A rental car gives you full comfort. The final stretch of the secondary access road is packed dirt, flat and easy to drive. Parking is free, on the roadside above the beach, but due to its popularity, spots close to the access path fill up fast after 10:00. A gentle dirt path leads down to the beach.",
    echipament: [{ titlu: "No water shoes needed", text: "The seabed is clean, entirely covered in fine sand that's pleasant to the touch, with zero risk of stepping on anything sharp." }, { titlu: "Good sunglasses", text: "The colourful volcanic rocks reflect the strong midday light straight onto the sand." }, { titlu: "A camera", text: "A huge boulder that's fallen into the sea right in the middle of the beach makes for a stunning photo backdrop." }],
    preturi: "The beach is partly organised. A set of two sunbeds with an umbrella in the area run by the eco-friendly beach bar costs around €15-20 a day. A frappe costs €4, cold water is €1.50, and quick snacks (sandwiches, salads) run €7-9. The rest of the beach is completely free for towels.",
    turisti: [{ titlu: "The most comfortable beach in the south", text: "Every visitor praises the perfect balance between the wild volcanic scenery and the presence of comfortable sunbeds." }, { titlu: "Great for families", text: "The gentle entry into the calm sea is a strong point often mentioned by parents." }],
    tips: [{ titlu: "Best time to go", text: "Arrive around 09:15 in the morning to get a parking spot close to the path. For more privacy, walk toward the far right end of the beach (past the huge rock in the water). That area is completely wild, quiet, and away from the bar's music." }],
  },
  "Canal d'Amour Sidari": {
    scurt: "Canal d'Amour (Canal of Love) is one of the most unique and unusual geological formations in all of Greece. Located in the resort of Sidari, the beach is made of layered yellow sandstone that wind and waves have sculpted into narrow channels, grottoes, and spectacular arches. The beach itself is tiny, set at the end of a turquoise-water channel. The spot is legendary and draws thousands of couples in love every summer.",
    cumAjungi: "Sidari sits in the extreme north of Corfu, about 36km from the capital. The main road is paved but crosses the mountains in the island's centre, with many narrow stretches and tight bends. A rental car gives you huge comfort for this long drive at your own pace. Near the channel there are small paid private car parks (around €4-5 a day) and free spots on the side streets behind the hotels.",
    echipament: [{ titlu: "A mat or thick towel", text: "Since the beach is tiny, most visitors settle right on the flat yellow sandstone platforms on the rocks." }, { titlu: "Snorkelling mask", text: "The soft sandstone continues underwater, creating fascinating underwater tunnels you can swim through." }, { titlu: "Don't leave valuables unattended", text: "The rocky area gets busy, so it's worth having a small waterproof backpack to carry with you." }],
    preturi: "Access to the natural landmark is free. On the rocks, a few rows of sunbeds are offered by bars for around €15 a set. A frappe costs €4, and a portion of pancakes or a quick snack at the bar pools behind is around €6-8.",
    turisti: [{ titlu: "The legend lives on", text: "Everyone mentions the local myth that couples who swim through the channel together stay in love for life, and single visitors will find their soulmate." }, { titlu: "Very crowded and noisy", text: "Reviews mention the spot is very touristy and tight, getting stifling by midday." }],
    tips: [{ titlu: "Best time to go", text: "Come in the late afternoon, around 17:30. Most tour buses have already left, the yellow rocks take on a warm orange glow in the sunset light, and the atmosphere becomes much more romantic and photo-friendly." }],
  },
  "Plaja Voidokilia Pylos": {
    scurt: "Voidokilia is one of the most spectacular, famous, and Instagram-worthy beaches in all of Greece. Picture a perfect crescent-shaped bay (or the Greek letter Omega), where two large rocky headlands narrow the opening to the sea, fully sheltering the water from waves. The sand is fine as talc, and the water is warm, very shallow, and an otherworldly turquoise. As a protected nature reserve of huge ecological and historical importance, the beach has remained completely untouched by commerce.",
    cumAjungi: "The beach lies on the Peloponnese's west coast, in the Messinia region, near the town of Pylos. Public transport doesn't reach this isolated nature reserve at all, so a car is absolutely essential. The final stretch of road is partly paved and partly narrow packed dirt, winding past the Gialova salt lake. Drive slowly and you can park for free right in the dirt lot behind the sand dunes, just a minute's walk from the beach.",
    echipament: [{ titlu: "Your own beach umbrella and tent", text: "Voidokilia is 100% public and unorganised. There are no bars, sunbeds, or kiosks on the sand. Come fully equipped with your own shade." }, { titlu: "A well-stocked cooler", text: "Bring plenty of cold still water and snacks, as the nearest shop is in the village of Gialova, a few kilometres away." }, { titlu: "No water shoes needed", text: "The whole bay's seabed is covered exclusively with fine, soft, clean sand, with zero risk of stepping on anything sharp." }],
    preturi: "Beach access and parking behind the dunes are completely free. There are no vendors on the sand, so your expenses here will be zero. For a warm lunch after the beach, it's best to drive 10 minutes to the charming tavernas on the seafront in the neighbouring village of Gialova.",
    turisti: [{ titlu: "A breathtaking landscape", text: "Every review praises the bay's perfect shape and the stunning water colour, like an exotic lagoon." }, { titlu: "Climb up to the castle for the view", text: "Many tourists recommend a short but steep hike up to the ruins of the old Paleokastro castle on the rock above the beach, which offers the best view of the bay's perfect Omega shape." }],
    tips: [{ titlu: "Best time to go", text: "Arrive at the car park around 09:00 in the morning. You'll find the access path quieter, the sea completely flat like a mirror, and enjoy the bay's peacefulness before the sun gets too strong. Please respect the protective signs around the sand dunes, home to rare plants protected by law." }],
  },
  "Plaja Costa Navarino Pylos": {
    scurt: "Costa Navarino beach (often associated with The Dunes beach or the beaches of Navarino Bay) is one of the most spectacular, long, and exclusive coastal destinations in the Messinia region of the Peloponnese. It's a huge stretch of fine, warm golden sand, caressed by the deep, clean waters of the Ionian Sea. Flanked by ecologically protected sand dunes and vast olive groves, the beach strikes a perfect balance between world-class resort luxury and untouched wild nature.",
    cumAjungi: "The beach lies on the Peloponnese's west coast, near the historic town of Pylos. The long distance from the main airports in Athens or Kalamata makes a car absolutely essential for travelling in this region. The main road is fully paved and modern, offering stunning mountain and sea views. For day visitors, there are well-signposted public access points where you can park completely free on the large dirt areas behind the sand dunes, just a minute's walk from the beach.",
    echipament: [{ titlu: "No water shoes needed", text: "The whole beach and seabed are covered exclusively with fine, soft, clean sand, making the entry into the open sea a real pleasure." }, { titlu: "Your own beach umbrella (optional)", text: "Since the beach is huge, the commercial organised sections only cover limited areas near the resorts, leaving the rest of the beach with unlimited space for towels." }, { titlu: "Good polarised sunglasses", text: "The long stretch of sand reflects the midday light strongly." }],
    preturi: "In the areas run by the luxury beach clubs, prices are fairly steep, with a set of sunbeds costing €20-40 a day depending on the facilities. That said, access to the free sections of the beach is completely free. A frappe costs around €4-5, and a meal at the excellent tavernas in nearby villages (like Gialova) costs around €15 per person.",
    turisti: [{ titlu: "Immaculate natural scenery", text: "Every review praises how well the sand dunes are protected and maintained, giving the beach a very select, clean feel." }, { titlu: "Memorable sunsets", text: "Visitors are captivated by the sight of the sun setting directly into the open sea, painting the sky in stunning shades of red and gold." }],
    tips: [{ titlu: "Best time to go", text: "Arrive around 09:30 in the morning, when the sea is usually extremely calm. If you're into history or nature, use the car in the afternoon to drive 10 minutes to the famous perfect-crescent Voidokilia beach or the ruins of Paleokastro castle, both right near Navarino Bay." }],
  },
  "Plaja Kavourotrypes Sithonia": {
    scurt: "Kavourotrypes (also known as Orange Beach) is arguably the most spectacular and exotic spot in all of Sithonia. It's not one single classic beach, but a network of intimate little coves hidden among pines and soft white limestone rocks, shaped by the waves into strange forms. The water here has such a clear, intense turquoise-emerald colour that the place feels cut straight out of an exotic island. It's a photographer's paradise, but also a favourite for those who love a bohemian vibe.",
    cumAjungi: "The beach is on Sithonia's east coast, about a 10-minute drive north of the resort town of Sarti. There's no big roadside signage, just a discreet turn onto a rough dirt track through the forest. Without a car, it's nearly impossible to find or reach it. Drive slowly, and you can leave your car completely free of charge in the shade of the pine forest behind, then it's about a 5-minute walk on narrow paths.",
    echipament: [{ titlu: "Snorkelling mask", text: "The smooth white rocks continue underwater, creating small caves and channels full of fish — one of the best snorkelling spots in the region." }, { titlu: "A mat or thick towel", text: "If you don't grab a spot on the small strips of sand, the best places to sit are directly on the flat white rock platforms, where a thin towel isn't very comfortable." }, { titlu: "Comfortable walking shoes", text: "Avoid basic flip-flops for the forest and rock path, as it's steep and slippery in places." }],
    preturi: "Most of the little coves are completely free and open to everyone. There's a single organised area with one beach bar (Portokali), where a set of two sunbeds with an umbrella costs around €15-20, often as a minimum-spend arrangement. A frappe costs around €4.50, and a quick sandwich runs €6-7.",
    turisti: [{ titlu: "Fills up extremely fast", text: "Since the coves are small, the beach feels packed almost immediately. Visitors recommend arriving very early to grab a spot on the sand." }, { titlu: "Incredible scenery", text: "Everyone praises the contrast between the green pines, white rock, and turquoise sea." }],
    tips: [{ titlu: "Best time to go", text: "Come before 08:30 in the morning. You'll get good parking, total peace and quiet, and be able to admire the water's clarity before it's stirred up by hundreds of tourists." }],
  },
  "Plaja Faliraki Faliraki": {
    scurt: "Faliraki Beach is the heart of entertainment and mass tourism on Rhodes. Stretching an impressive 5km along the east coast, this huge beach is made entirely of fine golden sand. The sea is clean, warm, with a gentle entry, sheltered from strong winds. Faliraki is probably the best-equipped beach on the island: an unbroken row of modern beach bars, tavernas, hotels, and shopping centres, giving it a lively, energetic atmosphere.",
    cumAjungi: "Faliraki is about 12km south of Rhodes Town. The road is a modern, wide, fully paved highway. Although it's the best-connected resort by public transport, a rental car gives you a huge advantage: since the beach is so vast, a car lets you quickly move from one end to the other, or visit the famous Faliraki Water Park (Greece's largest water park, on the nearby hill). Parking is simple and free in the large dirt lots behind the beach.",
    echipament: [{ titlu: "Budget for water sports", text: "Faliraki is a water sports paradise; you can try anything, from parasailing and jet skis to pedal boats and rental motorboats." }, { titlu: "No water shoes needed", text: "The seabed is entirely covered in fine, soft sand, with no stones or sea urchins." }, { titlu: "High-SPF sunscreen", text: "The long stretch of golden sand retains heat and reflects sunlight strongly all day long." }],
    preturi: "Heavy competition keeps prices very affordable. A set of two sunbeds with an umbrella costs around €10-15 a day, or is included with a minimum order at the bars. A frappe costs €3.50, a quick gyros is around €4, and a full family dinner at the countless tavernas behind the beach costs around €35-45.",
    turisti: [{ titlu: "Top-notch facilities", text: "Every visitor praises the complete amenities: plentiful showers, toilets, changing cabins, and lifeguards along the whole beach." }, { titlu: "Excellent for kids", text: "The gentle entry and soft sand are much appreciated by parents." }],
    tips: [{ titlu: "Best time to go", text: "If you want to escape the loud music in the central area and want more peace, head to the southern end of the beach (the area called Kathara Beach), near the fishing harbour. The atmosphere there is much more relaxed, the sand just as fine, and the scenery with small wooden boats is very picturesque." }],
  },
  "Plaja Tsambika Archangelos": {
    scurt: "Tsambika Beach is considered one of the most beautiful, largest, and most spectacular sandy beaches on the whole island of Rhodes. It's a huge stretch of shimmering golden sand, dramatically framed by bare mountain slopes. The sea has remarkable clarity, is warm, and has a gorgeous light turquoise shade. Its landmark feature is the historic Tsambika Monastery, perched on the huge vertical cliff guarding the beach's left side, giving the spot a backdrop of real natural grandeur.",
    cumAjungi: "The beach lies about 26km south of Rhodes Town. Local buses only drop you at the main road up top, from where it's a long, tiring walk in the sun. A rental car is absolutely essential to drive comfortably right down to the shore. The secondary access road is fully paved, modern, and fast. Parking is among the easiest on the island: since the beach is so vast, there's a huge public dirt area right behind it where you can park completely free, just steps from the sunbeds.",
    echipament: [{ titlu: "No water shoes needed", text: "The whole bay's seabed is made exclusively of soft, fine, clean sand, with zero risk of stepping on stones or sea urchins." }, { titlu: "Plenty of sand toys for the kids", text: "The sand quality and the extremely gentle slope into the sea make this an ideal, very safe beach for children." }, { titlu: "Budget for water sports or a mini water park", text: "There are excellent centres for renting pedal boats or trying the large inflatable water platforms." }],
    preturi: "A set of two sunbeds with an umbrella costs around €15 a day. Behind the beach there are a few large wooden canteens and tavernas run by locals. A frappe costs €3.50, a cold beer is €4, and a quick gyros or fresh salad runs €7-10.",
    turisti: [{ titlu: "An endless stretch of golden sand", text: "Every review praises the beach's size and the quality of the soft sand, calling it the perfect spot for a family relax day." }, { titlu: "A unique view from the cliff", text: "Visitors recommend driving and then climbing the 350 steps up to the hilltop monastery for a dreamlike panorama over the whole bay." }],
    tips: [{ titlu: "Best time to go", text: "Arrive at the car park around 09:30 in the morning. The bay is incredibly quiet in the early part of the day, with the sun lighting the golden sand directly. For more free space to lay your towel, head toward the far right end of the beach, which is completely unorganised and very open." }],
  },
  "Plaja Sounion Riviera Ateniană": {
    scurt: "Sounion Beach offers an overwhelmingly beautiful historic setting, sitting right at the foot of the huge cliff on which the famous Temple of Poseidon (built in the 5th century BC) stands. The beach is tucked into a picturesque cove covered with fine golden sand and small white pebbles. The water is extremely clean, warm, and a brilliant turquoise, offering the unique experience of swimming in the Aegean Sea while admiring the ancient temple's white marble columns straight from your sunbed.",
    cumAjungi: "The beach lies at the southernmost point of Attica, about 65km from Athens. The long distance and lack of regular bus routes make a car absolutely essential for a relaxed trip. The coastal road is fully paved, modern, and offers spectacular views. Parking is free, either on the side of the secondary road leading down to the beach or in the dedicated spaces of the seafront tavernas, just a minute's walk from the water.",
    echipament: [{ titlu: "No water shoes needed", text: "The seabed in the central area is clean, made entirely of fine sand, with a very pleasant entry." }, { titlu: "A charged camera or phone", text: "The sight of the ancient temple on the cliff above the sunbeds is simply spectacular and an essential holiday photo." }, { titlu: "A stylish sun hat", text: "Being sheltered from strong winds, the bay gets noticeably hot at midday." }],
    preturi: "As a highly sought-after historic location, prices are mid-to-high range. A set of two sunbeds with an umbrella costs around €15-25 a day, depending on proximity to the water. A frappe costs €4, and the excellent traditional tavernas on the seafront serve very good food. A full meal will cost around €15-20 per person.",
    turisti: [{ titlu: "A one-of-a-kind mythological setting", text: "Every review is captivated by the grandeur of the place and the special feeling of swimming under the sea god's watchful eye." }, { titlu: "Very safe for kids", text: "Visitors praise the gentle water gradient and the lack of big waves." }],
    tips: [{ titlu: "Best time to go", text: "Plan your day so you're on the beach in the morning around 09:30, when the bay is calm. In the late afternoon, drive up to the Temple of Poseidon — the sunset seen from the ancient rocks is considered the most beautiful and spectacular in all of mainland Greece." }],
  },
  "Plaja Agios Gordios Corfu": {
    scurt: "Agios Gordios is one of the most spectacular and imposing beaches on Corfu's west coast. Set in a huge bay, the beach is framed by green mountains covered in pine forests and olive groves that seem to tumble into the Ionian Sea. It's a long, wide beach, made mostly of fine golden sand. Its emblematic feature is the huge Ortholithi rock, rising majestically straight out of the turquoise water on the bay's left side, giving the scene a dramatic, storybook backdrop.",
    cumAjungi: "The beach lies about 15km south-west of the capital, Corfu Town. The road crossing the island through mountain villages (like Sinarades) is fully paved but fairly narrow, full of tight bends and steep descents toward the coast. Green buses run on a rigid schedule, making a rental car the better option. Parking near the sand can be a challenge in season; there are paid private car parks close to the shore (around €5 a day) or free spots along the access road if you arrive early.",
    echipament: [{ titlu: "No water shoes needed in the central area", text: "The seabed is covered with soft, very fine sand, ideal for sensitive feet, though a few stones can appear near the edges." }, { titlu: "A charged camera or phone", text: "The isolated offshore rock and the spectacular sunset make for great photo material." }, { titlu: "Snorkelling mask", text: "Near the large rocks at the ends of the bay, underwater life is quite active." }],
    preturi: "Renting a set of two sunbeds with an umbrella costs around €12-18 a day. Along the seafront there are numerous excellent bars and tavernas. A frappe costs €4, a gyros on the seafront is €4.50, and a full family dinner at the traditional tavernas costs around €35-45.",
    turisti: [{ titlu: "Scenery that wins you over", text: "Every visitor praises the grandeur of the green mountains and the beauty of the offshore Ortholithi rock." }, { titlu: "Great for families and swimmers", text: "Tourists appreciate the fairly gentle entry into the clean sea and the beach's excellent organisation." }],
    tips: [{ titlu: "Best time to go", text: "Stay on the beach until late. Facing due west, Agios Gordios delivers an amazing show as the sun sinks into the open sea. For more peace, head to the left end of the beach (toward the rock), where the area is more open and you can lay your towel straight on the sand." }],
  },
  "Plaja Afandou Afandou": {
    scurt: "Afandou Beach is one of the longest, most expansive beaches on Rhodes, stretching an impressive nearly 4km. Made of a mix of coarse sand and fine, wave-rounded pebbles, this huge bay is the very definition of space and freedom. Thanks to its massive size, Afandou never feels crowded, making it the ideal spot for tourists who want to escape the crowds and enjoy an extremely clean, deep, and refreshing sea.",
    cumAjungi: "The beach lies on the east coast, about 20km from Rhodes Town and very close to Faliraki. Public transport only drops you at the edge of Afandou village, from where it's over a kilometre's walk in the sun. A car is absolutely necessary to reach the shore directly. Access from the main road is fully paved, flat, and very easy. Parking is among the easiest on the island: you can leave your car completely free right behind the beach, along the long road that follows the shoreline.",
    echipament: [{ titlu: "Aqua shoes", text: "Highly recommended for stepping comfortably over the band of pebbles at the entry into the deeper sea." }, { titlu: "Your own beach umbrella", text: "Most of this huge beach is completely wild and unorganised, giving unlimited space for anyone who wants to lay out a towel." }, { titlu: "Snorkelling mask", text: "Since the water is extremely clear and clean, underwater visibility is excellent, especially near the rock formations at the end of the beach." }],
    preturi: "In the few organised sections near guesthouses, a set of two sunbeds costs around €10-12 a day. A few caravans and local tavernas are scattered along the coast. A large bottle of still water costs €1.50, a frappe is €3.50, and food prices are considerably lower than in Lindos.",
    turisti: [{ titlu: "A huge beach all to yourself", text: "Visitors are delighted at how much distance you can keep from the next tourist, even in peak summer." }, { titlu: "The water deepens quickly", text: "Reviews mention the sea gets deep after just 3-4 steps from shore, making it ideal for strong swimmers." }],
    tips: [{ titlu: "Best time to go", text: "Head to the far right end of the beach (the area known as Traganou), where large rocks hide spectacular sea caves. It's the most photogenic spot on the beach and offers welcome natural shade in the afternoon." }],
  },
  "Plaja Prasonisi Prasonisi": {
    scurt: "Prasonisi is a one-of-a-kind place in the world and one of Greece's most spectacular geographical attractions. At the very southern tip of Rhodes, Prasonisi is a peninsula (or an island connected to the mainland by a long strip of fine sand) where two different seas meet: the Aegean and the Mediterranean. The phenomenon creates a stunning contrast: on one side of the sand spit the sea has big waves and strong wind, making it a world-class windsurfing haven, while on the other side the water is completely flat, calm, and still.",
    cumAjungi: "Prasonisi lies about 90km south of Rhodes Town. Due to the long distance and its isolated location, public transport is almost non-existent. A car is absolutely essential to reach this end-of-the-world spot. The island's main road is fully paved, flat, and very straight in its final stretch. Once you arrive, you can drive right onto the wide sand strip at the base of the beach, where parking is huge and completely free. Just be careful not to park too close to the water, to avoid getting stuck in wet sand at high tide.",
    echipament: [{ titlu: "Polarised sunglasses and a scarf", text: "The wind blows strongly here almost constantly, kicking up fine sand, so eye protection is essential." }, { titlu: "A kite or sturdy beach gear", text: "Even if you don't windsurf, simply walking the sand spit where the two seas meet is a memorable experience." }, { titlu: "No large inflatable mattresses", text: "Due to the strong wind on the Aegean side, there's a real risk of being carried out to sea." }],
    preturi: "Beach access is free. There are a few sunbed sections in the sheltered area, where a set costs around €15. A small tourist village has grown up behind the beach, full of windsurfing schools, gear shops, and tavernas. A full lunch costs around €12-15 per person, and renting windsurf or kitesurf gear starts at €40 an hour.",
    turisti: [{ titlu: "A show put on by nature", text: "Every review praises the unique feeling of standing on a strip of sand with big waves on your right and a sea as calm as a lake on your left." }, { titlu: "A camera is a must", text: "The sight of hundreds of colourful sails against the blue sky makes for incredible photos." }],
    tips: [{ titlu: "Best time to go", text: "If you want to explore the rocky island at the end of the beach, go for a walk in the morning. In years when the tide doesn't cover the sand strip, you can walk straight across to the island and climb up to the old lighthouse at the top, which offers a stunning panorama over the \"kiss of the two seas\"." }],
  },
  "Plaja Aliki Thassos": {
    scurt: "Aliki is one of the most charming, history-rich spots on Thassos. Set on a narrow peninsula in the island's south-east, it actually offers two twin beaches back to back. The main bay is small, fully sheltered from the wind, and looks like it's straight out of a postcard: emerald water, fine sand, and charming taverna tables that almost touch the sea. On top of that, the site is scattered with ancient Greek and Roman ruins.",
    cumAjungi: "Aliki is about 30km from Limenas (the island's capital). The main road around the island is paved and immaculate, offering superb sea views, though with quite a few slopes and bends. A car is the most comfortable way to get there, letting you arrive early — parking is the big challenge at Aliki. Space is limited along the main road, and the walk down to the beach is a short footpath.",
    echipament: [{ titlu: "Comfortable walking shoes (sandals or light trainers)", text: "The peninsula hides the ruins of an ancient temple and a former Roman marble quarry partly submerged in the sea. A 20-minute walk among the pines to see them is well worth it." }, { titlu: "Snorkelling mask", text: "The water is extremely calm and sheltered, perfect for a long session exploring the seabed." }],
    preturi: "Given the tight space, the tavernas manage the sunbeds on the sand. A set of sunbeds is usually free if you have lunch there (or with a minimum spend of around €20-30). A portion of fresh fish or seafood costs around €12-16.",
    turisti: [{ titlu: "Excellent seaside dining", text: "Everyone praises the experience of enjoying a traditional Greek lunch just steps from the emerald water." }, { titlu: "Very crowded in July and August", text: "Since the bay is small, sunbeds are placed fairly close together, and the beach fills up quickly." }],
    tips: [{ titlu: "Best time to go", text: "If you want to avoid the crowds on the main taverna-lined beach, walk to the other side (the beach behind the peninsula). It's much wilder, often unorganised, and perfect for those who want a quiet spot with just a towel." }],
  },
  "Plaja Sani Kassandra": {
    scurt: "Sani Beach is the definition of luxury and elegance on the Kassandra peninsula. Set inside a huge private complex of 5-star resorts, this beach will surprise you with powder-fine white sand and unreal, brilliant turquoise water. Everything is framed by an immaculately maintained pine forest and an exclusive promenade, giving the place a sophisticated vibe reminiscent of Saint-Tropez.",
    cumAjungi: "Sani Resort sits on the north-west coast of the Kassandra peninsula. Although it's a private area, the beach is accessible to all visitors. Public transport has no direct or efficient routes into the heart of the complex, so a rental car is essential to get there comfortably. The road is fully paved and well signposted. For day visitors, the complex offers huge organised car parks (some free, others paid, near the private marina). A car also gives you the freedom to stay late for Sani's famous sunset.",
    echipament: [{ titlu: "Light but elegant evening wear", text: "The private marina (Sani Marina) is lined with fine restaurants and luxury boutiques — well worth a stroll after the beach." }, { titlu: "No water shoes needed", text: "The seabed is an unbroken stretch of fine, clean, extremely soft sand, with no stones or sea urchins." }, { titlu: "Polarised sunglasses", text: "The fine white sand reflects the midday sun strongly." }],
    preturi: "As an exclusive destination, prices run well above the Halkidiki average. Renting a set of two sunbeds with an umbrella in the hotel-run areas can cost €30-50 (or more in peak season). There are, however, small free stretches where you can lay a towel for nothing. A frappe or juice at the beach bars costs around €6-7, and dinner at the marina restaurants starts from €25-30 per person.",
    turisti: [{ titlu: "Top-tier service and cleanliness", text: "Every review praises the immaculate cleanliness of the sand (raked daily) and the staff's attention to detail." }, { titlu: "The sunset is a must", text: "Visitors mention the sunsets seen from the hill by Sani's old tower are the most beautiful in the region." }],
    tips: [{ titlu: "Best time to go", text: "Arrive around 09:00 in the morning. You'll find parking easily and enjoy the bay's full quiet before resort guests come down to the beach. If you're there in summer, check whether the Sani Festival is on — there are brilliant open-air jazz concerts right on the hill by the sea." }],
  },
  "Plaja Karidi Sithonia": {
    scurt: "Karidi Beach, in the Vourvourou area, is considered Sithonia's natural gem and the ideal family beach. Picture a perfectly enclosed bay, sheltered from the wind, where the sand is so fine and white it feels like talcum powder. The sea is warm as a bath, has no waves at all, and stays so shallow you have to walk dozens of metres out before the water passes your knees. The backdrop is decorated with age-old pines in spectacular shapes.",
    cumAjungi: "Karidi is at the edge of Vourvourou village. Although you could walk if you're staying very close, most tourists come from other resorts, in which case a car is indispensable. The road to the beach is paved, and the pleasant surprise is that you can park completely free right in the pine forest behind the sand, just 20 metres from the sea. This makes carrying beach toys and cooler bags extremely easy.",
    echipament: [{ titlu: "Your own beach umbrella", text: "Karidi is a 100% wild, unorganised beach. There are no sunbeds or umbrellas to rent, so you'll need to bring everything from home." }, { titlu: "Large inflatable mattresses", text: "Since the sea is completely flat like a mirror, this is the perfect island spot for hours of relaxed floating." }, { titlu: "No water shoes needed", text: "The seabed is entirely fine, extremely soft, clean sand, with no stones or sea urchins." }],
    preturi: "Being a free beach, the cost is zero. In high season, 1-2 mobile canteens set up in the forest behind, selling water, frappe, juice (around €3-4) and doughnuts or sandwiches (€5-7). For a proper lunch, you'll need to drive 3-4 minutes to the tavernas in central Vourvourou.",
    turisti: [{ titlu: "A kids' paradise", text: "Every parent praises the total safety offered by the shallow, wave-free water for little ones." }, { titlu: "The pines give brilliant shade", text: "Many tourists mention that if you grab a spot early under the edge pines, you don't even need a beach umbrella." }],
    tips: [{ titlu: "Best time to go", text: "Come in the morning before 09:00. The bay gets very crowded during the day. A local tip: on the right side of the beach, past the rounded rocks, there's a second, smaller beach (Micro Karidi) that's often much quieter." }],
  },
  "Plaja Kalamaki Zakynthos": {
    scurt: "Kalamaki Beach sits in the same huge bay as Laganas, but is its polar opposite in terms of atmosphere. It's an extremely calm, clean, and airy beach, with fine golden sand stretching flawlessly to crystal-clear water. As a key zone for the National Marine Park (most of the turtle nests are here), the beach has been spared aggressive commercial development, offering deep relaxation amid nature.",
    cumAjungi: "Kalamaki is just 5km from Zakynthos Town and is essentially the quieter neighbour of Laganas resort. A rental car gives you total comfort on the paved road leading to the beach. There's a large public dirt car park right at the beach entrance, where you can leave your vehicle completely free. From there, it's just a minute's walk along a shaded lane.",
    echipament: [{ titlu: "Your own (eco-friendly) umbrella", text: "Although there's a small central area with a few sunbeds to rent, most of the beach is completely free. If you bring your own umbrella, volunteers will show you exactly where to place it to avoid the underground nests." }, { titlu: "No ball games or water sports", text: "Ball games or racquets near the dunes are restricted so as not to stress the protected wildlife. The beach is dedicated exclusively to swimming and relaxing." }, { titlu: "A camera", text: "The sandstone cliffs at the end of the beach (the area called Crystal Beach) make a superb photo backdrop." }],
    preturi: "A set of two sunbeds with an umbrella in the small organised area costs around €12-15. Behind the beach (a few minutes' walk) there are a few charming tavernas and hotels. A frappe costs €3.50, and a large Greek salad or light lunch runs €8-12.",
    turisti: [{ titlu: "An incredibly gentle entry", text: "Every family with young kids praises being able to walk dozens of metres out with the water only reaching their knees, the seabed being like a floor of fine sand." }, { titlu: "Planes fly over the beach", text: "Tourists mention as a fun quirk that planes landing at the nearby airport fly fairly low, right over the Kalamaki bay." }],
    tips: [{ titlu: "Best time to go", text: "Head to the far right end of the beach (facing the sea), where the large sandstone rocks meet the sand. The atmosphere there is even more intimate, and the water is usually extremely warm. Note that the beach must close an hour before sunset, when park volunteers begin clearing it to let turtles come ashore to lay their eggs." }],
  },
  "Plaja Dafni Zakynthos": {
    scurt: "Dafni Beach is one of the wildest, most isolated, and authentic hidden beaches on Zakynthos. Set inside the Laganas bay but tucked behind steep hills, Dafni will surprise you with spectacular scenery: a wide strip of coarse sand mixed with pebbles, incredibly warm water, and a superb direct view toward the uninhabited island of Pelouzo. As a strictly protected environmental area, there are no big hotels or bar chains here, and the place keeps the feel of an old-fashioned Greek taverna spot.",
    cumAjungi: "Reaching Dafni Beach is the main reason you absolutely need a sturdy car. From the paved main road in Vassilikos, a secondary dirt and gravel road, about 3-4km long, winds down the hillside. The road is very steep, narrow, dusty, and full of serious bumps, considered one of the toughest driving routes on the island. Buses don't reach here under any circumstances. At the bottom, local tavernas offer large, completely free parking spaces under improvised netted shade for their customers.",
    echipament: [{ titlu: "Aqua shoes", text: "Although there's plenty of warm sand on shore, the water's entry has a band of flat rocks and underwater boulders where small sea urchin colonies have settled." }, { titlu: "Snorkelling mask", text: "As the water is extremely clean and calm (sheltered by Pelouzo island), the underwater rocky area is full of interesting marine life to explore." }, { titlu: "High-SPF sunscreen", text: "The bay is very warm, with some of the highest water temperatures on the island, so you'll spend a lot of time swimming." }],
    preturi: "The system on the beach is very welcoming: the small family tavernas behind offer the sunbeds on the sand for free or with a minimum spend at their terrace (a coffee or beer bought from them). Food prices are very fair for Zakynthos: a portion of freshly grilled fish or traditional oven dishes costs around €10-14.",
    turisti: [{ titlu: "The road is scary, but the beach is a paradise", text: "Every review mentions the drive is very demanding and requires full attention, but once you're down, the beauty and peace of the place make the effort worthwhile." }, { titlu: "The warmest water on the island", text: "Tourists praise the incredibly pleasant sea temperature in this sheltered bay." }],
    tips: [{ titlu: "Best time to go", text: "Arrive around 09:30 in the morning to make the descent before other cars come up in the opposite direction (the road being very narrow, two cars passing each other requires careful manoeuvring). Also, respect the wooden or wire cages set up on the sand — they protect active Caretta-Caretta turtle nests." }],
  },
  "Plaja Tsilivi Zakynthos": {
    scurt: "Tsilivi Beach is a long, vibrant urban beach, awarded the Blue Flag certificate for excellent water quality and organisation. Set on the island's east coast, the beach is made of fine sand and suits every type of tourist: from families with young kids, who appreciate the calm, shallow water, to young travellers looking for lively beach bars and water sports. The backdrop is completed by green hills full of olive trees.",
    cumAjungi: "Tsilivi is just 5km north of Zakynthos Town. If you're staying right in the resort, you can walk there in minutes. If you're coming from other parts of the island, a rental car will give you extra comfort. Parking right by the beach can be tricky at midday; there are, however, small dirt lots behind the main bars or free spots along the streets leading to the sea. With a car, you can also easily head to the quieter beaches in the north in the afternoon.",
    echipament: [{ titlu: "Beach paddles (beach tennis)", text: "The sand is fine and compact at the water's edge, ideal for dynamic games on shore." }, { titlu: "No special footwear needed", text: "The entry into the Ionian Sea is gentle, entirely over soft sand, with no stones or hazards." }, { titlu: "Water-resistant sunscreen", text: "You'll spend a lot of time in the sea, since the water stays shallow for a generous distance offshore." }],
    preturi: "Depending on the bar you choose, a set of two sunbeds with an umbrella costs €12-20. Many places offer the sunbeds with a minimum bar order. A gyros at the beachfront tavernas costs €4-5, and a full dinner for two comes to €35-45.",
    turisti: [{ titlu: "A complete beach", text: "Visitors appreciate having everything at hand: showers, toilets, lifeguards, shops, and a wide range of tavernas just steps from the sand." }, { titlu: "Very popular", text: "In high season, the beach gets quite lively and noisy in the central areas with music." }],
    tips: [{ titlu: "Best time to go", text: "For more peace, head to the far left end of the beach (the area called Bouka Beach), where there are fewer tourists and the scenery with the small fishing harbour offers a much more relaxed atmosphere." }],
  },
  "Plaja Mylos Lefkada": {
    scurt: "Mylos is one of the most spectacular, unspoilt beaches on Lefkada. Set in the north-west of the island, this huge stretch of white sand and fine pebbles is flanked by steep mountain hills and washed by an incredibly milky-blue sea. With no direct road access, the beach has kept a completely wild feel, untouched by commercialisation — the ideal destination for anyone seeking pure nature and freedom.",
    cumAjungi: "The beach is right by the picturesque village of Agios Nikitas. A rental car is needed to cover the island's main road up to the village entrance. Once in Agios Nikitas, you have two options to cross the hill to Mylos: either a 20-25 minute hike on a fairly steep, rocky path (offering a dreamlike view from above), or a water taxi (small boat) from the village harbour.",
    echipament: [{ titlu: "Your own beach umbrella is essential", text: "There are no beach bars or sunbed rentals at Mylos. It's just you and nature, so you'll need your own shade." }, { titlu: "A backpack with plenty of water and snacks", text: "There are no kiosks down there, and the effort of the hike or the strong sun will dehydrate you quickly." }, { titlu: "Trainers", text: "If you choose to walk the path over the hill, avoid flip-flops entirely." }],
    preturi: "Beach access is completely free. If you choose to go or return by water taxi (boat), a ticket costs around €5-7 per person, one way. In Agios Nikitas village, where you'll leave your car, a taverna lunch costs around €12-15 per person.",
    turisti: [{ titlu: "The view is worth every bit of effort", text: "Everyone praises the spectacular sight of the beach from the top of the hill path." }, { titlu: "Watch out for waves", text: "Tourists note that in the afternoon, very large waves and strong currents can form." }],
    tips: [{ titlu: "Best time to go", text: "Come early in the morning, around 09:00. You'll find it much easier to get a free parking spot at the entrance to Agios Nikitas village (parking becomes chaotic later) and cross the hill on foot in pleasant temperatures." }],
  },
  "Plaja Agios Ioannis Lefkada": {
    scurt: "Agios Ioannis is a huge, spectacular, and energetic beach at the very north of the island, just a step from the capital. It's a strip stretching for kilometres, made of white sand and fine pebbles, world-famous for its historic stone windmills at its edge and for being a haven for kitesurfing enthusiasts. The sea has an incredibly intense electric-turquoise shade, but it's dynamic, constantly exposed to strong breezes in the second half of the day.",
    cumAjungi: "The beach is just 3km from Lefkada Town. Although the distance is small, public transport doesn't run frequent routes to this open stretch of coast, making a rental car the best option. The road is fully paved, flat, and fast. A big advantage at Agios Ioannis is parking: the local road passes right behind the beach, and there's huge space along the roadside or in the bars' dedicated areas where you can park completely free, just steps from the sand.",
    echipament: [{ titlu: "Your own sturdy beach umbrella and tent", text: "The wind blows strong and steady almost every afternoon, so your umbrella needs to be well secured." }, { titlu: "Aqua shoes", text: "Although the shore is a sand mix, the entry into the open sea can have rock plates and small stones smoothed by waves." }, { titlu: "Good polarised sunglasses", text: "Light reflection off the turquoise water and white sand is very strong." }],
    preturi: "Since the beach is huge and mostly public, access is free. In the few areas organised by charming bars, a set of two sunbeds costs around €12-15 a day. A frappe costs €3.50, a cold beer is €4, and the excellent tavernas behind the beach serve traditional lunches for around €12-15 per person.",
    turisti: [{ titlu: "A show of colourful kites", text: "Every visitor is fascinated by the sight of dozens of kitesurfers filling the sky with colourful kites in the afternoon." }, { titlu: "The water has an unreal colour", text: "Reviews praise the unique electric-blue shades typical of the island's west coast." }],
    tips: [{ titlu: "Best time to go", text: "If you want a quiet swim or are with kids, come in the morning between 08:30-11:30, when the sea is completely calm, flat as a mirror, and wind-free. If you want adrenaline or want to watch the surfers, your time is after 14:00, when the thermal breeze kicks in at full strength." }],
  },
  "Plaja Barbati Corfu": {
    scurt: "Barbati Beach is one of the most elegant, spectacular, and clean beaches in north-east Corfu, regularly awarded the European Blue Flag. Set at the foot of the imposing Mount Pantokrator, the beach is a long strip of snow-white pebbles, perfectly smoothed by waves. The contrast between the massive green mountain, the immaculate white beach, and the extremely transparent turquoise sea is simply stunning. It's an ideal spot for those who love deep, clean water and mountain-meets-sea scenery.",
    cumAjungi: "The beach lies about 20km north of Corfu Town. The main coastal road is fully paved but fairly narrow, full of tight mountain bends. Buses run fairly rarely on this route. A rental car is by far the best solution. From the main road, a sloped secondary road drops straight down to the sea. There are large dirt car parks behind the beach (some free, others private, belonging to the bars, for a small €3-5 fee).",
    echipament: [{ titlu: "Aqua shoes are essential", text: "The beach and the whole entry into the sea are made exclusively of white stones and pebbles; walking barefoot is very uncomfortable." }, { titlu: "Snorkel mask and tube", text: "As the water gets deep from the first steps and is incredibly transparent, the underwater rocky terrain attracts large schools of fish, making it a real snorkelling paradise." }, { titlu: "A thick towel or folding mat", text: "The white shore pebbles are beautiful, but a slightly thicker mat will give you more comfort if you're settling in the free areas." }],
    preturi: "Renting a set of two sunbeds with an umbrella costs around €15-20 a day. Along the kilometre-long beach there are several modern, charming bars and tavernas. A frappe costs €4, a cold beer is €4.50, and an excellent lunch based on fresh fish or seafood at the tavernas costs around €15-18 per person.",
    turisti: [{ titlu: "The water clarity is astounding", text: "Every visitor praises the sea's transparency, mentioning you can see the seabed even where the water goes past 10 metres deep." }, { titlu: "Stunning mountain scenery", text: "Tourists are fascinated by the sight of the tall Pantokrator mountain seeming to tumble straight into the Ionian Sea." }],
    tips: [{ titlu: "Best time to go", text: "Arrive around 09:15 in the morning. The bay is very quiet then, and the morning sun lights the white pebbles perfectly, creating phosphorescent colours in the water. Note that the water gets deep quickly (after just two steps from shore), so the beach is ideal for strong swimmers and less suited for babies left at the water's edge." }],
  },
  "Plaja Paleokastritsa și Grotele Palaiokastritsa": {
    scurt: "Paleokastritsa is considered the most spectacular and famous coastal region of Corfu. The central bay is a gem squeezed between huge rock walls, cloaked in dense pine and olive forests. The beach is a mix of fine sand and white pebbles, and the sea has an incredible bright emerald-green shade, so clear that boats seem to float in mid-air. It's a legendary spot of dramatic beauty.",
    cumAjungi: "Paleokastritsa lies on the west coast, about 25km from Corfu Town. The road is fully paved but full of steep slopes and tight bends. A rental car is essential, as the region consists of 6 different bays spread over several kilometres, and a car lets you move quickly between them. Parking in the central bay (near the harbour) is large, partly free and partly paid (around €5 a day), but gets extremely crowded after 10:00.",
    echipament: [{ titlu: "Snorkelling mask is essential", text: "The rocky terrain and underwater caves make this the island's best snorkelling spot." }, { titlu: "Aqua shoes", text: "Although the shore has plenty of sand, you'll encounter large stones and rocks in the water." }, { titlu: "A hoodie or large towel for later", text: "The water here is known to be the coldest on the island, due to deep underwater currents, making it extremely refreshing in August." }],
    preturi: "A set of two sunbeds with an umbrella costs around €15-20. A 30-minute local boat trip to visit the hidden sea caves (like Nausika or the Blue Eye) costs around €15 per person. A full lunch at the cliffside tavernas costs around €15-18 per person.",
    turisti: [{ titlu: "World-class scenery", text: "Every visitor praises the stunning views and recommends driving up to the 13th-century monastery on the hill too." }, { titlu: "The water really is cold", text: "Many reviews warn that the water is considerably colder than on the east coast." }],
    tips: [{ titlu: "Best time to go", text: "Arrive around 09:00 in the morning. You'll get parking right by the beach and be able to take a boat to the caves before the sun gets too strong and creates harsh reflections on the water." }],
  },
  "Plaja Kolymbia Archangelos": {
    scurt: "Kolymbia Beach is an elegant, extremely peaceful destination, set in a picturesque bay sheltered from the wind on the island's east coast. Made of a mix of fine sand and small white pebbles, the shore is bordered by charming resorts and spectacular green cliffs. The sea is calm, crystal clear, and takes on gorgeous azure shades, making it an ideal choice for tourists who want total comfort without the buzz of Faliraki.",
    cumAjungi: "Kolymbia sits halfway between Rhodes Town and Lindos (about 25km from each). The access road from the main highway is famous on the island: a 2km straight line lined with huge eucalyptus trees (Eucalyptus Boulevard). Buses only drop you on the main road, so a rental car is essential to reach the sea directly. Parking is free, spacious, and set on dirt right behind the beach.",
    echipament: [{ titlu: "Aqua shoes", text: "Although the shore has plenty of warm sand, there's a band of rounded pebbles at the entry into the calm sea." }, { titlu: "Snorkelling mask", text: "On the right side of the bay, where the massive rock meets the sea, fish are very active." }, { titlu: "A camera", text: "A short walk to the rock at the edge of the bay will give you a superb panoramic view of the whole coastline." }],
    preturi: "A set of two sunbeds with an umbrella costs around €12-15 a day. The traditional tavernas behind the beach offer fresh dishes, with a meal for two coming to €35-45. A frappe at the bar costs €3.50, and a large bottle of still water is around €1.50.",
    turisti: [{ titlu: "A relaxed, clean atmosphere", text: "Visitors praise the beach's generous size, which never feels stiflingly crowded, keeping a select feel." }, { titlu: "A fairly gentle entry", text: "Every family appreciates how calm and safe the sea is for swimming in this protected bay." }],
    tips: [{ titlu: "Best time to go", text: "Arrive around 09:30 in the morning. The bay has a special quiet in the early part of the day. For a completely free area for your towel, head to the far left end of the beach, where the atmosphere is much more secluded and wild." }],
  },
  "Plaja Ixia Rhodos Town": {
    scurt: "Ixia Beach sits on the north-west coast and is completely different from those on the east side. It's a long, modern beach, made mainly of large white pebbles and stones smoothed by waves. Facing directly onto the open sea and exposed to constant Meltemi winds, Ixia is a top meeting point for windsurfing and kitesurfing enthusiasts. The sea has a deep, dynamic blue and is extremely clean.",
    cumAjungi: "The beach is just 5km west of Rhodes Town, along the coastal road toward the airport. Access is fully paved, flat, and fast. A rental car gives you total independence, letting you carry beach gear comfortably and move quickly to the calmer eastern beaches if you want. Parking is simple and free: you can leave your vehicle right on the roadside or in the dedicated spaces of the large seafront hotels.",
    echipament: [{ titlu: "Aqua shoes are essential", text: "Both the beach and the whole entry into the sea are exclusively large stones; walking barefoot is very uncomfortable and painful." }, { titlu: "Budget for windsurfing lessons", text: "Ixia hosts some of the island's best windsurfing schools, making it the ideal place to learn the sport." }, { titlu: "Polarised sunglasses", text: "The white stones reflect sunlight strongly throughout the day." }],
    preturi: "Sets of two sunbeds with an umbrella cost around €10-15 a day. Along the seafront there are numerous hotel bars and restaurants. A frappe costs €4, a cocktail is around €10, and a quick gyros or club sandwich lunch runs €7-10.",
    turisti: [{ titlu: "Memorable sunsets", text: "Everyone mentions the sunset here, with the outline of the Turkish coast in the distance, is among the most beautiful in Rhodes." }, { titlu: "Not ideal for young kids", text: "Reviews warn that the constant waves and stones at the entry make this beach less suited for little ones." }],
    tips: [{ titlu: "Best time to go", text: "If you want to swim safely when the sea is calmer, come in the morning between 08:30-11:00. The bay is much quieter then. If you want adrenaline and want to try windsurfing, your time is after 14:00, when the wind picks up to full strength." }],
  },
  "Plaja Stegna Archangelos": {
    scurt: "Stegna is a charming, authentic beach, opposite the village of Archangelos, on the island's east coast. Unlike the large commercial resorts, Stegna has managed to keep the feel of a traditional Greek fishing village. The beach is long, made of a mix of fine sand and small pebbles, and the water is calm and crystal clear. It's the ideal spot for tourists who want to escape the bustle and experience a relaxing holiday where life moves at a slower pace.",
    cumAjungi: "The beach lies about 30km south of Rhodes Town. The main road is excellent, but the final descent from Archangelos into Stegna bay is a narrow road full of tight hairpins and steep slopes offering superb sea views. Local buses rarely reach here, making a rental car absolutely necessary. A big advantage is that you can park for free right along the road following the beach line or in the large spaces near the fishing harbour.",
    echipament: [{ titlu: "Aqua shoes", text: "Although the shore has plenty of warm sand, there's a band of pebbles and flat stones at the entry into the sea." }, { titlu: "Snorkelling mask", text: "On the right side of the bay, where the large rocks meet the sea, the underwater terrain is full of colourful fish." }, { titlu: "Polarised sunglasses", text: "Sunlight reflected off the clean water in this sheltered bay is very strong at midday." }],
    preturi: "Prices in Stegna are very reasonable. A set of two sunbeds with an umbrella costs around €10-12 a day. The village is known for its fishing tavernas. A frappe costs €3.50, and a delicious lunch based on fish caught that same morning or seafood comes to around €12-15 per person.",
    turisti: [{ titlu: "An authentic Greek vibe", text: "Every review praises the peace of the place and the lack of huge resort hotels, appreciating the family-run restaurants." }, { titlu: "Very clean sea", text: "Tourists note the water's transparency is impeccable, ideal for long swims." }],
    tips: [{ titlu: "Best time to go", text: "Stay for dinner. The tavernas set right along the road, steps from the sea, offer an incredibly romantic and relaxing atmosphere as evening falls, when the fishing harbour goes completely quiet." }],
  },
  "Plaja Elli Rhodos Town": {
    scurt: "Elli Beach is the main urban beach of the capital, Rhodes Town, and is considered by many historians one of the most elegant, cosmopolitan city beaches in the whole Mediterranean. Stretching right at the island's northern tip, the beach is made of a fine mix of sand and small white pebbles. The sea is remarkably clean, a deep, refreshing blue. Its landmark feature is the historic concrete diving platform (The Trampoline), built out in the sea during the Italian period, from which tourists jump straight into the waves.",
    cumAjungi: "The beach is within walking distance of the historic centre and the old town of Rhodes. If you're staying in the capital, you'll get there instantly on foot. If you're coming from other resorts on the island (Faliraki, Ialyssos, or Lindos), a rental car will give you full comfort on the fast paved road. Finding free parking near Elli Beach can be nearly impossible at midday. Our tip is to leave the car in the large public car parks near Mandraki harbour (just a 5-minute walk) and cross the esplanade to the sea.",
    echipament: [{ titlu: "Aqua shoes (optional)", text: "Depending on the section you settle in, the pebbles at the water's entry can be slightly uncomfortable underfoot." }, { titlu: "Swimming goggles or a mask", text: "Swimming out to the famous concrete diving platform is the beach's main activity — worth a look underwater too." }, { titlu: "A stylish city sun hat", text: "With the seafront full of modern bars, casinos, and historic buildings, a long walk calls for a relaxed holiday outfit." }],
    preturi: "As a very popular city beach, prices are mid-to-high range. A set of two sunbeds with an umbrella costs around €15-20 a day. Along the beach there are numerous top beach bars and restaurants (like Ronda). A frappe costs €4, a cocktail is around €10, and a full lunch starts from €15-20 per person.",
    turisti: [{ titlu: "Everything close at hand", text: "Tourists greatly appreciate the proximity to restaurants, hotels, shops, and the historic sights of the old town." }, { titlu: "Jumping off the platform", text: "Everyone mentions the concrete platform as a must-do fun experience when visiting Elli Beach." }],
    tips: [{ titlu: "Best time to go", text: "This beach is gorgeous in the second half of the day. Since it sits right at the island's tip, the sea breeze is constant and pleasant, and you can enjoy the sun late into the day here. After the beach, take a walk through the historic Mandraki harbour, said to be where the famous Colossus of Rhodes once stood." }],
  },
  "Plaja Plakias Rethymno": {
    scurt: "Plakias Beach is a huge, imposing stretch of fine sand mixed with small pebbles, set in a wide bay on Crete's south coast. Known as one of the longest beaches in the south, Plakias gives you sweeping views of the Libyan Sea and the rocky mountains around it. The water is crystal clear, refreshing, and a deep blue. It's an extremely airy, well-organised beach, ideal for combining wild southern scenery with full facilities.",
    cumAjungi: "Plakias is about 35km south of Rethymno. The drive is spectacular, passing right through the impressive Kourtaliotiko Gorge (where the rocks seem to tumble over the road). The road is fully paved and safe, but buses run on a rigid schedule. A car is very comfortable for exploring the bay and for parking for free right by the beach or in the large spaces behind the resort's tavernas.",
    echipament: [{ titlu: "Good sunglasses and protection", text: "Since the bay is very open, the sun hits straight on in the second half of the day." }, { titlu: "No special footwear needed in the sandy areas", text: "The main beach is predominantly sandy, though bands of fine pebbles can appear at the water's entry." }, { titlu: "Beach paddles or a ball", text: "The generous space lets you play on the sand without bothering neighbouring sunbeds." }],
    preturi: "A set of two sunbeds with an umbrella costs around €10-12 a day. The seafront behind the beach is full of excellent cafés and tavernas. A frappe costs €3.50, a quick gyros is €4, and a full dinner based on fresh fish or traditional dishes costs around €12-15 per person.",
    turisti: [{ titlu: "Perfect for a relaxed family day", text: "Visitors appreciate the beach's cleanliness, and the presence of showers, changing rooms, and lifeguards." }, { titlu: "The wind can be strong", text: "Many reviews mention that, being open to the south, the north wind (Meltemi) sometimes comes strongly down the gorge toward the sea, kicking up sand." }],
    tips: [{ titlu: "Best time to go", text: "Head to the far left end of the beach, toward the area called Paligremnos. There's a huge vertical rock face, over 80 metres tall, dropping straight into the sea. It's an extremely spectacular spot for photos, and the cliff offers huge natural shade in the second half of the afternoon." }],
  },
  "Plaja Preveli Rethymno": {
    scurt: "Preveli is one of the most famous, wild, and stunning beaches in all of Crete. Set on the south coast, it's the magical spot where a mountain river (flowing through the imposing Kourtaliotiko Gorge) empties directly into the Libyan Sea. Its unique feature is the second-largest natural palm forest (Theophrastus) in Crete, growing along the river's banks and creating an exotic, tropical-oasis scenery. The beach is made of dark coarse sand and fine white pebbles.",
    cumAjungi: "The beach sits isolated in the south of the Rethymno region. Public transport is rare and rigid, making a rental car absolutely essential for a safe trip. You'll drive on the paved road through the gorge to the large car park set on the rock, for a small fee (around €2-3). From the car park, the adventure begins on foot: a long stone path down with over 150 steep steps (about 15-20 minutes), giving a dreamlike view of the palm oasis below.",
    echipament: [{ titlu: "Comfortable trainers", text: "The stepped path from the car park down requires care, being tiring and definitely not recommended in basic flip-flops." }, { titlu: "Your own beach umbrella and backpack", text: "Preveli is a 100% public, protected beach. There are no sunbeds or big bars set up on the sand. The palm forest offers natural shade only along the freshwater river." }, { titlu: "Aqua shoes", text: "Recommended for stepping comfortably over the pebbles at the entry into the deep sea." }],
    preturi: "Access to the nature reserve is free. At the edge of the palm forest, a small wooden canteen/kiosk operates in season, where you can buy cold water or a frappe for €3.50-4. There are no other commercial costs down there. A full lunch at the tavernas on the way back will cost you around €12-15 per person.",
    turisti: [{ titlu: "An unmatched experience", text: "Every visitor is overwhelmed by the beauty of the walk through the palm forest along the freshwater river, and the chance to alternate between swimming in the cold river water and the warm sea." }, { titlu: "The final climb is a real test", text: "Reviews warn that climbing the 150 steps back to the car at midday is quite demanding." }],
    tips: [{ titlu: "Best time to go", text: "Arrive at the car park around 09:00 in the morning. You'll go down the path in cool conditions (the rock blocks the sun in the early morning) and be able to walk through the exotic palm forest in total peace, before the small excursion boats from Plakias bring large tourist groups after 11:00." }],
  },
  "Plaja Kommos Heraklion": {
    scurt: "Kommos Beach is a huge, imposing stretch of fine, dark sand, running for kilometres along the Libyan Sea. Right next to the famous resort of Matala, Kommos offers a completely different setting: a wild, quiet, history-rich place. Right at the edge of the sand dunes lies the archaeological site of an ancient Minoan port. It's an airy beach, known as a protected area where Caretta-Caretta sea turtles lay their eggs, and for the mysterious offshore rock, Volakas.",
    cumAjungi: "The beach is in the south of the Heraklion region, just a few kilometres from Pitsidia and Matala. Local buses only drop you in the surrounding villages, from where the walk through the sun is long and tiring. A rental car is essential to reach the beach directly. The secondary road is mostly paved and ends in a wide dirt area where you can park completely free, right behind the beach and the Minoan ruins.",
    echipament: [{ titlu: "Aqua shoes", text: "Although the shore is just fine sand, at the entry into the sea there's a large, flat, fairly slippery natural rock slab worth stepping over carefully." }, { titlu: "Your own beach umbrella", text: "The area is considered a nature reserve, so the organised sunbed section is limited to a small central portion only." }, { titlu: "Good quality sunglasses", text: "Since the beach is long and fully open, midday sunlight is very strong." }],
    preturi: "In the small organised area, a set of two sunbeds with an umbrella costs around €10-12. There's a single excellent taverna set above the beach, on the rocks. A frappe costs €3.50, a cold beer is €4, and a portion of homemade traditional Cretan food is around €10-13.",
    turisti: [{ titlu: "Endless space and dreamy sunsets", text: "Every review praises the fact that the beach is never crowded, and the sunset seen from here is considered among the most spectacular in southern Crete." }, { titlu: "Note the naturist area", text: "Tourists mention that the northern section of the beach (the wildest part) is traditionally used for naturism." }],
    tips: [{ titlu: "Best time to go", text: "Come in the second half of the afternoon, around 16:30. Enjoy a long swim in the clean sea, and toward evening book a table at the taverna on the hill to dine while watching the sun set straight into the sea, behind the Paximadia islands visible on the horizon." }],
  },
  "Insula Chrissi Lasithi": {
    scurt: "Chrissi Island (officially also known as Gaidouronisi) is a unique nature reserve in the Libyan Sea, famous for its exotic scenery reminiscent of the Caribbean. The island is completely uninhabited and hosts Europe's largest natural Lebanon cedar forest. The main coastal beach (the famous Golden Beach) is a spectacular stretch of fine white sand mixed with millions of tiny pink shells, and the sea has an unreal light-turquoise colour and is extremely warm.",
    cumAjungi: "Chrissi lies about 15km south of Crete's coast. To get there, you need a car to drive to the port town of Ierapetra (Europe's southernmost town), on a fully paved, fast road. From Ierapetra's harbour, large cruise boats or private speedboats connect to the island. You can leave your car completely free in the large public car parks near Ierapetra's harbour.",
    echipament: [{ titlu: "Your own beach umbrella and mat are essential", text: "To protect the island's fragile ecosystem, Greek authorities have banned heavy beach infrastructure and removed all beach bars or sunbeds. You need to bring your own shade from the mainland." }, { titlu: "Comfortable walking shoes (sandals or light trainers)", text: "The cedar forest is protected by fences, and getting from the boat drop-off point to the golden beach is along marked paths through hot sand." }, { titlu: "Snorkelling mask", text: "As the water is extremely clear and shallow at the shore, underwater visibility over the white sandy bed is exceptional." }],
    preturi: "A return ferry ticket from Ierapetra to Chrissi Island costs €25-35 per person, depending on the company. There's also a small municipal environmental fee (around €1), usually included in the ticket. Since there are no shops on the island, it's vital to buy food and water in Ierapetra's harbour, where a frappe costs €3.50 and a sandwich is €5.",
    turisti: [{ titlu: "A tropical paradise in Europe", text: "Every visitor is impressed by the electric turquoise colour of the water and the fine sand with its pink shimmer." }, { titlu: "Check the current rules", text: "Many recent reviews mention that, to protect the cedar forest, boats sometimes only stop in the bay a few metres from shore for swimming straight from the boat, without landing on the beach. Check at the harbour before buying your ticket." }],
    tips: [{ titlu: "Best time to go", text: "Choose a small private speedboat departing at 08:30 from Ierapetra. You'll reach the golden bay before the big cruise boats, with the chance to swim in warm, crystal-clear water in complete peace." }],
  },
  "Plaja Kavouri Riviera Ateniană": {
    scurt: "Kavouri Beach (locally split into Megalo and Mikro Kavouri) is one of the most beautiful, green, and beloved public beaches on the Athens Riviera. Set in a wide, pine-filled bay in the residential Vouliagmeni area, the beach stands out for its wide strip of warm golden sand and extremely shallow, warm water at the shore. It's an airy beach, naturally blending green grassy areas and elegant bars with huge open spaces, making it the ideal destination around Athens for families with kids and long walks along the water's edge.",
    cumAjungi: "Kavouri is about 20km south of central Athens. Public transport has infrequent lines and stops fairly far from the sea, making the trip tiring in the sun. A rental car gives you total comfort on the fast, fully paved road. A big advantage at Kavouri is parking: there are large free public spots along the local road following the beach line, right under the pines, offering easy car access just a minute's walk from the sunbeds.",
    echipament: [{ titlu: "Plenty of sand toys for little ones", text: "The seabed is an unbroken stretch of soft sand, and the water stays shallow for a huge distance offshore, making this a genuinely safe paradise for children." }, { titlu: "No water shoes needed", text: "The risk of stepping on stones or sea urchins inside this sandy bay is zero." }, { titlu: "Beach paddles (beach tennis)", text: "The sand is fine and compact at the water's edge, and the beach is famous among Athenians for dynamic games on shore." }],
    preturi: "Access to the free areas of the beach is completely free. In the sections organised by modern beach bars, renting a set of two sunbeds with an umbrella costs around €15-20 a day. A frappe costs €4, a cold beer is €4.50, and a full meal at the renowned seafront tavernas costs around €15-18 per person.",
    turisti: [{ titlu: "The park behind the beach is a blessing", text: "Tourists greatly appreciate the shaded green areas bordering the sand, offering a perfect shaded walk at midday." }, { titlu: "Excellent for kids", text: "Every family praises the extremely gentle entry into the water and the complete absence of big waves in this protected bay." }],
    tips: [{ titlu: "Best time to go", text: "Stay on the beach or at a seafront terrace until sunset. Kavouri faces perfectly west and delivers an amazing show as the sun sinks straight into the Saronic Gulf. A short walk along the coastal footpath will take you to small rocky peninsulas where the ruins of ancient Greek fortifications lie." }],
  },
  "Plaja Lagonisi Riviera Ateniană": {
    scurt: "Lagonisi Beach (often known as Grand Beach Lagonisi) is the definition of luxury, elegance, and premium comfort on the Athens Riviera. Set inside an exclusive private complex on a gorgeous peninsula, the beach offers a wide strip of fine, light-coloured sand and rarely transparent water, in brilliant turquoise shades. The complex offers top-tier facilities: a spectacular pool built right into the sea, elegant wooden jetties, modern bars, and fine restaurants.",
    cumAjungi: "Lagonisi is about 40km south of Athens. The considerable distance from the city makes public transport completely impractical for a relaxed day trip. A rental car ensures a fast, fully comfortable journey on the fully paved coastal road. The complex has a huge, well-organised, secure private indoor car park, with very easy car access right at the beach entrance.",
    echipament: [{ titlu: "Elegant resort wear", text: "As a very select premium location, light but chic summer clothes are ideal for lunch breaks at the jetty bars." }, { titlu: "No water shoes needed", text: "The seabed inside this private bay is entirely covered with fine, soft, extremely clean sand, free of stones." }, { titlu: "Good polarised sunglasses", text: "The light-coloured sand reflects sunlight strongly at midday." }],
    preturi: "As a luxury location, prices run well above the Greek average. Entry to the organised beach is ticketed (around €30-50 per person depending on season and day, including access to facilities, a premium sunbed, and umbrella). A frappe costs €5-6, a cocktail is around €14-16, and lunch starts from €25 per person.",
    turisti: [{ titlu: "Impeccable service and cleanliness", text: "Every review praises the flawless quality of service, mentioning the sand is raked daily and the water is as warm as a pool." }, { titlu: "The sea pool is a dream", text: "Visitors are fascinated by the long wooden walkway leading to the pool built right above the seawater." }],
    tips: [{ titlu: "Best time to go", text: "Arrive around 09:00 in the morning to grab the best spots on the wooden jetties or the front row of sunbeds on the sand, enjoying an incredibly quiet atmosphere in the early part of the day." }],
  },
  "Plaja Porto Vathy Thassos": {
    scurt: "Just a few hundred metres past Marble Beach, Porto Vathy is its smaller but equally spectacular sister. It shares the same magic secret: fine white marble pebbles and an unreal turquoise sea. The big advantage of Porto Vathy is that the landscape is a bit more open, framed by a massive marble quarry right in the background, giving it an industrial edge softened by nature.",
    cumAjungi: "The access road is the direct continuation of the unpaved forest track leading to Marble Beach. Conditions are identical: white dust, gravel and bumps. It's not a route you want to walk or ride a small scooter on. A car gives you the safety you need and saves you the effort. Parking is free, set up behind the beach right next to the old olive trees.",
    echipament: [{ titlu: "Snorkelling mask", text: "Head towards the rocky side of the bay; the water's clarity lets you see whole schools of fish foraging among the rocks." }, { titlu: "Wet wipes in the car", text: "Extremely handy on the way out, to quickly clean off the white marble dust before you get behind the wheel." }, { titlu: "High-SPF sunscreen (SPF 50)", text: "Light reflecting off the white pebbles speeds up your tan, but it also raises the risk of fast sunburn." }],
    preturi: "The beach has a modern, chill-out beach bar. A set of sunbeds costs around €20-25, and sometimes that amount can be turned into bar credit for drinks or snacks. A simple burger or club sandwich costs around €8-10.",
    turisti: [{ titlu: "A great alternative to Marble Beach", text: "Many visitors who find Marble Beach too crowded head a few minutes further on to Porto Vathy, where the atmosphere is often a touch more relaxed." }, { titlu: "Spectacular scenery", text: "The marble quarry behind the beach creates a unique visual contrast that photography lovers really appreciate." }],
    tips: [{ titlu: "Best time to go", text: "If you want a truly relaxed atmosphere, come after 4:30 PM. The sun starts to dip, the water takes on warmer colours, and most tourists are already heading back to their hotels." }],
  },
  "Giola Thassos": {
    scurt: "Giola isn't a beach in the classic sense — it's a spectacular natural lagoon or pool, carved by waves directly into the coastal rock. Enclosed by stone walls up to 8 metres high, Giola is constantly refilled with fresh seawater through waves breaking over its edge. The water in the pool is often warmer than the open sea and has a gorgeous jade-green tint. It's the perfect spot for the brave, keen to jump in from height.",
    cumAjungi: "Giola lies in the south of the island, near the village of Astris. Public transport won't drop you anywhere near this spot. A car is essential. From the main paved road, a fairly steep, rough dirt track branches off, full of large stones. There's a paid parking area (around €3-4) next to a local tavern, and from there you still have a 10-15 minute walk down over the rocks to reach the pool.",
    echipament: [{ titlu: "Grippy shoes or trainers", text: "The climb down and walking on the rocks around Giola can be very slippery and dangerous in plain beach flip-flops." }, { titlu: "A light backpack with water", text: "Down at the pool there is absolutely no infrastructure, shop or natural shade. It's just bare rock exposed to the sun." }, { titlu: "Aqua shoes for swimming", text: "The inner edges of the pool are full of sea urchins, so if you'd rather not jump and prefer to ease into the water slowly, special footwear will protect you." }],
    preturi: "Access to the natural pool is completely free. The only cost is the parking up top (if you choose not to leave the car further down, on the edge of the rough road). At the tavern where the footpath starts, a cold drink or snack costs around €3-5.",
    turisti: [{ titlu: "Watch out when jumping", text: "Many tourists recommend checking the water depth and watching out for other people before jumping from the highest rocks." }, { titlu: "The walk back is tiring", text: "Climbing back up to the parking area around midday can be very demanding because of the heat." }],
    tips: [{ titlu: "Best time to go", text: "Go to Giola in the morning, around 8:00-8:30 AM. You'll find the pool completely empty, the water perfectly clean (no sunscreen film on the surface), and you'll be able to get those magazine-worthy shots without dozens of people in the background." }],
  },
  "Plaja Psili Ammos Thassos": {
    scurt: "Psili Ammos literally means \"Fine Sand\", and the beach lives up to its name to the letter. Located in the south of the island, it's a vibrant beach with a young, cosmopolitan feel. The bay is flanked by hills covered in pines and olive trees, and the sea has a rare clarity. It's the favourite spot for those who want to combine a great beach day with good music mixed by DJs at the modern beach bars along the shore.",
    cumAjungi: "The beach is about 5 km from the resort of Potos. Buses do stop on the main road above the beach, but relying on them in the height of summer heat isn't pleasant. By car you get there in under 10 minutes from Potos or Limenaria. Free parking sits right behind the beach, shaded by olive trees, but space runs out after about 10:30 AM.",
    echipament: [{ titlu: "Snorkelling mask", text: "At both ends of the bay there are spectacular underwater rock formations, full of fish and hidden octopuses." }, { titlu: "Noise-cancelling headphones for kids", text: "If you're bringing babies, sit further from the bars' big speakers, as the music can get fairly loud after lunch." }, { titlu: "An after-sun lotion", text: "The sand here tends to hold heat strongly, so your skin will need extra hydration in the evening." }],
    preturi: "Sunbeds are usually tied to a minimum spend at the beach bars, ranging between €15-25 per person, depending on how close to the water you want to sit. A cocktail costs around €8-10, and a portion of fries or a club sandwich is around €6-8.",
    turisti: [{ titlu: "The water is colder here", text: "Many visitors note the water in this bay tends to be 1-2 degrees cooler than in the north of the island, due to cold currents, but it's incredibly refreshing in July and August." }, { titlu: "Great atmosphere in the evening", text: "Sunset parties are highly praised by younger crowds." }],
    tips: [{ titlu: "Best time to go", text: "Come around 9:15 AM. You'll find parking in deep shade under the olive trees and be able to pick the best front-row sunbeds, right at the water's edge." }],
  },
  "Plaja Potos Thassos": {
    scurt: "Potos beach is the town beach of one of Thassos's liveliest resorts. If you like being right in the middle of the action, where the beach blends naturally into taverns, cafes and souvenir shops, this is the place. The beach has a mix of sand and fine pebbles, and the water is calm and clean. It's the kind of laid-back beach where you can go straight from a swim to a table with fresh fish.",
    cumAjungi: "Potos is an important road hub in the south of the island. If you're staying right in the resort, you can walk there in a few minutes. If you're coming from other areas (like Limenaria or Thassos Town), a car is the best option. Parking inside the Potos resort can be a real challenge in season; there are paid private car parks (around €4-5 per day) very close to the seafront that save you from circling the narrow streets.",
    echipament: [{ titlu: "Aqua shoes", text: "Even though there's plenty of sand, there are stretches with pebbles at the water's entry and occasionally a few hidden sea urchins near the rocks." }, { titlu: "Cash in your pocket", text: "Some of the smaller taverns or the beach doughnut vendors prefer cash payment." }, { titlu: "Volleyball", text: "Volleyball nets are often set up on the beach by the local bars." }],
    preturi: "The rental system is very friendly: most taverns give you sunbeds for free if you order drinks or food from them (a minimum spend of €10-15 per set). A frappe costs €3.50, and a full lunch for a family costs around €35-45.",
    turisti: [{ titlu: "Close to everything you need", text: "Tourists really appreciate having toilets, showers, pharmacies and shops just steps from the beach." }, { titlu: "Crowded seafront", text: "In the evening, the area behind the beach turns pedestrian and gets very busy." }],
    tips: [{ titlu: "Best time to go", text: "Stay on the beach until sunset. The island's south-west coast puts on a superb show as the sun dips into the sea, and the taverns light up their romantic lamps right on the sand." }],
  },
  "Plaja Skala Rachoni Thassos": {
    scurt: "If Paradise or Psili Ammos are vibrant, lively beaches, Skala Rachoni is the exact opposite: an oasis of quiet, peace and total relaxation. Located in the north-west of the island, the beach is famous for its huge pine trees that grow right out of the sand and stretch their branches over the water, offering brilliant natural shade. The water is shallow, clean, and so warm and calm it feels like a huge lake.",
    cumAjungi: "The beach is about 10 km from Thassos Town (Limenas). The road is perfectly paved, flat and very easy to drive. By car you get there quickly and can park for free right in the shade of the trees behind the beach, without the stress you'd find in the bigger resorts. It's a great choice for those wanting a day of total unplugging in nature.",
    echipament: [{ titlu: "A good book", text: "The atmosphere is so quiet (no thumping music from speakers) that it's the perfect place to read in the shade of the pines." }, { titlu: "Inflatable mattress", text: "With water as flat as a mirror, you can drift for hours without worrying about big waves." }, { titlu: "Insect repellent spray", text: "Because of the lush vegetation and the pine trees on the beach, a few small insects can appear in the late afternoon." }],
    preturi: "A set of sunbeds costs around €8-12, or is likewise offered against a reduced minimum spend at the nearby taverns. Food prices are somewhat lower than in the southern resorts: a portion of tzatziki costs €4, and a portion of grilled local fish is around €10-12.",
    turisti: [{ titlu: "The natural shade is perfect", text: "Many tourists praise not needing an umbrella at all thanks to the old pines that keep it cool all day." }, { titlu: "Ideal for seniors and children", text: "The quiet and the shallow water are strong points frequently mentioned in reviews." }],
    tips: [{ titlu: "Best time to go", text: "This beach is gorgeous in the second half of the day. Facing west, you can enjoy sun until late and a clean, peaceful, very romantic sunset." }],
  },
  "Plaja Metalia Thassos": {
    scurt: "Metalia is one of the most unusual and mysterious beaches on Thassos, with a strong industrial and historical character. Located near Limenaria, the beach sits on the site of a former German ore-processing plant (hence the name Metalia). The landscape is marked by the ruins of old stone furnaces, abandoned mine shafts, and — most interesting of all — a huge labyrinth built from stones on the plateau above the beach, along with zodiac signs carved into marble.",
    cumAjungi: "The beach is right on the edge of the Limenaria resort. You can walk there from the harbour over the hill, but the route is tiring and steep. By car, access is via a side road that descends from the main road. The road is unpaved, fairly steep and gravelly, so it needs to be driven slowly. Parking at the bottom is free, spacious, and set up right next to the historic ruins.",
    echipament: [{ titlu: "Aqua shoes are a must", text: "The seabed is entirely covered by a large slab of natural rock, slippery and uneven, where many sea urchins have settled. Without special footwear, getting into the water is quite risky." }, { titlu: "Snorkelling mask", text: "The rocky, industrial underwater area has attracted plenty of fish species and marine plants; it's a fascinating place to explore." }, { titlu: "Camera/charged phone", text: "The ruins and the stone labyrinth up top are perfect for an offbeat, atmospheric photo session." }],
    preturi: "There's a single beach bar open on the beach during summer. A set of sunbeds costs around €10-15. A beer or juice at the bar costs €4, and quick snacks are around €6-8.",
    turisti: [{ titlu: "An open-air museum", text: "All visitors are fascinated by the site's history and recommend making sure to climb up to the plateau above the beach to see the marble zodiac signs." }, { titlu: "Getting into the water is tricky", text: "Reviews constantly warn about the rock slab at the sea entry." }],
    tips: [{ titlu: "Best time to go", text: "Set aside an hour of your day (ideally before sunset, when it's not so hot) to explore the old tunnels and abandoned factory buildings. The light coming through the stone windows creates an incredible atmosphere." }],
  },
  "Plaja Astris Thassos": {
    scurt: "Astris (or Astrida Beach) is a picturesque beach on an open bay in the south of the island, known for its deep blue waters and quiet atmosphere, away from mass tourism. The beach is made up of a mix of coarse sand and fine pebbles. Its name means \"Island of the Stars\", and locals say that on clear summer nights the sky is absolutely spectacular from here.",
    cumAjungi: "The beach is right in the far south, about 7 km past the resort of Potos, just before reaching the Giola natural pool. Public transport is almost non-existent in this isolated stretch of coast. A rental car is essential to get here comfortably. Access from the main ring road is very easy, paved, and the car can be left in an improvised dirt parking area right behind the beach, completely free.",
    echipament: [{ titlu: "Aqua shoes", text: "Although there's plenty of sand on the shore, the sea entry has stretches with fairly slippery stones and a few steep drops." }, { titlu: "Your own beach umbrella", text: "The area set up with sunbeds is quite small. If you prefer privacy, the wild edge of the beach is perfect, but fully exposed to the sun." }, { titlu: "Fishing or snorkelling gear", text: "With the bay being open and rocky at the edges, it attracts a wide variety of fish." }],
    preturi: "If you grab a spot in the organised area, a set of two sunbeds with an umbrella costs around €10, or is offered against a minimum spend at the tavern across the road. A simple meal for two at the local tavern (famous for its fresh fish) will cost around €30-35.",
    turisti: [{ titlu: "Watch out for currents", text: "Many tourists mention that, since the bay is open, the sea deepens fairly quickly and strong waves can appear on windy days." }, { titlu: "Total peace and quiet", text: "Highly praised by those wanting to escape the loud music of Potos or Limenaria." }],
    tips: [{ titlu: "Best time to go", text: "This beach makes a great strategic stop for lunch or relaxation after visiting the Giola natural pool early in the morning. The tavern here serves one of the best traditional kitchens in the south." }],
  },
  "Plaja Pefkari Thassos": {
    scurt: "Pefkari is one of the top beaches in southern Thassos, repeatedly awarded the Blue Flag certificate for its exemplary water cleanliness. Its name comes from \"pefko\" (pine tree in Greek), since the whole beach is fringed by a stunning pine forest that comes down almost to the water's edge, scenting the air with a unique aroma of resin and salty breeze. The beach is made of coarse sand mixed with shiny white pebbles.",
    cumAjungi: "Pefkari sits in a cosy little bay right between the resorts of Limenaria and Potos. The short distance (under 2 km either way) makes it easy to reach if you have a car. The road drops you right behind the beach. Although parking on the narrow streets near the hotels can get busy in July and August, there are free spots set up along the access road. A car lets you move here quickly if the town beach in Potos feels too crowded.",
    echipament: [{ titlu: "Aqua shoes", text: "Entry into the water goes over a smooth but fairly slippery rock slab in places, where small families of sea urchins have settled." }, { titlu: "Budget for water sports", text: "Pefkari is famous on the island for having the best water sports centre (parasailing, jet-ski, water skiing or pedal boats)." }, { titlu: "Snorkelling mask", text: "The water is so clear that underwater visibility often exceeds 15 metres." }],
    preturi: "Sunbed sets belong to the bars and hotels along the shore and cost around €12-15 a day, or are included if you order drinks worth a similar amount. A frappe costs €4, and a cold beer is around €4.50.",
    turisti: [{ titlu: "Flawless infrastructure", text: "Tourists appreciate that the beach is very clean, has showers, changing cabins, and plenty of excellent taverns in the shade of the pines." }, { titlu: "Not ideal for very young children", text: "Since the water gets deep fairly quickly, parents need to keep an eye on little ones." }],
    tips: [{ titlu: "Best time to go", text: "Skala Pefkari is well known for its diving centre. If you want to try your first diving lesson in Greece, morning is the best time, when the sea is calm as a mirror." }],
  },
  "Plaja Kinira Thassos": {
    scurt: "Kinira beach is the definition of wilderness and intimacy on the east coast of Thassos. Facing the small fishing village of the same name, the beach stretches along a quiet bay, with the private rocky island of Kinirioti straight ahead. It's a long, narrow beach, made up mostly of fine gravel and sand, completely untouched by bar noise or commercial music.",
    cumAjungi: "Kinira is about 24 km from the capital Limenas and just 4 km north of the famous Paradise Beach. The local bus drops you on the main road, but the way down to the beach is along narrow dirt-and-gravel lanes. A rental car is by far the best option, letting you carry umbrellas and towels right down to the water's edge. Parking is completely free anywhere you find a spot along the roadside near the beach.",
    echipament: [{ titlu: "Beach umbrella and a thick mat", text: "The beach is mostly unorganised and there are no pines near the water for shade, and the pebbles call for a slightly thicker mat for comfort." }, { titlu: "Portable cool box", text: "There are no beach bars on the sand, so it's vital to bring cold water, fruit and snacks bought from the village." }, { titlu: "Aqua shoes", text: "The entry into the Aegean is rocky in the first few metres from shore." }],
    preturi: "Being a free beach, the cost is zero. If you want to eat, you'll need to go up to the traditional taverns in Kinira village (set above the main road). Prices are very affordable, lower than the rest of the island: a huge portion of souvlaki or a fresh Greek salad costs around €7-9.",
    turisti: [{ titlu: "A beach just for you", text: "Many tourists praise the fact that, even in August, you can be dozens of metres from the next person." }, { titlu: "Wonderful view", text: "The private island offshore offers a stunning wild backdrop for seascape lovers." }],
    tips: [{ titlu: "Best time to go", text: "Come here at sunrise or early morning. The east coast offers a spectacular view as the sun rises right from behind the rocky island offshore, creating a totally peaceful atmosphere." }],
  },
  "Plaja Skala Prinou Thassos": {
    scurt: "Skala Prinou is the island's second gateway (this is where ferries from Kavala dock) and is home to a very long, flat and quiet beach on its north-west side. The beach is entirely covered in fine, light-coloured sand, and the water is incredibly calm, shallow and clean. It's a well-known spot for its spectacular sunsets and its very relaxed, traditional holiday vibe.",
    cumAjungi: "The location sits on the west coast. If you arrive by ferry from Kavala, you land right by the beach. If you're staying elsewhere on the island, a car offers huge comfort, since the main western road is very straight, flat and quick to drive. Plus, from Skala Prinou you can drive up in just 10 minutes to the mountain village of Kazaviti, the oldest and most spectacular stone village on the island. Parking by the beach is public, huge and free.",
    echipament: [{ titlu: "Comfy footwear for long walks", text: "As the beach stretches for kilometres and is very fine, it's ideal for walking along the water's edge." }, { titlu: "No aqua shoes needed", text: "The seabed is entirely fine, clean sand with no stones, perfect for sensitive feet." }, { titlu: "Water-resistant sunscreen", text: "The sun hits directly from the front in the second half of the day, so protection matters a lot." }],
    preturi: "Sunbed sets are quite cheap or included with just an €8-10 total minimum spend at the taverns behind the beach. An excellent lunch of traditional Greek dishes costs around €12 per person.",
    turisti: [{ titlu: "Perfect for children", text: "The gentle entry into the water and the total lack of big waves make it a favourite destination for families." }, { titlu: "Memorable sunsets", text: "Everyone mentions that the sunset here, with the mainland's outline in the distance, is the most beautiful on Thassos." }],
    tips: [{ titlu: "Best time to go", text: "Plan your day so you sunbathe here in the afternoon, then in the evening make sure to drive up to the village of Megalos Prinos (Kazaviti) for dinner at a traditional tavern tucked into the mountain, shaded by centuries-old trees." }],
  },
  "Plaja Limenaria Thassos": {
    scurt: "Limenaria beach is the main town beach of the island's second-largest town. Stretched along a charming promenade, the beach offers a mix of fine sand and pebbles in certain spots. What makes it so loved is its accessibility: you're just a minute from hotels, patisseries, shops and the tourist harbour, while still having clean water and a wide view over the Aegean.",
    cumAjungi: "Limenaria sits in the south-west of Thassos island. The town is easy to reach on the main ring road, but finding a free parking spot on the narrow central streets behind the beach can become an extreme sport in the afternoon. It's best to use the large free public car park near the harbour (at the left end of the beach) and walk a minute along the promenade. A car gives you the freedom to hang out on this beach and quickly nip off shopping elsewhere on the island.",
    echipament: [{ titlu: "Aqua shoes (optional)", text: "Depending on which part of the beach you settle on, sea entry can have rock slabs or larger stones." }, { titlu: "Swimming goggles", text: "The water near the harbour is clean, and around the pier you can spot plenty of small fish." }, { titlu: "A chic town hat", text: "With the promenade full of modern cafes, a stroll between swims calls for casual holiday style." }],
    preturi: "Almost all sunbeds are offered for free if you order a coffee, frappe or snack from the seafront bars (an average spend of €10-15 for the whole set). A seafood lunch at the well-known promenade taverns costs around €15-18 per person.",
    turisti: [{ titlu: "Very convenient", text: "Tourists praise the closeness of all town facilities (ATMs, shops, pharmacies)." }, { titlu: "Varies from spot to spot", text: "Reviews mention that some stretches have perfect sand, while others need a bit of care entering the water because of stones." }],
    tips: [{ titlu: "Best time to go", text: "If you head to the right end of the beach (towards the town exit), it becomes much wider, sandier and much less crowded, ideal if you want to escape the bustle of the commercial promenade centre." }],
  },
  "Plaja Makriammos Thassos": {
    scurt: "Makriammos is a stunning private beach set in an isolated, enclosed bay, completely surrounded by a forest of vivid green pines. The sand is fine and light-coloured, and the water has exceptional clarity with a brilliant emerald tint. The beach is run by a well-known hotel complex and is considered one of the best-kept and safest beaches in the north of the island, even with a small deer reserve right behind it.",
    cumAjungi: "The beach is just 2 km east of the island's capital, Limenas. Despite the short distance, the access road climbs and drops steeply through the forest, making it tiring to walk in the summer heat. By car you get there in just 5 minutes. Entry to the beach is via the complex's reception, where there's a huge, well-shaded car park, completely free for visitors.",
    echipament: [{ titlu: "Camera or charged phone", text: "In the park area behind the beach, deer and peacocks roam freely and are very used to people, making for great photo opportunities." }, { titlu: "No special footwear needed", text: "The whole bay has a seabed covered in soft, fine sand, making it a pleasure to walk barefoot through the water." }, { titlu: "Swimming goggles", text: "The water is so calm it feels like a pool, ideal for long swims or lessons for little ones." }],
    preturi: "Being a private beach with premium services, there's an entry fee (around €3-5 per person). Renting a set of two sunbeds with an umbrella costs around €15-20. A drink at the beach bar costs about €4-5, and the complex also has an excellent seaside tavern.",
    turisti: [{ titlu: "Spotless cleanliness", text: "All reviews praise how the sand is raked daily and the water is completely free of seaweed or stones." }, { titlu: "Perfect for families", text: "Parents appreciate the safety of the place, the gentle entry into the sea and the presence of lifeguards." }],
    tips: [{ titlu: "Best time to go", text: "Come in the morning around 9:30 AM. You'll catch the cool of the pine forest, a good shaded parking spot, and be able to feed the deer in the complex before the beach gets very busy." }],
  },
  "Plaja Possidi Kassandra": {
    scurt: "Possidi beach (more precisely, Possidi Cape) is one of the most astonishing natural phenomena in Halkidiki. Picture a huge, sharp \"tongue\" of fine, brilliant white sand, stretching several hundred metres straight into the deep waters of the Aegean. What makes it truly magical is that it changes shape, length and orientation from one week to the next, depending on sea currents and wind. It's a completely wild, spectacular, and wonderfully open place.",
    cumAjungi: "The beach lies in the south-west of the Kassandra peninsula, near the village of Possidi. Public transport only drops you in the village centre, from where you'd have quite a few kilometres to walk in the sun. A car is essential to reach this spectacular spot. The road to the historic lighthouse (built in 1864), at the base of the sand spit, is paved. You can leave your car for free in the dirt car park by the lighthouse. From there, the adventure continues on foot: about a 10-15 minute walk over hot sand to the sharp tip of the peninsula.",
    echipament: [{ titlu: "Your own beach umbrella and a beach tent", text: "On the Possidi sand spit there is absolutely no beach bar, sunbed or tree. It's just you, the sand and the sea, so your own shade is a matter of survival." }, { titlu: "A cool box full of water and snacks", text: "The nearest shop is in the village, at least a 20-minute walk away." }, { titlu: "Be very careful when swimming", text: "Never swim at the very tip of the sand spit! The currents there are incredibly strong and unpredictable, making the sea extremely dangerous even for professional swimmers." }],
    preturi: "Access to the Possidi Cape sand spit is completely free and open, as is the parking near the lighthouse. If you want comfort, at the start of the beach (near the hotels) there are organised areas where a set of sunbeds costs around €12-15. At the taverns in Possidi village, a delicious traditional lunch costs around €15 per person.",
    turisti: [{ titlu: "You feel like you're in the middle of the ocean", text: "Tourists are fascinated by the feeling of standing at the tip of the sand spit, with the sea to your left, right and straight ahead." }, { titlu: "Walking through the sand is hard work", text: "Many warn that the sand is very soft and fine, making the hike to the tip with heavy bags quite tiring." }],
    tips: [{ titlu: "Best time to go", text: "Plan your visit after 4:30 PM or even at sunset. The sun is no longer so harsh (important, given there's no shade), and photos of the historic lighthouse with the sea crashing in from two different directions have absolutely magical light." }],
  },
  "Plaja Xenia Kassandra": {
    scurt: "Xenia beach (also known locally as Chroussou or Paliouri) is considered one of the best and most comfortable family beaches on all of Kassandra. Set in a wide bay, well sheltered from the wind, the beach offers extremely fine, clean sand that's pleasant to the touch, in a warm golden colour. The sea is warm, astonishingly clear, and very shallow for a long stretch out, making it feel like a giant pool for kids.",
    cumAjungi: "The beach is at the very southern tip of the Kassandra peninsula, near the village of Paliouri. Being close to the end of the peninsula, the distance from the lively resorts up north is considerable. Public transport is rare and only stops on the main road, leaving you with a tiring walk down. By car you get there quickly and can drive right down behind the beach. There's a very large dirt car park, partly shaded by pines, where you can leave your car completely free.",
    echipament: [{ titlu: "Inflatable mattresses and sand toys", text: "It's the ideal beach for water activities; the seabed is exclusively fine sand, with no stones at all." }, { titlu: "No water shoes needed", text: "You don't need special footwear here, the risk of getting pricked or slipping is basically zero." }, { titlu: "Strong sunscreen", text: "With the water shallow and warm, you'll tend to spend hours in the sea without noticing time pass." }],
    preturi: "The beach is split between a few large beach bars and extended free areas. A set of two sunbeds with an umbrella costs around €15-20 (often via a required minimum spend at the bar). A frappe costs €4, a burger or club sandwich portion is around €8-10. Local vendors occasionally pass by the beach with warm honey-and-cinnamon doughnuts (€3).",
    turisti: [{ titlu: "A paradise for families with children", text: "Parents unanimously praise the very gentle entry into the water and the total absence of big waves." }, { titlu: "Gets busy on weekends", text: "Tourists note that on Saturdays and Sundays the beach gets quite full, also visited by many locals from Thessaloniki." }],
    tips: [{ titlu: "Best time to go", text: "Head to the left side of the beach (facing the sea), near the small harbour where the boats leave from. There the pines are closer to the sand, and the water is often the calmest in the whole bay." }],
  },
  "Plaja Hanioti Kassandra": {
    scurt: "Hanioti beach is the town beach of one of Kassandra's most charming and popular resorts. If you love the classic style of holiday, where a long, well-organised beach blends perfectly with a green park, traditional taverns and lively pedestrian streets, Hanioti will win you over instantly. The beach is made of a mix of fine sand and small pebbles at the water's edge, and the sea is a clean, refreshing blue.",
    cumAjungi: "Hanioti sits on Kassandra's east coast. If you're staying right in the resort, you can reach the beach in a few minutes on foot. If you're visiting from other parts of the peninsula, a car is the best choice. Finding a free parking spot on the narrow streets near the beach can be nearly impossible in July and August. Our advice is to leave the car in the large public car parks at the resort entrance or in the paid private lots (around €5 per day), then walk through the central park down to the sea.",
    echipament: [{ titlu: "Aqua shoes", text: "Although there's plenty of sand on shore, the water entry has a fairly wide band of round stones that can bother bare feet." }, { titlu: "Snorkelling mask", text: "Around the piers or stone platforms in the water you can spot plenty of small fish." }, { titlu: "Comfortable evening shoes", text: "The seafront and resort centre turn fully pedestrian in the afternoon, ideal for long strolls." }],
    preturi: "It's the classic Greek system: most beach bars give you a free sunbed if you order drinks or snacks from them worth a minimum amount (around €15-20 per set). A frappe costs €4, and a cold beer is €4.50. The taverns behind the beach offer excellent menus, with a full dinner for two reaching €35-45.",
    turisti: [{ titlu: "The park behind the beach is a blessing", text: "Tourists really appreciate the leafy park bordering the beach, offering a perfect shaded spot for a walk at midday." }, { titlu: "Gets deep fairly fast", text: "Reviews mention the water isn't as shallow near shore as at Xenia beach, deepening after just a few steps." }],
    tips: [{ titlu: "Best time to go", text: "Stay on the beach or at a seafront terrace until dusk falls. Hanioti has a wonderful summer atmosphere at sunset, when the souvenir stalls open up and the air fills with the smell of roasted corn and warm waffles." }],
  },
  "Plaja Glarokavos Kassandra": {
    scurt: "Glarokavos beach is one of the most interesting and well-kept secrets in the south of the Kassandra peninsula. Also known as the \"Glarokavos Lagoon\", this spot is actually a unique combination of a huge, completely wild beach, a coastal pine forest, and a hidden natural lagoon that serves as a natural harbour for small fishing boats. The beach has white sand mixed with fine pebbles, and the water has remarkable clarity, perfect for those wanting to escape the commercial resorts.",
    cumAjungi: "The beach is about 4 km south of the resort of Pefkohori. There are no bus lines that drop you near the lagoon. A car is required to explore this area. The road from Pefkohori is mostly paved, but the final approach to the beach and around the lagoon runs on fairly uneven dirt and sand tracks. You can drive slowly and park the car completely free wherever you like, right under the old pines that give dense, cool shade throughout the day.",
    echipament: [{ titlu: "A portable cool box and an umbrella", text: "Although a beach bar has appeared at one end in recent years, most of the beach (stretching for kilometres) remains completely wild and unorganised." }, { titlu: "Aqua shoes", text: "Useful since the sea entry has stretches with gravel and flat stones." }, { titlu: "Snorkelling or fishing gear", text: "The area around where the lagoon meets the sea is an excellent spot to observe marine wildlife." }],
    preturi: "Being a mostly free beach, costs are minimal or zero. If you choose to sit in the beach-bar area, a set of sunbeds involves a minimum spend of around €15-20. A large bottle of still water is €1.50, and a frappe costs around €4. For lunch, it's best to drive a few minutes back to Pefkohori.",
    turisti: [{ titlu: "Huge space and quiet", text: "Every tourist looking to escape the crowds of Pefkohori praises Glarokavos's impressive size, where you can sit a huge distance from anyone else." }, { titlu: "Perfect spot for camping vibes and shade", text: "Many visitors appreciate the pines that let you park cars in deep shade." }],
    tips: [{ titlu: "Best time to go", text: "Head to the exact spot where the narrow lagoon opens into the open sea. The scenery there, with wooden fishing boats slowly passing the sand spit, is incredibly picturesque and offers a perfect setting for relaxed holiday photos." }],
  },
  "Plaja Kalogria Sithonia": {
    scurt: "Kalogria beach is a long, elegant strip of fine golden sand on Sithonia's west coast, an area known for its calm waters and warm sunsets. What makes it special is the water's clarity — the sea has a superb light turquoise tint and is so transparent you can perfectly see fish swimming past your feet. It's a well-balanced beach, offering both areas with modern bars and large stretches of free beach.",
    cumAjungi: "Kalogria is about 6 km south of Nikiti. Although it's close to the main paved road, the distance isn't one to walk from any large resort. A car gives you the flexibility to get there in just a few minutes from Nikiti or Neos Marmaras. Parking near the beach is free, on dirt, set up along the narrow access road, but shaded spots run out quickly after about 9:30 AM.",
    echipament: [{ titlu: "Swimming goggles or mask", text: "Right in the middle of the bay, about 50 metres from shore, sits a small rocky island (a large pine-topped rock). It's a pleasure to swim out to it and snorkel around it, as it's teeming with marine life." }, { titlu: "Water-resistant sunscreen", text: "The entry into the sea is very gentle, over fine sand, which will make you want to spend a lot of time in the water." }],
    preturi: "The beach has organised beach-bar areas where a set of two sunbeds with an umbrella costs around €15-20 (or a required minimum spend at the bar). A frappe costs around €4, a cocktail is €9-11, and a quick bar snack runs to €8.",
    turisti: [{ titlu: "The water feels like a pool", text: "All tourists praise the lack of stones and the water's clarity, considered one of the cleanest beaches on the peninsula." }, { titlu: "Busy parking", text: "Many warn that the access road is narrow and parking can turn chaotic around lunchtime." }],
    tips: [{ titlu: "Best time to go", text: "Stay on the beach late. Facing west, Kalogria offers one of the most spectacular, clean sunsets in Sithonia, with the sun sinking straight into the sea behind the distant Kassandra peninsula." }],
  },
  "Plaja Tristinika Sithonia": {
    scurt: "If you want to fully escape the crowds and are looking for huge, open, breezy space, Tristinika beach is the perfect destination. Located in south-west Sithonia, it's a massive beach, several kilometres long and very wide, made of clean golden sand. The sea here is clean, a deep, open blue, offering a unique sense of freedom. It's the ideal place for those who just want to hear the breeze and the waves, with no club music in the background.",
    cumAjungi: "The beach is near the village of Toroni. Access from the main road is via a secondary unpaved dirt track, about 1.5 km long, passing a few farms and olive groves. Public transport doesn't reach the area at all. A car is absolutely necessary to cover this route without hassle. Parking is huge, free and open, right on the dirt field behind the sand dunes.",
    echipament: [{ titlu: "Your own umbrella and a beach tent", text: "With the beach being immense and mostly completely wild, there are no pines or natural shade near the water." }, { titlu: "A comfortable beach mat", text: "The sand is excellent, but the huge space will tempt you into long sunbathing sessions." }, { titlu: "Watch the kids", text: "Entry into the water is fairly sudden, with the sea getting deep after just 3-4 steps from shore." }],
    preturi: "Being mostly a free beach, the cost is zero. However, at one end there's the famous Ethnik bar, a bohemian bar perched up on the rock, with a relaxed, hippie vibe. A beer at the bar costs €4-5, a cocktail is €10, and sunbeds below the bar rent for around €15 per set.",
    turisti: [{ titlu: "Endless space", text: "Tourists are delighted they don't have to sit \"packed like sardines\" and can have a huge area to themselves, even in peak summer." }, { titlu: "Ethnik Bar is worth visiting", text: "Everyone praises the design and vibe of the bar on the rock." }],
    tips: [{ titlu: "Best time to go", text: "Come in the afternoon around 4:00 PM. Enjoy a relaxing swim in the deep, clean sea, and at sunset make sure to head up to the Ethnik bar terrace. It's considered one of the best spots in all of Halkidiki to sip a cocktail while watching the sun set spectacularly into the sea." }],
  },
  "Plaja Porto Koufo Sithonia": {
    scurt: "Porto Koufo is one of the safest and most unusual maritime locations in Greece. Its name means \"Deaf Harbour\", since it's the country's largest and deepest natural harbour — a huge bay almost entirely enclosed by tall rocky mountains, leaving just a narrow opening to the sea. Because of this, there are never waves or wind inside the bay, with the sea as flat and calm as a mountain lake. The beach is a long, narrow strip of sand mixed with pebbles, ideal for a day of total relaxation.",
    cumAjungi: "The location is at the very southern tip of Sithonia. The long distance from the entrance to the peninsula makes a car the only sensible way to get there. The main road circling the peninsula drops you right at the entrance to Porto Koufo village. Access is fully paved and very scenic, offering a stunning panoramic view over the whole natural harbour from above. You can park completely free in the public car parks near the small fishing harbour, or even on the roadside near the beach.",
    echipament: [{ titlu: "Aqua shoes", text: "Although there's plenty of sand on shore, entering the inner sea goes over round, fairly steep pebbles." }, { titlu: "Snorkelling gear or swimming goggles", text: "With the water extremely deep in the middle of the bay (used in the past as a submarine hideout during the war), and rock walls along the edges, marine life is very rich." }, { titlu: "Skip large mattresses if it's windy offshore", text: "Although the bay itself is calm, currents at the opening to the sea can be deceptive." }],
    preturi: "The beach is mostly free and open, with only small organised areas run by local guesthouses. The great advantage here is the food: Porto Koufo is famous for the best fish taverns in Halkidiki. A hearty meal of fresh fish brought in by fishermen that same morning, or grilled squid, costs around €15-20 per person.",
    turisti: [{ titlu: "The freshest fish on the peninsula", text: "Every review recommends having lunch or dinner at the harbour taverns, the food being legendary." }, { titlu: "A strange but fascinating sea", text: "Tourists often note the unusual feeling of swimming in a completely calm sea, surrounded by huge rocky mountains." }],
    tips: [{ titlu: "Best time to go", text: "Come in the second half of the day for a relaxing swim in the calm water, and towards evening book a table at one of the waterfront taverns (such as Taverna O Psaras). The atmosphere with wooden fishing boats pulling in at sunset is incredibly picturesque and authentically Greek." }],
  },
  "Plaja Alykes Zakynthos": {
    scurt: "Alykes beach sits on the island's north-east coast and takes its name from the old salt pans (alykes in Greek) behind the resort. It's a gorgeous, long, narrow beach covered in extremely fine white sand, giving the sea an incredibly bright light-turquoise tint. The bay is very well sheltered, offering warm, extremely calm water, flat as a mirror, considered one of the safest beaches on the island.",
    cumAjungi: "Alykes is about 18 km north of Zakynthos Town. The coastal road leading here is paved, scenic and easy to drive. Public transport is fairly rare on this route. A car is the best option for arriving early and also exploring the neighbouring beach, Alykanas, in the same bay. Parking is free, along the secondary road behind the beach or in the dedicated spaces of the seafront taverns.",
    echipament: [{ titlu: "Inflatable mattress", text: "With the sea completely wave-free most days, it's a pleasure to float on the water." }, { titlu: "No aqua shoes needed", text: "Entry into the Ionian Sea is extremely gentle, exclusively over soft, clean sand, perfect for children." }, { titlu: "Snorkelling mask", text: "The water is very clear, though marine life is more active towards the rocky edges of the bay." }],
    preturi: "Prices are very friendly: a set of sunbeds costs around €10-15, or is offered for free if you order lunch or drinks from the seafront taverns. A frappe costs €3.50, and a portion of fresh fish or baked local dishes costs around €11-14.",
    turisti: [{ titlu: "Ideal for a family relaxation", text: "All reviews praise the total safety the shallow water near shore offers for children, and the calm atmosphere." }, { titlu: "Picturesque scenery", text: "Tourists appreciate the nearby old stone bridge and the small river that flows into the sea." }],
    tips: [{ titlu: "Best time to go", text: "Come in the morning around 9:15 AM. The scenery is incredibly quiet then, the water is completely clear, and you can take a short walk behind the resort to see the channels of the old historic salt pans." }],
  },
  "Plaja Alykanas Zakynthos": {
    scurt: "Alykanas beach shares the same large bay with Alykes beach, being its natural continuation to the south. It's a wide beach with fine golden sand, with a somewhat more open, relaxed feel than its neighbour. The sea is remarkably clean, with a gorgeous turquoise colour and a very gentle entry. Alykanas blends the comfort of a fully organised beach with wide stretches of untouched nature, where pines come down close to the sand.",
    cumAjungi: "Alykanas is about 16 km north of the island's capital. With a rental car you get there quickly on the main paved road. A car is a big advantage, since the resort is spread out and the beach has several secondary access points. You can park completely free in the large dirt areas behind the beach or near the small tourist harbour at the end of the bay.",
    echipament: [{ titlu: "Snorkelling mask", text: "Around the harbour and the stone breakwater at the end of the beach, the water hides many small fish species, making it a great spot to explore." }, { titlu: "Your own umbrella (optional)", text: "If you want to settle in the less commercial, more open parts of the beach, you'll have plenty of space for your towel." }, { titlu: "No aqua shoes needed", text: "The seabed is clean, with no stones or sea urchins." }],
    preturi: "Renting a set of two sunbeds with an umbrella ranges between €10-15, depending on the bar. Many traditional taverns offer sunbeds for free to customers who order food. A full lunch of traditional Greek dishes costs around €12-15 per person.",
    turisti: [{ titlu: "More space than Alykes", text: "Many tourists note in reviews that Alykanas feels somewhat wider and less crowded than Alykes, offering more privacy." }, { titlu: "Great boat trips", text: "Tourists appreciate that from the small harbour here you can take boats for a much quicker trip to Navagio Beach or the Blue Caves up north." }],
    tips: [{ titlu: "Best time to go", text: "Stay on the beach into the late afternoon. As the sun starts setting behind the western mountains, the whole bay gets a warm, peaceful, very relaxing atmosphere." }],
  },
  "Plaja Agios Nikolaos Zakynthos": {
    scurt: "Agios Nikolaos beach (in the Vassilikos area, not to be confused with the harbour of the same name in the north) is one of the most spectacular organised beaches in the south of the island. It has fine golden sand and rare, deep-blue water clarity. Its landmark feature is a small white stone church perched on a rocky hill at the right end of the beach, giving the place an authentic Greek feel and a stunning backdrop for photos.",
    cumAjungi: "The beach is in the south-east of the island, about 15 km from Zakynthos Town. The access road through the Vassilikos peninsula is fully paved, winding through pine and olive groves. Although some of the big beach bars run free buses from major resorts, their schedules are fixed and limit you. With a rental car you have total freedom. Parking down by the beach is huge, laid out on dirt in the shade of trees, and completely free.",
    echipament: [{ titlu: "Budget for water sports or diving", text: "The beach is home to one of the best scuba diving and water sports centres on the island." }, { titlu: "No aqua shoes needed", text: "Entry into the water is very gentle and clean, exclusively over soft sand, making it extremely pleasant." }, { titlu: "Camera/phone", text: "A short walk up to the little white church on the rocks will give you a stunning panoramic view of the whole bay." }],
    preturi: "Sunbed sets with an umbrella cost around €15-20, though you can also find areas included with a minimum spend at the modern beach bars along the shore. A frappe costs €4, a cocktail is around €10, and a light meal at the taverns above the beach costs around €15 per person.",
    turisti: [{ titlu: "Great atmosphere and good music", text: "Tourists praise the beach's vibe, a lively, clean and very well-kept spot." }, { titlu: "The hilltop church is worth visiting", text: "Everyone recommends the easy climb up to the chapel for the spectacular view." }],
    tips: [{ titlu: "Best time to go", text: "Arrive around 9:45 AM to grab the best shaded parking spots and sunbeds close to the sea. For an excellent snorkelling session, head right to the base of the rock the church sits on, where marine life is extremely rich." }],
  },
  "Plaja Porto Vromi Zakynthos": {
    scurt: "Porto Vromi is actually a narrow, deep natural fjord, hidden among steep mountain slopes covered in Mediterranean vegetation. It's not a large classic beach, but a picturesque little cove with white pebbles and water of an unreal clarity, in intense shades of emerald and turquoise. The place has a very picturesque, wild feel, while also serving as the main departure point for boats taking tourists to the famous Navagio beach.",
    cumAjungi: "Porto Vromi is on the west coast, completely isolated from the big commercial resorts. There are two separate roads leading down to this fjord (one from Anafonitria village, one from Maries) which don't meet at the bottom. A rental car is absolutely essential, since public transport doesn't reach here at all. The drive is spectacular, with tight switchbacks and steep slopes, but fully paved. Down by the water, there's a small dirt car park where you can leave the car completely free.",
    echipament: [{ titlu: "Aqua shoes", text: "The shore and seabed are entirely covered with white stones and pebbles; special footwear is vital for comfort." }, { titlu: "Snorkelling mask", text: "Since the bay is naturally sheltered by tall rocks, the water is calm as a pool and full of fish along the underwater rock walls." }, { titlu: "Camera/phone", text: "The fjord scenery seen from above as you drive down is simply spectacular." }],
    preturi: "Being a very small beach, it's not set up with sunbeds on a large commercial scale. There's a small canteen/bar near the jetty where you can buy water, frappes or juices for €3-4. A rented boat trip or an organised tour from here to Navagio and the Blue Caves will cost around €20-25 per person.",
    turisti: [{ titlu: "The best starting point for Navagio", text: "Tourists recommend Porto Vromi because it's the closest harbour to the shipwreck beach, meaning a shorter boat ride and less seasickness." }, { titlu: "An authentic place", text: "Many appreciate the lack of hotels and the pure, uncommercial feel of the cove." }],
    tips: [{ titlu: "Best time to go", text: "Come in the morning around 8:30 AM. You'll find parking right by the boats, avoid the crowds, and be able to catch the first morning boat to Navagio to get the beach empty. Also, look at the rock face of the bay for the \"Profile of Poseidon\" — a rock shape naturally carved by the wind that perfectly resembles a human face." }],
  },
  "Plaja Makris Gialos Zakynthos": {
    scurt: "Makris Gialos is a gorgeous, long and relatively narrow beach on the island's mountainous north-east coast. Unlike the sandy beaches in the south, Makris Gialos offers a dramatic setting, with clean white pebbles and an incredibly clear, electric-blue sea. The bay is deep and clean, considered one of the best spots in Zakynthos for those wanting to swim in deep, clear water within a spectacular natural setting flanked by cliffs.",
    cumAjungi: "The beach is about 25 km north of the capital, Zakynthos Town, on the secondary coastal road towards Agios Nikolaos harbour. Public transport is rare and totally impractical for a beach day. A rental car gives you a relaxed drive on a fully paved road with dreamy sea views. Parking is free, either right along the road above the beach or in the small organised car park by the local tavern. Access to the water is down a few easy stone steps.",
    echipament: [{ titlu: "Aqua shoes", text: "The white pebbles on the beach and in the water can be uncomfortable to walk on and get very hot around midday." }, { titlu: "Snorkelling mask and snorkel", text: "With the water deep and flanked by rock walls, underwater life is very rich. You can also explore small sea caves reachable by swimming right from the beach." }, { titlu: "Your own umbrella (optional)", text: "The organised sunbed area is small, so if you want to sit in the free zone, you'll need your own shade." }],
    preturi: "In the small organised area, a set of two sunbeds and an umbrella costs around €10-15. Right above the beach there's an excellent traditional Greek tavern. A frappe costs €3.50, and a lunch of fresh fish or tasty souvlaki costs around €12-15 per person.",
    turisti: [{ titlu: "The water's clarity is amazing", text: "Visitors praise the sea's transparency, mentioning you can see the bottom even where the water is very deep." }, { titlu: "Mind the water depth", text: "Reviews warn that the water gets deep after just two steps from shore, making it not ideal for young children." }],
    tips: [{ titlu: "Best time to go", text: "Arrive around 9:30 AM to grab a good roadside parking spot and enjoy the sea when it's perfectly calm. Shorter, cheaper private boat tours to the Blue Caves are also organised from this spot." }],
  },
  "Plaja Pelagaki Zakynthos": {
    scurt: "Pelagaki is a small, hidden, extremely intimate beach right next to the much better-known Xigia beach. It's known locally as the \"Warm Springs\", since much of its water is influenced by the same therapeutic sulphur springs with collagen properties as Xigia. It's a picturesque cove flanked by tall cliffs, covered in fine white pebbles, offering a distinctive milky-blue sea, and it's much less crowded than its neighbour.",
    cumAjungi: "The location is on the north-east coast, about 22 km from Zakynthos Town. There's no bus line that drops you near this hidden cove. A rental car is essential. Access is from the coastal road towards Agios Nikolaos, down a narrow secondary road. You can park for free on the dirt area above the beach, near a small tavern. From there, a set of steps leads straight down to the sand.",
    echipament: [{ titlu: "Aqua shoes", text: "Recommended for walking comfortably over the pebbles on the beach and at the entry into the deep water." }, { titlu: "Snorkelling mask", text: "The milky, mineral-rich water offers an unusual swimming experience, and near the rocks you can spot marine life drawn by the springs." }, { titlu: "Sealed bags for your belongings", text: "A sulphur smell (similar to boiled eggs) is present due to the therapeutic springs; it's a good idea to keep dry clothes protected in your bag." }],
    preturi: "The beach has a small organised area in peak season, where a set of sunbeds costs around €12-15. The tavern above serves drinks and quick snacks. A frappe costs €3.50, and a quick lunch such as a salad or souvlaki is around €8-11.",
    turisti: [{ titlu: "Quieter than Xigia", text: "Tourists see it as a great alternative to the main Xigia beach, with the same therapeutic water properties but far fewer people." }, { titlu: "The distinctive smell", text: "Most reviews mention the strong sulphur smell, but note you get used to it after the first 10 minutes." }],
    tips: [{ titlu: "Best time to go", text: "Come around 10:00 AM. The sun lights the bay directly in the first part of the day, making the water's colour look almost phosphorescent. The water has an excellent therapeutic effect on skin and joints thanks to the sulphur and natural collagen in the springs." }],
  },
  "Plaja Agiofili Lefkada": {
    scurt: "Agiofili is a true hidden gem tucked into a picturesque little cove in the south of the island. Wedged between white limestone cliffs covered in green shrubs, the beach will win you over instantly with its stunning water clarity, resembling a natural aquarium. The beach is made of small, shiny white pebbles, and the sea has a light turquoise colour so clean it's considered one of the best snorkelling spots on Lefkada.",
    cumAjungi: "The beach is just 3 km from the southern resort of Vassiliki. A rental car will get you along the paved road from Vassiliki, followed by a short, fairly narrow unpaved forest track up to the private car park above the beach (costs around €5). From the car park, you go down a set of wooden steps straight onto the sand. Alternatively, you can leave the car in Vassiliki and take a water taxi from the harbour.",
    echipament: [{ titlu: "Snorkelling mask is a must", text: "The water's clarity and the rocky terrain make this bay the perfect spot to watch fish swimming right by the shore." }, { titlu: "Aqua shoes", text: "Walking barefoot on the white pebbles can hurt, and the water entry is full of rounded stones." }, { titlu: "Polarised sunglasses", text: "The white rocks reflect strong light at midday." }],
    preturi: "If you choose the boat option from Vassiliki, the ticket costs around €7-8 return. On the beach there's a small organised area in season where a set of sunbeds costs €15-20. There are no large taverns down there, just a small drinks kiosk, so a bottle of still water is around €1.50.",
    turisti: [{ titlu: "A miniature natural aquarium", text: "All snorkelling fans praise the water's clarity and the large numbers of fish." }, { titlu: "Gets tight at lunchtime", text: "With the bay being small, the beach feels very crowded as soon as tourist boats start arriving." }],
    tips: [{ titlu: "Best time to go", text: "Come very early in the morning, before 9:00 AM, by car. You'll find the bay completely empty, the sea flat as a mirror, and enjoy total quiet before the first water taxis bring groups of tourists from the harbour." }],
  },
  "Plaja Vassiliki Lefkada": {
    scurt: "Vassiliki beach, in the wide bay in the south of the island, is recognised worldwide as one of the best windsurfing spots in all of Europe. This is due to a unique weather phenomenon called \"Eric\" — a strong local wind that regularly starts blowing every afternoon from the surrounding mountains over the bay. The beach is a long strip made of a mix of sand and fine gravel, and the water is warm and very safe.",
    cumAjungi: "Vassiliki is a major resort in the south of the island, about 38 km from Lefkada Town. The main road crossing the island from north to south is fully paved, wide and offers stunning scenery. A car gives you the comfort of bringing beach gear along and stopping at traditional villages on the way. Parking is very easy: there are large free public spaces right behind the beach and along the resort's seafront.",
    echipament: [{ titlu: "Aqua shoes", text: "Useful especially at the sea entry, where the pebbles can bother bare feet." }, { titlu: "Budget for windsurfing lessons", text: "Even if you've never tried it before, the schools on the beach offer excellent instructors and full beginner gear." }, { titlu: "A light jacket for the afternoon", text: "The afternoon wind is strong and can leave you feeling chilly once you're out of the water." }],
    preturi: "Sunbed sets belong to the bars and windsurfing clubs along the shore and cost around €10-15 a day, or are included with a similar minimum spend. An excellent lunch at the well-known fish taverns in Vassiliki harbour costs around €12-15 per person.",
    turisti: [{ titlu: "The colourful sail show", text: "Tourists mention the sight of hundreds of windsurfers filling the bay every afternoon as a standout attraction." }, { titlu: "Mornings are perfect for kids", text: "In the first part of the day, the sea is completely calm, wind-free and very safe for little ones." }],
    tips: [{ titlu: "Best time to go", text: "If you want a quiet swim or you're bringing kids, come in the morning between 8:30 and 11:30 AM. The bay is flat as a lake then. If you want adrenaline and want to try windsurfing, your moment is after 2:00 PM, when the wind kicks in at full strength." }],
  },
  "Plaja Nidri Lefkada": {
    scurt: "Nidri beach is the town beach of Lefkada's liveliest and most developed resort. It's a long, relatively narrow beach, made of a mix of sand and fine gravel, but its big draw is the view. The bay faces east and is completely sheltered by a stunning archipelago of green islands offshore (including the famous private island Skorpios, once owned by the Onassis family). Because of this, the water here is warm, extremely calm and flat as a lake, with no big waves.",
    cumAjungi: "Nidri is on the east coast, about 17 km from the capital. The road is fully paved and very straight. If you're staying in Nidri, you can walk there right away. If you're driving in from other areas, parking on the narrow streets near the water can be tough in peak season. It's best to use the large paid public car parks (around €3-5 per day) signposted at the resort entrance and walk two minutes to the sand.",
    echipament: [{ titlu: "Aqua shoes", text: "The small pebbles at the sea entry can be uncomfortable to walk on." }, { titlu: "Motorboat rental", text: "Nidri is the best spot on the island to rent a small motorboat (no license needed) and explore the green islands offshore." }, { titlu: "Casual clothes for the promenade", text: "The area behind the beach is packed with lively restaurants, cafes and souvenir shops." }],
    preturi: "Sunbed sets with an umbrella cost around €10-15 a day, often offered for free with a similar order from the bar. A frappe costs €3.50, and a full lunch at the seafront taverns comes to about €13-15 per person.",
    turisti: [{ titlu: "A million-dollar view", text: "Everyone praises the view of the green islands on the horizon, which block the big waves and give the beach a unique atmosphere." }, { titlu: "Full infrastructure", text: "Visitors appreciate having every possible facility just steps away." }],
    tips: [{ titlu: "Best time to go", text: "This beach makes an ideal afternoon stop. And if you want a short nature adventure, take the car and drive 10 minutes to the Dimosari Waterfalls (at the edge of the Nidri resort). A cool walk through the gorge to the waterfall hidden in the mountains is the perfect way to round off a great day." }],
  },
  "Plaja Gyra Lefkada": {
    scurt: "Gyra beach is a long, spectacular strip of fine sand mixed with pebbles, on the far north of the island, along the sandbar that closes off the lagoon in front of Lefkada Town. It's an open, breezy beach facing straight out to the open sea, meaning the water is incredibly clean, refreshing and a deep blue. The scenery is completed in a striking way by the historic windmills visible in the distance.",
    cumAjungi: "The beach is just 3-4 km from the island's capital (Lefkada Town). A car is extremely useful, since the road around the lagoon is fully paved, flat and very fast to drive. By car you can cover this whole northern stretch of coast and switch spots within minutes. Parking is huge, on dirt right behind the dunes, and completely free and open at any time of day.",
    echipament: [{ titlu: "Your own beach umbrella", text: "Although there's a small organised sunbed area near the main tavern, most of this several-kilometre-long beach remains completely wild." }, { titlu: "Camera", text: "The lagoon on one side of the road and the open sea on the other offer great opportunities for unique photos." }, { titlu: "No large inflatables on windy days", text: "Being exposed towards the open sea, the breeze can create currents that quickly pull you away from shore." }],
    preturi: "In the small organised area, a set of two sunbeds with an umbrella costs around €10-12. There's an excellent traditional tavern right on the roadside, where a frappe costs €3.50, and a portion of souvlaki or a fresh Greek salad is around €8-11.",
    turisti: [{ titlu: "Peace just minutes from town", text: "Tourists really appreciate being able to escape the capital's bustle in just a 5-minute drive, finding a beach with plenty of space." }, { titlu: "Fun waves", text: "Many reviews note that nice waves often form in the afternoon, perfect for a bit of fun." }],
    tips: [{ titlu: "Best time to go", text: "Stay on the beach or drive along the sand spit at sunset. Facing north-west, Gyra puts on a stunning show as the sun dips into the sea, painting the sky and the lagoon in intense shades of pink and purple." }],
  },
  "Plaja Ammoglossa Lefkada": {
    scurt: "Ammoglossa literally means \"Sand Tongue\", and the beach lives up to its name to the letter, sitting right at the entrance to the island, next to the swing bridge and the historic Santa Maura fortress. It's a spectacular tongue of extremely fine, soft white sand stretching into the sea. The water here is incredibly clear and warm, ranging in tint from light green to electric blue. It's a completely wild beach, perfect for those wanting an unforgettable first swim right after crossing onto the island.",
    cumAjungi: "The beach sits exactly at the link point between the mainland and Lefkada. A car is essential to reach the island, and Ammoglossa is the first strategic stop. The road is fully paved. You can leave the car for free in the dirt car park near the Santa Maura fortress, or even on the roadside near the beach access. From there, it's just a one-minute walk over the fine sand.",
    echipament: [{ titlu: "Beach umbrella and mat", text: "The beach is 100% wild and protected. There are no sunbeds, bars or natural shade, so come fully equipped from home." }, { titlu: "No aqua shoes needed", text: "The seabed is covered in fine, very pleasant sand, with no stones or sea urchins." }, { titlu: "Portable cool box", text: "Bring cold drinks and snacks with you, as the nearest shop is in town." }],
    preturi: "Being a completely public, free beach, access and parking cost nothing. If you want to visit the medieval Santa Maura fortress a minute away (which we highly recommend), the entry ticket costs around €3-4.",
    turisti: [{ titlu: "A magical first stop", text: "Many tourists say in reviews that stopping at Ammoglossa right after arriving on the island instantly gave them the perfect holiday vibe." }, { titlu: "Currents can be deceptive", text: "Because of its position between the lagoon and the open sea, the water deepens fairly abruptly, and currents at the tip of the sand tongue can be strong." }],
    tips: [{ titlu: "Best time to go", text: "Come in the morning between 8:30-10:30 AM. The sea is usually calm as a mirror, and the morning light perfectly lights up the old fortress walls behind you, creating a spectacular historic backdrop for swimming and photos." }],
  },
  "Plaja Nikiana Lefkada": {
    scurt: "Nikiana beach is a cosy, quiet town beach on the island's east coast, facing the fishing village of the same name. Made of a pleasant mix of fine sand and small white pebbles, the beach is spared from big waves thanks to its sheltered position in the inner bay between the island and the mainland. The sea is warm, clean and very calm, feeling like a relaxing natural pool, perfect for those wanting to escape the bustle of Nidri.",
    cumAjungi: "Nikiana is about 9 km north of Nidri and 9 km south of Lefkada Town. The main road along the east coast is fully paved, flat and very easy to drive. A rental car gives you the flexibility to cover this route quickly. Parking is free, either in spaces set up along the village's fishing harbour or on the secondary streets running down from the main road straight to the beach.",
    echipament: [{ titlu: "Aqua shoes", text: "Although there's plenty of sand on shore, the pebbles at the sea entry can be a little uncomfortable underfoot." }, { titlu: "Inflatable mattress or a stand-up paddle board (SUP)", text: "With the sea flat as a mirror most days, this is the ideal spot on the island for a quiet paddle." }, { titlu: "Swimming goggles", text: "Water visibility is excellent, ideal for long, relaxed swims." }],
    preturi: "Sunbed sets with an umbrella belong to the bars and taverns along the shore and cost around €10-12 a day, or are included with a similar minimum spend. A frappe costs €3.50, and a delicious lunch with fresh seafood at the traditional taverns in Nikiana harbour costs around €12-15 per person.",
    turisti: [{ titlu: "Intimate, relaxed atmosphere", text: "Visitors appreciate that the beach is never as packed or loud as Nidri, keeping a traditional Greek feel." }, { titlu: "Great for kids", text: "The gentle entry and total lack of waves are strong points parents mention often." }],
    tips: [{ titlu: "Best time to go", text: "Stay on the beach or at a harbour tavern for lunch. Nikiana's harbour is famous for local fishermen bringing in fresh catch every morning, offering one of the most authentic culinary experiences on the east coast." }],
  },
  "Plaja Desimi Lefkada": {
    scurt: "Desimi beach is a hidden gem in a deep, perfectly enclosed and sheltered bay, on the Vlycho valley peninsula in the east of the island. Flanked by spectacular mountain hills entirely covered by a dense forest of olive and pine trees, Desimi will surprise you with a completely flat, warm, wave-free sea of an incredible emerald-green colour. The beach is made of fine white pebbles and has an intimate, secluded, extremely soothing feel.",
    cumAjungi: "The beach is about 22 km south of Lefkada Town and just a few kilometres from Nidri. From the main paved road, a narrow, winding secondary road branches off, descending through olive groves to the beach. Public transport doesn't reach here at all, so a car is mandatory. Down behind the beach, parking space is fairly limited; you can leave the car for free at the two campsites in the area, or for a small fee (around €3-5) if you're not their guest.",
    echipament: [{ titlu: "Aqua shoes are a must", text: "The shore and the entire sea entry are made of pebbles and flat stones; special footwear ensures full comfort." }, { titlu: "Budget for renting a pedal boat or kayak", text: "Desimi bay is famous for the sea caves hidden along the surrounding cliffs, which you can reach very easily in just 10 minutes of kayaking." }, { titlu: "Snorkelling mask", text: "The rocky terrain around the bay's edges hides plenty of small fish species and marine plants." }],
    preturi: "Renting a pedal boat for an hour costs around €15. There are two excellent traditional taverns on the beach, run by local families. A set of sunbeds costs around €10-12 (or a minimum spend at the tavern). A frappe costs €3.50, and a portion of fresh grilled squid is around €11-13.",
    turisti: [{ titlu: "A natural emerald pool", text: "All visitors praise the water's unique colour and the fact that the sea is completely calm, ideal for swimming in total safety." }, { titlu: "The hidden-caves adventure", text: "Exploring the sea caves by kayak is mentioned as a top holiday experience." }],
    tips: [{ titlu: "Best time to go", text: "Come around 9:30 AM. You'll get the best parking spot in the shade of the olive trees and can rent a kayak to explore the small sea caves along the cliffs before the sun gets too strong." }],
  },
  "Plaja Episkopos Lefkada": {
    scurt: "Episkopos beach is a small, narrow, extremely quiet strip on the island's east coast, in an area with lush vegetation. Made of a mix of coarse sand and round white pebbles, the beach offers a warm, clean, completely flat sea with no big waves or dangerous currents. It has a very intimate feel, ideal for those wanting to read a book in peace or take a quick swim, away from the commercial bustle of the big resorts.",
    cumAjungi: "Episkopos is about 8 km south of the capital, Lefkada Town, just 2 km before reaching Nikiana. The main road is fully paved, flat and winds right along the water's edge in this stretch. A rental car will get you there quickly and comfortably. Parking is simple and free: you can leave the vehicle right on the main roadside or in the small dirt pull-offs near the beach access.",
    echipament: [{ titlu: "Aqua shoes", text: "Recommended for walking comfortably over the pebbles at the sea entry." }, { titlu: "A good book or headphones", text: "With such a calm atmosphere, it's the ideal place for total relaxation with no background noise." }, { titlu: "Your own umbrella (optional)", text: "The commercially organised part is small, with the rest of the beach fully free for towels." }],
    preturi: "If you choose the sunbed area near the small guesthouses or cosy bars, a set costs around €8-10 a day, or a minimum spend at the bar. A frappe costs €3.50, a large water is €1.50, and a quick snack at the bar is around €6-8.",
    turisti: [{ titlu: "A perfect roadside stop", text: "Many tourists mention in reviews that Episkopos is the ideal beach for a quick one- or two-hour stop for a refreshing swim while exploring the east coast by car." }, { titlu: "Total peace and quiet", text: "Visitors appreciate the lack of stifling crowds and loud music." }],
    tips: [{ titlu: "Best time to go", text: "This beach is wonderful in the first part of the day, between 9:00 AM and noon. The sun lights the east coast directly then, making the sea look incredibly transparent and perfect for a long swim before lunch." }],
  },
  "Plaja Glyfada Vestul insulei": {
    scurt: "Glyfada is one of the most popular, largest and best-loved sandy beaches on all of Corfu. Located on the west coast, this beach is a generous stretch of fine, warm golden sand, spectacularly framed by steep cliffs covered in pines and olive trees. The sea has exceptional clarity and a superb turquoise tint. It's a full-service, very cosmopolitan beach, ideal for those seeking flawless comfort, modern beach bars and water sports in a dreamy natural setting.",
    cumAjungi: "The beach is about 16 km west of the island's capital, Corfu Town. The road crosses the island from east to west through a scenic mountainous area, full of tight bends and steep descents to the coast. Local buses run fairly infrequently and drop you on the main road, from where you have a walk. A rental car is essential to get here comfortably. Behind the beach there's a large public dirt car park where you can leave the car completely free, as well as paid spots (around €5-10) offered by bars.",
    echipament: [{ titlu: "No aqua shoes needed", text: "The whole bay has a seabed covered in soft, fine sand, and entry into the water is gentle and extremely pleasant." }, { titlu: "Budget for water sports", text: "Glyfada is known on the island for its excellent water sports centres (jet-ski, water skiing, pedal boats)." }, { titlu: "Polarised sunglasses", text: "The fine sand holds heat and reflects sunlight strongly around midday." }],
    preturi: "Depending on the beach bar you choose, renting a set of two sunbeds with an umbrella costs between €15-25 a day. A frappe at the bar costs €4, a cocktail is around €10, and a quick gyros or club sandwich lunch is around €7-10. The traditional taverns behind the beach offer fresh dishes, with a meal for two reaching €35-45.",
    turisti: [{ titlu: "A paradise for families and young people", text: "Tourists appreciate the gentle water entry and the quality of the services offered by the seafront bars (such as the famous Aloha bar)." }, { titlu: "The sunset is like something out of a story", text: "Facing west, the beach puts on a wonderful show as the sun sinks straight into the Ionian Sea." }],
    tips: [{ titlu: "Best time to go", text: "Arrive around 9:30 AM to grab a free parking spot closest to the sand. If you want a stunning view over the beach before heading down, stop the car on the roadside in Pelekas village (at the viewpoint called Kaiser's Throne)." }],
  },
  "Plaja Porto Timoni Corfu": {
    scurt: "Porto Timoni is, without doubt, the most famous, photographed and spectacular wild beach in Corfu. Picture two stunning twin beaches, set back to back and separated only by a narrow strip of green land. Each beach opens onto a different bay, meaning they have different water colours and temperatures: one is light turquoise, the other a deep emerald. The place is completely unspoiled, wild and hidden among steep rocky hills.",
    cumAjungi: "The beach is in the north-west of the island, near the traditional village of Afionas. Public transport doesn't reach this isolated area at all, so a rental car is absolutely essential. You drive to Afionas, where you can leave the car in a paid private car park at the village entrance (around €5 a day). From there, the adventure continues on foot: a demanding 20-30 minute hike down a rocky, steep path to the sea.",
    echipament: [{ titlu: "Comfortable sports shoes (trainers)", text: "The path is full of loose stones and steep sections. Going down or up in plain flip-flops is extremely dangerous." }, { titlu: "Your own beach umbrella and plenty of water", text: "Porto Timoni is 100% public and unorganised. There are no bars, shops or sunbeds down there. Come fully equipped with food and water from home." }, { titlu: "Aqua shoes", text: "Both twin beaches are made of a mix of pebbles and stones, both on shore and at the entry into the deep sea." }],
    preturi: "Access to the beach is completely free. The only mandatory cost is parking up in the village. If you don't want to make the tiring hike back up, you can hire a water taxi (a small boat) from the beach that will take you to the neighbouring Agios Georgios bay, for a fee of €10-15 per person.",
    turisti: [{ titlu: "The scenery is surreal", text: "Everyone recommends stopping halfway down the path for the famous overhead shot, where both twin bays are perfectly visible." }, { titlu: "The climb back up is tough", text: "Many tourists warn that the walk back up around midday is tiring and needs at least a minimum level of fitness." }],
    tips: [{ titlu: "Best time to go", text: "Arrive in Afionas village very early, ideally before 8:30 AM. You'll find parking easily, walk down the path in the shade, and enjoy the twin beaches in total peace before boats from nearby resorts start bringing large groups after 10:30 AM." }],
  },
  "Plaja Dassia Corfu": {
    scurt: "Dassia beach is a long, flat, excellently organised town beach on the island's east coast. Often praised for its complete infrastructure, the beach is made of a mix of fine sand and small white pebbles. Because it faces the inner bay between Corfu and the mainland, the sea here is warm, extremely calm and flat as a mirror, sheltered from big waves or dangerous currents. It's the favourite destination for those wanting comfort, water sports and modern bars along the shore.",
    cumAjungi: "Dassia is just 12 km north of the capital, Corfu Town, along the main coastal road. Access is very simple and fully paved. Although served by frequent local buses, a rental car offers huge comfort for carrying heavy beach bags and moving quickly towards the northern beaches in the afternoon. Parking is easy: there are plenty of free public spots on the secondary streets behind the beach, or dedicated spaces provided by the larger beach bars.",
    echipament: [{ titlu: "Aqua shoes", text: "Recommended especially at the entry into the calm sea, where small pebbles can be uncomfortable underfoot." }, { titlu: "Budget for water skiing or wakeboarding", text: "Dassia is known as an excellent spot for dynamic water sports thanks to a sea as flat as a lake." }, { titlu: "Casual daywear", text: "The seafront is lined with modern cafes and cosy restaurants where you can take a cool break at lunch." }],
    preturi: "Sets of two sunbeds with an umbrella cost around €12-20 a day, but you can also find modern bars (such as Malibu Beach Club) where the sunbed is included with a required minimum spend. A frappe costs €4, a cocktail is €9-11, and a full meal at the excellent seafront taverns comes to €15-20 per person.",
    turisti: [{ titlu: "Flawless infrastructure", text: "Tourists appreciate the cleanliness, and the presence of showers, changing rooms and lifeguards on the beach." }, { titlu: "A very safe sea", text: "All families with children praise the total lack of big waves and the warm water in this sheltered bay." }],
    tips: [{ titlu: "Best time to go", text: "Arrive around 9:30 AM. The bay is especially quiet in the first part of the day. If you want a green, grassy area with shade under trees right by the sand, head to the left end of the beach, where the atmosphere is much more relaxed and less commercial." }],
  },
  "Plaja Halikounas Corfu": {
    scurt: "Halikounas is a huge, completely wild, unique beach, a paradise untouched by mass commercial tourism. It's basically a massive tongue of dark, fine sand, over 3 kilometres long, separating the Ionian Sea from the protected, salty Korission Lake. Being constantly exposed to strong offshore winds, Halikounas is known as Corfu's most important meeting point for kitesurfing and windsurfing enthusiasts.",
    cumAjungi: "The beach is on the south-west coast of the island. Public transport doesn't reach this isolated nature reserve at all, so a car is absolutely essential. The road is paved up to the beach entrance, where it turns into a long dirt-and-sand track winding along the dunes. You can drive slowly and park the car completely free wherever you like, right at the edge of the beach.",
    echipament: [{ titlu: "Beach umbrella and a sturdy beach tent", text: "The wind blows almost constantly here, kicking up sand, so a small beach tent will give you extra comfort." }, { titlu: "A well-stocked portable cool box", text: "With the beach being huge and ecologically protected, there are no buildings, hotels or shops nearby." }, { titlu: "No aqua shoes needed", text: "The whole beach and seabed are made exclusively of fine sand, with the open sea entry free of stones." }],
    preturi: "Access and parking along the 3 km of beach are 100% free. In peak season, at one end of the beach there's a single mobile wooden beach bar and a kitesurfing school. A frappe costs €4, and renting kite gear is around €40-50 an hour. For food, you'll need to drive 5 minutes to the taverns in the neighbouring villages.",
    turisti: [{ titlu: "Endless space and freedom", text: "Tourists looking to escape crowded areas praise the beach's impressive size, where you can sit a huge distance from everyone else." }, { titlu: "The colourful kite show", text: "Visitors are fascinated by the dozens of kitesurfers doing spectacular tricks in the sky in the afternoon." }],
    tips: [{ titlu: "Best time to go", text: "If you want to see flamingos or other protected species, cross the small wooden footbridge behind the beach towards Korission Lake early in the morning. If you want a relaxed day on your towel, pick a day from the forecast when the wind is lighter, to avoid blowing sand." }],
  },
  "Plaja Sidari Corfu": {
    scurt: "The main beach in Sidari is the town beach of one of the most developed and lively resorts in the north of the island. It's a very long, wide beach, covered in fine golden sand. The bay is open, but the water is remarkably warm and has a very gentle, shallow entry, with the sea perfectly safe. Behind the beach sits a huge, lively commercial promenade full of hotels and entertainment facilities.",
    cumAjungi: "Sidari is in the north of Corfu, about 36 km from the capital. The road is fully paved but fairly long and mountainous in the central section. A rental car gives you total independence, letting you carry family luggage comfortably. In the resort there are large free public car parks right behind the beach, on dirt, as well as paid car parks (around €4 a day) near the harbour where the boats leave from.",
    echipament: [{ titlu: "Sand toys and large mattresses", text: "It's the ideal beach for activities in the water and on shore, with the sand perfectly clean and free of stones." }, { titlu: "No special footwear needed", text: "Sea entry is exclusively over soft sand, with zero risk of stepping on sea urchins." }, { titlu: "Plenty of sunscreen", text: "With the area open, the sun beats down strongly throughout the day." }],
    preturi: "Sets of two sunbeds with an umbrella are very affordable, costing around €10-12 a day, or offered for free by bars with a similar minimum spend. A frappe costs €3.50, a gyros on the promenade is €4, and a full family dinner at the British or Greek taverns costs around €35-45.",
    turisti: [{ titlu: "Huge commercial infrastructure", text: "English and European tourists praise the huge number of bars, free-access pools, shops and travel agencies behind the beach." }, { titlu: "The water stays shallow for a long way", text: "Parents appreciate the total safety the shallow sea offers for children." }],
    tips: [{ titlu: "Best time to go", text: "This beach is ideal for a full day of family fun. From here you can walk along the rocks in just 10 minutes to also visit the famous Canal d'Amour, located at the left end of the same resort." }],
  },
  "Plaja Kassiopi Corfu": {
    scurt: "Kassiopi beach (more precisely, Kalamionas beach or the little coves around the Kassiopi peninsula) is a picturesque beach in a stunning traditional fishing village in the north-east of the island. Made of a mix of shiny white pebbles and coarse sand, the bay offers water of astonishing transparency, in shades of emerald. The backdrop is dominated by an elegant small yacht harbour and the ruins of an old 14th-century Byzantine fortress perched on the hill.",
    cumAjungi: "Kassiopi is about 35 km north of Corfu Town, along the scenic coastal road. The road is fully paved and spectacular, offering superb views towards the coast of Albania, which is a short distance away. Green local buses run fairly infrequently, making a rental car absolutely necessary for a relaxed trip. Parking near the harbour beaches can be tight; there's a large paid public car park (around €5 a day) at the village entrance, a two-minute walk away.",
    echipament: [{ titlu: "Aqua shoes are a must", text: "Both the main beach and the hidden coves (like Bataria or Pipitos) are exclusively stones and pebbles; walking barefoot is painful." }, { titlu: "Snorkelling mask", text: "With the water deep and flanked by large white cliffs, underwater visibility is legendary, full of colourful fish." }, { titlu: "Comfortable walking sandals", text: "The Byzantine castle ruins behind the harbour are worth a 15-minute visit for a superb view." }],
    preturi: "Renting a set of two sunbeds costs around €12-15 a day. Being an active fishing harbour village, the surrounding taverns are known for excellent food. A frappe costs €3.50, and a delicious lunch of fresh fish or squid costs around €13-16 per person.",
    turisti: [{ titlu: "The Bataria and Pipitos coves are dreamy", text: "Every visitor recommends going past the main beach to the hidden coves behind the peninsula, considered a far more spectacular setting." }, { titlu: "A village full of authentic charm", text: "Tourists appreciate the elegant, quiet atmosphere of the harbour in the evening." }],
    tips: [{ titlu: "Best time to go", text: "Arrive around 9:15 AM. Head straight to Bataria cove (the most beautiful spot in Kassiopi). You'll get the first sunbeds right under the cliffs, the sea will be flat as an aquarium, and you'll be able to swim in total peace before the small cove gets busy." }],
  },
  "Plaja Agathi Archangelos": {
    scurt: "Agathi beach (often known as Golden Beach) is a small gem hidden in a sheltered bay on the east coast of Rhodes. It's a gorgeous beach covered in extremely fine, soft, clean sand of a warm golden tint. The sea has remarkable clarity, a light turquoise colour and is very calm, with no big waves. The atmosphere is warm and relaxing, considered one of the most intimate and pleasant family beaches on the island.",
    cumAjungi: "The beach is near the village of Haraki and about 10 km north of Lindos. Local buses don't have stops near this secluded bay. A rental car is the only comfortable option. From the main road, you follow a secondary road, partly paved and partly compacted dirt, that goes down to the sea, passing a medieval chapel carved into the rock. Parking down below is improvised on dirt behind the beach, spacious and completely free.",
    echipament: [{ titlu: "No aqua shoes needed", text: "The whole bay has a clean seabed, covered exclusively in fine sand, making entry into the shallow sea a pleasure." }, { titlu: "Snorkelling mask", text: "Head towards the rocky edges of the bay; the water's clarity lets you see plenty of small fish hidden among the rocks." }, { titlu: "Sand toys for kids", text: "The quality of the sand here is legendary, ideal for sandcastles." }],
    preturi: "Sets of two sunbeds with an umbrella cost around €12-15 a day. Behind the beach there are 2-3 small wooden taverns/canteens run by locals. A frappe costs €3.50, and a quick lunch of gyros, souvlaki or fresh salad is around €8-11.",
    turisti: [{ titlu: "A safe, clean beach", text: "Parents appreciate the very gentle water entry and the fact that the bay is sheltered from wind, keeping the sea always calm." }, { titlu: "The castle on the hill", text: "Many tourists recommend admiring the ruins of the medieval Feraklos Castle, perched on the nearby mountain, from the beach." }],
    tips: [{ titlu: "Best time to go", text: "Arrive around 9:30 AM. The bay is incredibly quiet in the first part of the day, and the sun lights the golden sand directly, giving the water unique tropical-pool tints. On the way, stop for a minute to visit the small Byzantine rock-carved church of Agios Nikolaos, right on the road to the beach." }],
  },
  "Plaja Kallithea Kallithea": {
    scurt: "Kallithea beach is an elegant, refined destination, famous for its historic thermal baths complex with restored Oriental-Italian architecture, built in the interwar period. The beach itself isn't a large stretch of sand, but a picturesque cove made of rock platforms and small strips of sand, immaculately laid out among palm trees and blooming gardens. The water is incredibly clean, has a deep emerald tint and is considered the number one spot in Rhodes for diving and snorkelling.",
    cumAjungi: "Kallithea Springs is on the east coast, just 9 km south of Rhodes Town and 4 km north of Faliraki. The road is fully paved, modern and very fast. By car you get there in under 10 minutes from the capital. The monumental complex has its own huge car park, excellently laid out on dirt in the shade of trees, where you can leave the vehicle completely free. A car lets you combine a relaxed morning at the baths with an afternoon stroll in Rhodes Old Town.",
    echipament: [{ titlu: "Snorkelling mask and snorkel are a must", text: "The deep, rocky bay is a true natural aquarium. Underwater visibility is legendary, full of colourful fish and small corals hidden in the rock crevices." }, { titlu: "Aqua shoes", text: "Recommended for stepping safely on the rock platforms and cliffs at the sea entry." }, { titlu: "Casual but elegant clothes", text: "The restored complex (with white pavilions, round stone mosaics and fountains) is an architectural masterpiece that calls for a long, magazine-worthy photo session." }],
    preturi: "Entry to the historic complex requires a ticket (around €3-4 per person). Renting a set of two premium sunbeds set right on the rock platforms by the water costs around €15-20. There's an elegant beach bar inside the complex. A frappe costs €4, a water is €1.50, and quick snacks are around €10.",
    turisti: [{ titlu: "A relaxed, refined atmosphere", text: "Tourists praise the stunning design of the location, the background chill-out music, and the immaculate cleanliness of the whole complex." }, { titlu: "A diver's paradise", text: "Every diving enthusiast mentions this as home to the best diving schools on the island." }],
    tips: [{ titlu: "Best time to go", text: "Arrive around 9:15 AM. You'll tour the historic pavilions in pleasant temperatures, grab the best sunbeds right by the sea, and enjoy a fantastic snorkelling session before the sunlight gets too strong." }],
  },
  "Plaja Glystra Lindos": {
    scurt: "Glystra beach is a small oasis of calm and untouched nature, tucked into a perfectly sheltered circular cove in the south-east of the island. It's a small beach, covered in fine, soft, golden sand, entirely flanked by sand dunes and green juniper bushes. The water is shallow, warm as a pool and flat as a mirror, fully sheltered from waves. It's one of the most intimate and relaxing beaches on the island, ideal for reading a book or letting your children play safely.",
    cumAjungi: "Glystra is about 11 km south of Lindos, towards Kiotari. Public transport is rare in this more secluded stretch of coast. By car you get there very easily, as the beach sits right next to the fully paved main road. Parking is free, spacious, laid out on dirt in the shade of trees right behind the beach. This makes driving there extremely convenient, just a one-minute walk from the sunbeds.",
    echipament: [{ titlu: "No aqua shoes needed", text: "The seabed is one continuous stretch of extremely soft, clean sand, with no stones or sea urchins at all." }, { titlu: "Sand toys", text: "If you're travelling with little ones, the fine, mouldable sand here is the best on the island for sandcastles." }, { titlu: "Swimming goggles", text: "With the water extremely calm, it's a pleasure to swim leisurely along the sheltered bay." }],
    preturi: "The beach has a small commercially organised area. A set of two sunbeds with an umbrella costs around €12 a day. Behind the beach there's a single kiosk/canteen run by locals. A frappe costs €3.50, a large water is €1.50, and quick snacks (like a sandwich or a warm pastry) are around €5-7.",
    turisti: [{ titlu: "A well-kept secret", text: "Visitors describe it as the perfect quiet alternative to the crowded beaches in Lindos or Pefkos." }, { titlu: "Extremely gentle sea entry", text: "Parents appreciate in reviews that you can walk dozens of metres out and the water stays shallow, ideal for children." }],
    tips: [{ titlu: "Best time to go", text: "Arrive around 9:30 AM. The bay is especially quiet in the first part of the day, and the sun lights the golden sand directly, giving the water brilliant tints. For a relaxed snorkelling session, head towards the rocky edges enclosing the bay on the left and right." }],
  },
  "Plaja Ladiko Faliraki": {
    scurt: "Ladiko beach is a true natural gem, set in an extremely picturesque rocky cove, right on the other side of the hill from the famous Anthony Quinn beach. It's a small beach made of a pleasant mix of fine sand and white pebbles, tucked between green hills full of pines and unusual rock formations rising straight out of the sea. The water in this bay has legendary clarity, tinted in brilliant shades of emerald, making it an ideal spot for quiet relaxation and snorkelling.",
    cumAjungi: "The bay is about 3 km south of the Faliraki resort and 15 km from Rhodes Town. Local buses don't have direct lines to this secluded bay, leaving you a fair walk away. A rental car is essential to get here comfortably. The road from Faliraki is fully paved, modern and offers superb views. Down at the bottom, there's a large public car park, on dirt right behind the beach, where you can leave the vehicle completely free. Shaded spots fill up quickly in season, though.",
    echipament: [{ titlu: "Snorkelling mask and snorkel are a must", text: "The underwater rocky terrain in this sheltered bay is full of life. Visibility is excellent, making it an ideal spot to watch schools of fish foraging around the rocks." }, { titlu: "Aqua shoes", text: "Although there's plenty of sand on shore, the sea entry has flat stones and underwater rocks where sea urchins can be found." }, { titlu: "Large towel or mat", text: "With the bay being small, sunbeds are set fairly close together in season." }],
    preturi: "A set of two sunbeds with an umbrella costs around €12-15 a day. There's an excellent family-run traditional tavern on the beach. A frappe costs €3.50, a large water is €1.50, and a warm lunch of traditional Greek dishes or seafood at the tavern costs around €12-15 per person.",
    turisti: [{ titlu: "An emerald pool", text: "All tourists praise the water's unique colour and stunning clarity in this bay, naturally sheltered from big waves." }, { titlu: "More relaxed than Anthony Quinn", text: "Many visitors note that Ladiko has a bit more sand on shore and a somewhat more accessible atmosphere for relaxing than its neighbouring bay." }],
    tips: [{ titlu: "Best time to go", text: "Arrive around 9:00 AM. With the bay being small and very popular, front-row sunbeds and good parking spots fill up completely by 10:30 AM. Plus, the sea is especially calm in the morning, ideal for a long snorkelling session before lunch." }],
  },
  "Plaja Pefkos Lindos": {
    scurt: "Pefkos beach (also officially known as Lee Beach) is a gorgeous, very welcoming beach facing the charming resort of the same name. Its name comes from the old pine trees (\"pefko\") flanking the bay, giving the air a unique scent of resin and salty breeze. The beach is covered in extremely fine, warm golden sand, and the sea is very shallow near shore, clean and completely free of big waves, offering an extremely intimate, relaxing atmosphere.",
    cumAjungi: "Pefkos is just 5 km south of the famous village of Lindos. A rental car will get you there quickly on the main paved road, avoiding the crowds and high prices of Lindos. With the resort spread across hills, a car gives you extra comfort for driving right down behind the beach. There are small dirt car parks behind the main bars, or free spots along the streets leading to the sea, but spaces fill up fast after 10:00 AM.",
    echipament: [{ titlu: "No aqua shoes needed", text: "The seabed is one continuous stretch of fine, soft, clean sand, with zero risk of stepping on sea urchins." }, { titlu: "Snorkelling mask", text: "In the areas where the beach ends and the rocks at the edge of the bay begin, underwater life is very active." }, { titlu: "Sand toys for kids", text: "The quality of the sand here is ideal for little ones, being fine and compact at the water's edge." }],
    preturi: "Depending on the bar you choose, a set of two sunbeds with an umbrella costs between €12-15 a day. A frappe costs €3.50, a cold beer is €4, and a quick gyros or club sandwich lunch is around €6-8. The taverns behind the beach are excellent, with a family meal reaching €35-45.",
    turisti: [{ titlu: "The perfect alternative to Lindos", text: "Many tourists consider it in reviews a much airier, cheaper and more relaxed option than the beaches in Lindos." }, { titlu: "Excellent for kids", text: "Parents unanimously praise the extremely gentle water entry and the total lack of big waves." }],
    tips: [{ titlu: "Best time to go", text: "Arrive around 9:15 AM. The bay is especially quiet in the first part of the day. If you want a completely free area for your towel, head to the right end of the beach (the area called Kavos Beach), where the atmosphere is much more secluded and rocky." }],
  },
  "Plaja Ialyssos Rhodos Town": {
    scurt: "Ialyssos beach (or Trianda) is a long, cosmopolitan stretch of coast in the north-west of the island, facing one of the largest and most developed resorts in Rhodes. Similar to its neighbour, Ixia, the beach is made of a mix of white pebbles and coarse sand. It's a world-famous location for windsurfing and kitesurfing, thanks to the constant winds blowing in from the sea that create long waves ideal for dynamic water sports.",
    cumAjungi: "Ialyssos is about 8 km west of Rhodes Town. The main coastal road is fully paved, straight and very fast to drive. Buses run frequently, but a rental car gives you extra comfort for carrying heavy beach bags and gear. Finding a parking spot is fairly simple: there are numerous free public spaces along the long lanes running from the resort centre straight down to the sea, or on the roadside near the beach.",
    echipament: [{ titlu: "Aqua shoes are a must", text: "The large pebbles on shore and at the sea entry can be very uncomfortable underfoot." }, { titlu: "Budget for water sports", text: "Ialyssos hosts international windsurfing competitions; it's worth taking a lesson with a licensed instructor from the centres on the shore." }, { titlu: "Casual clothes for the promenade", text: "The area behind the beach has a long pedestrian promenade full of modern cafes, restaurants and lively shops." }],
    preturi: "Sets of two sunbeds with an umbrella cost around €10-12 a day, being very affordable. A frappe costs €3.50, a gyros on the promenade is €4, and a full family dinner at the excellent taverns behind the beach costs around €35-45.",
    turisti: [{ titlu: "Huge commercial infrastructure", text: "Tourists appreciate the huge number of bars, free-access pools, hotels and facilities behind the beach." }, { titlu: "Unforgettable sunsets", text: "As along the entire west coast, the sunset seen from the beach is considered a must-see daily attraction." }],
    tips: [{ titlu: "Best time to go", text: "If you want a calm swim, come in the morning between 8:30-11:00 AM, when the sea is calm. If you want action, come in the afternoon to watch the show of dozens of colourful sails filling the sky. After the beach, take the car and drive 10 minutes up the neighbouring Filerimos mountain to visit the historic monastery and see the peacocks roaming freely through the forest." }],
  },
  "Plaja Kedrodasos Chania": {
    scurt: "We leave Rhodes and head back to Crete for one of the wildest, most spectacular and unique beaches in all of Greece: Kedrodasos. Its name means \"Cedar Forest\", since the beach is flanked by a huge ancient forest of junipers and centuries-old cedars growing right out of the white sand. The water of the Libyan Sea here has an incredible electric-turquoise tint and is crystal clear. It's a completely unspoiled place, with no facilities, considered a true natural sanctuary.",
    cumAjungi: "The beach is in the far south-west of Crete, just 2-3 km from the famous Elafonisi beach. There's no public transport here, so a rental car is absolutely mandatory. From the main paved road leading to Elafonisi, a rough dirt-and-stone secondary track branches off, full of bumps, which you need to drive slowly. At the end of the road you leave the car for free in an improvised car park, and from there you still have about a 10-15 minute walk on an unmarked rocky path through the sun to the sand.",
    echipament: [{ titlu: "Your own beach umbrella and mat", text: "Kedrodasos is 100% public and unorganised. Although the cedars offer natural shade at the edges, the trees are legally protected and it's forbidden to break branches or camp directly beneath them." }, { titlu: "A cool box full of water and snacks", text: "The nearest shop is several kilometres away, in the Elafonisi area." }, { titlu: "Comfortable walking shoes (trainers)", text: "The path from the car park down is rocky and slippery in beach flip-flops." }],
    preturi: "Access to the beach and parking are completely free and open. There are no facilities, kiosks or beach bars down there, so your cost here will be zero. For a warm lunch after the beach, it's best to drive 10 minutes back to the small family taverns in the villages along the road to Chania.",
    turisti: [{ titlu: "A quiet alternative to Elafonisi", text: "All reviews praise it as the perfect place to escape the thousands of tourists at Elafonisi, offering total privacy in nature." }, { titlu: "An idyllic landscape", text: "Visitors are fascinated by the contrast between the white sand, the black volcanic rocks and the old cedars." }],
    tips: [{ titlu: "Best time to go", text: "Arrive around 9:00 AM. You'll get a much more pleasant temperature for the walk down from the car park and can pick the best spots on the sand. Note that the beach is very popular with naturist communities and campers seeking quiet, so respect for nature and discretion are unwritten local rules." }],
  },
  "Plaja Sougia Chania": {
    scurt: "Sougia is a huge, relaxing beach full of character, on the south coast of Crete. Stretching over a kilometre along a quiet bay, the beach is made of clean, medium-sized pebbles and dark coarse sand. What makes it unique is the feeling of total isolation and freedom: it's one of the few large beaches in Crete that has remained mostly unorganised, keeping that bohemian 1970s vibe. The water is incredibly deep, clean and a regal, dark blue.",
    cumAjungi: "Sougia village is about 70 km south of Chania. The road crossing the island through the White Mountains (Lefka Ori) is spectacular, fully paved, but full of tight switchbacks, narrow stretches and steep slopes. Local buses run extremely rarely (often just once or twice a day). A rental car is absolutely necessary to travel safely and at your own pace. Once you're down there, parking is extremely simple: there's a huge, free public space set up right behind the beach, in the shade of trees.",
    echipament: [{ titlu: "Aqua shoes are a must", text: "Both on shore and at the sea entry there are large stones and pebbles that get very hot at midday." }, { titlu: "Your own beach umbrella", text: "Although there's a small central area with sunbeds, over 80% of the beach is completely free. If you grab a spot early under the tamarisk trees at the edge, you'll have natural shade all day." }, { titlu: "Snorkelling mask", text: "With the water extremely deep right from shore and very clear, the underwater rocky terrain is ideal to explore." }],
    preturi: "Sougia is one of the most affordable destinations in Crete. A set of two sunbeds with an umbrella costs around €8-10. The village behind has fantastic family taverns. A frappe costs €3, a cold beer is €3.50, and a hearty lunch of traditional Cretan food will cost around €10-12 per person.",
    turisti: [{ titlu: "Total disconnection from technology", text: "Tourists praise the mystical quiet of the place; there are no clubs or loud music on the beach." }, { titlu: "Mind the water depth", text: "Reviews warn that the water gets very deep after just two steps from shore, not recommended for young children left unsupervised." }],
    tips: [{ titlu: "Best time to go", text: "Stay on the beach until sunset. At the left end of the beach (the area historically favoured by naturists and campers), huge rocks block the sun earlier, but offer an incredible natural backdrop for twilight photos." }],
  },
  "Plaja Damnoni Rethymno": {
    scurt: "Damnoni beach is a gorgeous, very modern beach in a small bay next to the resort of Plakias. It's covered in coarse white sand mixed with fine pebbles, which gives the sea a stunningly clear light-turquoise colour, similar to an Olympic pool. Being naturally sheltered by two large rocky headlands, Damnoni is much more protected from the strong southern winds than the main beach in Plakias, offering a calm, safe sea.",
    cumAjungi: "The beach is just 5 km east of Plakias and about 33 km from Rethymno. Public transport doesn't reach this beach directly, stopping in the main resort instead. A rental car is absolutely mandatory to get down into the bay. The road is paved, gently descending through olive groves. Parking down below is huge, laid out on dirt behind the beach and completely free, just a one-minute walk from the sand.",
    echipament: [{ titlu: "Budget for water sports", text: "Damnoni is home to one of the best water sports centres in southern Crete (kayak, windsurfing, water skiing or boat rental)." }, { titlu: "Aqua shoes", text: "Although there's plenty of clean sand on shore, the pebbles at the sea entry can be a little uncomfortable underfoot." }, { titlu: "Snorkelling mask", text: "The rocky area at the right end of the bay is full of small fish and interesting underwater formations." }],
    preturi: "A set of two sunbeds with an umbrella costs around €12-15 a day. Behind the beach there are 2-3 excellent family taverns, known for their grilled meat dishes and local olives. A frappe costs €3.50, and a full lunch comes to about €13-15 per person.",
    turisti: [{ titlu: "More sheltered than Plakias", text: "Many tourists note in reviews that on days when the wind is too strong in Plakias, Damnoni is the perfect refuge, with a much calmer sea." }, { titlu: "Spotless cleanliness", text: "All visitors praise the water's transparency and the beach's excellent organisation." }],
    tips: [{ titlu: "Best time to go", text: "Arrive around 9:30 AM. The bay is incredibly calm then, and the sunlight gives the water brilliant tints. From here you can also take small water taxis for a few-hour trip to the famous palm-fringed Preveli beach." }],
  },
  "Plaja Agios Pavlos Rethymno": {
    scurt: "Agios Pavlos (Saint Paul) is one of the most isolated, spectacular and wild locations in southern Crete. The area is famous for its two beaches: a small, rocky, extremely sheltered cove next to a small fishing settlement, and the large beach to the left (known as the Sand Dunes Beach). Here, huge dunes of dark, fine sand descend spectacularly from the mountain straight into the Libyan Sea. It's a place of primitive, dramatic beauty, perfect for those wanting to feel at the edge of the world.",
    cumAjungi: "The location is in the far south of the Rethymno region, far from any commercial tourist route. Public transport doesn't reach here at all, so a car is absolutely mandatory. The access road from the main road is paved, but very narrow, full of tight switchbacks and steep descents along the cliff edge. You can park the car completely free in the dirt car park above the small cove. To reach the big dunes beach, you have a short walk over rocks and a steep descent straight onto the sand.",
    echipament: [{ titlu: "Your own beach umbrella and a beach tent", text: "On the big dunes beach there is absolutely no facility, shop or natural shade. It's just you, the hot sand and the sea." }, { titlu: "Footwear with good grip (trainers)", text: "Going down, and especially climbing back up the steep sand dunes, is tiring and impossible in beach flip-flops." }, { titlu: "Snorkelling mask", text: "The water has astonishing clarity, and the unique folded rock formations (layered cliffs) on the edge continue underwater, offering fantastic underwater scenery." }],
    preturi: "Entry to the beaches is free. In the small cove, organisation is minimal, with a set of sunbeds costing around €8-10. Above the cove there's a single family tavern with a dreamy view. A frappe costs €3, and a portion of home-cooked Cretan food costs around €9-12.",
    turisti: [{ titlu: "A breathtaking landscape", text: "All tourists are fascinated by the grandeur of the sand dunes and the total quiet of the place, far from civilisation." }, { titlu: "Climbing the dunes is tough", text: "Reviews warn that the effort of climbing back up the sandy hill at midday is considerable and requires stamina." }],
    tips: [{ titlu: "Best time to go", text: "Stay on the big dunes beach until sunset. Agios Pavlos is considered one of the most spiritual and spectacular spots in Crete to watch the sun set straight into the sea, with the layered cliff profile offering unique, memorable photos." }],
  },
  "Plaja Triopetra Rethymno": {
    scurt: "Triopetra beach takes its name from the three huge, spectacular, layered rocks (trio petra — three stones in Greek) that rise majestically out of the sea at the tip of the peninsula, splitting the beach into two distinct zones. It's an immense beach, made of clean coarse sand mixed with fine pebbles, stretching for kilometres along the Libyan Sea. The water here is renowned for its crystal purity and deep blue tints. The place gives off a special energy, being a wild, breezy beach full of natural grandeur.",
    cumAjungi: "Triopetra is on the south coast of the Rethymno region, completely isolated from the major towns. There are no bus lines reaching this wild area. A rental car is indispensable for covering the paved road that winds through mountains and olive groves. The final descent to the sea is spectacular. Parking is extremely simple: with the beach being huge, you can leave the car completely free in the large dirt areas behind the dunes or right next to the small taverns on the shore.",
    echipament: [{ titlu: "Your own beach umbrella and mat", text: "Although there are small organised areas near the two taverns, over 90% of this huge beach is completely free and wild." }, { titlu: "Aqua shoes", text: "Recommended for walking comfortably at the sea entry, where flat underwater rock slabs can appear." }, { titlu: "Snorkelling mask", text: "The area around the three huge rocks in the sea is a top spot for snorkelling, full of fish and stone channels to explore." }],
    preturi: "If you grab a spot in the small organised area, a set of two sunbeds costs around €10, or is included if you order lunch at one of the two family taverns behind the beach. A frappe costs €3.50, a portion of fresh tzatziki is €4, and traditional oven-baked dishes cost around €10-13.",
    turisti: [{ titlu: "Endless space and unique energy", text: "All visitors praise the beach's impressive size, where you can enjoy the sea in total peace, with no crowds, even in August." }, { titlu: "Wind can create big waves", text: "Reviews mention that, being completely open to the south, the northern wind can create spectacular waves and strong currents." }],
    tips: [{ titlu: "Best time to go", text: "Visit the small beach east of the rocks first (Little Triopetra), which is more sheltered from the wind, then move to the large west beach in the afternoon. Walk to the base of the three huge rocks at sunset — the perfect geological layers in the stone offer an incredible backdrop for professional holiday photos." }],
  },
  "Plaja Agiofaraggo Heraklion": {
    scurt: "Agiofaraggo (translated as \"Canyon of the Saints\") is one of the most mystical, isolated and astonishing wild destinations in all of Greece. Set at the end of a deep canyon flanked by huge vertical rock walls, the beach opens up suddenly onto the Libyan Sea like a divine reward. It's a small, perfectly sheltered bay, covered in fine, round white pebbles, with water of unreal transparency, coloured in deep shades of emerald. The place was once a refuge for hermits and still carries an energy of absolute peace.",
    cumAjungi: "The beach is in the far south of the Heraklion region and completely isolated. A car with good ground clearance or extremely careful driving are vital, since a rough forest track of dirt and stone, about 5-6 km long and full of bumps, starts from the Odigitria Monastery. At the end of the road you leave the car for free in an improvised car park, and from there begins a spectacular 25-30 minute hike through the deep canyon gorge, walking along a dry riverbed among oleanders and wild pines.",
    echipament: [{ titlu: "Comfortable walking shoes (trainers)", text: "The route through the canyon needs care, being full of large stones, and walking in flip-flops is not recommended at all." }, { titlu: "A full backpack with food, water and an umbrella", text: "Agiofaraggo is 100% unspoiled. There are no shops, bars, sunbeds or phone signal down there. You're completely on your own in the middle of nature." }, { titlu: "Snorkelling mask is a must", text: "The vertical rock walls drop straight into the deep, clear sea, creating a fantastic underwater landscape full of fish, caves and stone channels to explore." }],
    preturi: "Access to the beach, walking the canyon and parking are all completely free. There's no commercial facility in the area, so your direct cost on the beach will be zero. Along the canyon route you can visit for free the historic 14th-century Agios Antonios chapel and the old hermits' cave nearby.",
    turisti: [{ titlu: "A unique spiritual experience", text: "All tourists are overwhelmed by the beauty of the canyon hike and the sight of the beach suddenly appearing among the huge rocks at the end of the path." }, { titlu: "Watch out for the wild goats", text: "Reviews often mention the friendly semi-wild goats in the canyon, which come very close to tourists to steal food from their backpacks." }],
    tips: [{ titlu: "Best time to go", text: "Start the hike early in the morning, around 9:00 AM. The canyon is cool and partly shaded then, and by the time you reach the beach you'll find the sea flat as a mirror and total peace, before the small excursion boats that sometimes come from Matala arrive in the afternoon." }],
  },
  "Plaja Voulisma Lasithi": {
    scurt: "Voulisma beach (often known as Golden Beach) is one of the most beautiful and well-organised beaches in eastern Crete. Set in the picturesque Mirabello bay, near the town of Istro, the beach will amaze you with its spectacular colour contrast: powder-fine white sand meets water of an incredibly bright electric turquoise. The bay is flanked by yellow earth walls covered in green shrubs, giving the beach an exotic look, similar to a lagoon on some far-off island.",
    cumAjungi: "Voulisma is about 12 km south-east of Agios Nikolaos town, along the main paved road leading to Sitia. A rental car is the most comfortable way to travel, letting you cover the route quickly and make stops along the superb Mirabello bay coastline. Above the beach there's a large public dirt car park where you can leave the vehicle completely free. From the car park, the way down to the sand is via a long, nicely laid-out stone staircase.",
    echipament: [{ titlu: "No aqua shoes needed", text: "The whole bay has a seabed covered in soft, fine sand, and entry into the clean sea is a real pleasure." }, { titlu: "Good sunglasses", text: "Light reflecting off the white sand and the turquoise water is very strong around midday." }, { titlu: "A backpack instead of bags", text: "The long stone stairs from the car park are easier to go down or up with your hands free." }],
    preturi: "Being a very popular top-tier beach, it's fully organised. A set of two sunbeds with an umbrella costs around €15-20 a day. Right at the top of the stairs above the beach, there's a modern snack bar. A frappe costs €4, a large water is €1.50, and a quick gyros or club sandwich lunch is around €8-10.",
    turisti: [{ titlu: "The water's colour is incredible", text: "All reviews praise the bay's unique turquoise tints, mentioning it as one of the most beautiful waters in all of Crete." }, { titlu: "Gets crowded fast", text: "Tourists warn that, with the beach being narrow, sunbeds are placed fairly close together, and the place gets tight after 10:30 AM." }],
    tips: [{ titlu: "Best time to go", text: "Arrive at the car park around 9:00 AM. You'll get a good shaded parking spot, be able to pick the best front-row sunbeds, and enjoy the sea while it's completely calm, like a pool. Note that, with the bay open to the north, strong wind (Meltemi) days can bring big waves and seaweed to shore; pick a calm day from the forecast for a perfect experience." }],
  },
  "Plaja Tsigrado Milos": {
    scurt: "Tsigrado is probably the most adventurous, isolated and talked-about beach on Milos. It's a tiny cove of incredible wild charm, squeezed between tall, steep walls of reddish volcanic rock. The sand below is fine and white, and the water is calm, shallow near shore and has a clean emerald tint. What makes it famous worldwide is the access: to reach the sand, you have to climb down through a narrow crack in the rock, using an old wooden ladder and a rope anchored into the stone.",
    cumAjungi: "The beach is on the south coast of the island. There's no public transport reaching this rocky, secluded area. A rental car is essential. The final road is partly paved and partly compacted dirt, easy to drive if you go slowly. You can leave the car completely free in the large dirt car park right on the plateau above the cliffs. From there, it's a one-minute walk to the edge of the drop where the ladder begins.",
    echipament: [{ titlu: "Trainers or shoes with good grip", text: "Climbing down the ladder and rope through the narrow, sandy, slippery passage is dangerous in plain beach flip-flops." }, { titlu: "A backpack instead of handbags", text: "It's vital to have both hands free to hold onto the rope and the ladder rungs during the climb down." }, { titlu: "Your own umbrella and water", text: "The cove is completely wild, natural shade only appears late in the afternoon under the cliff, and there are no commercial facilities down there." }],
    preturi: "Access to the beach and parking up top are completely free and open. There are no vendors down on the sand. For food or drinks, it's easiest to drive two minutes to the neighbouring organised beach, Firiplaka, which has a modern beach bar.",
    turisti: [{ titlu: "Not for everyone", text: "Tourists often warn that people who suffer from vertigo or claustrophobia, or families with very young children, should avoid the climb down, as the beach can be safely admired from above, at the cliff edge." }, { titlu: "An unforgettable adventure", text: "Those who make the climb praise the \"secret beach\" vibe and the beauty of the water." }],
    tips: [{ titlu: "Best time to go", text: "Arrive early in the morning, around 8:30-9:00 AM. You'll climb down the ladder safely, without having to wait in line in the narrow passage (where bottlenecks form when other tourists try to climb up), and you'll get the tiny patch of sand completely to yourself." }],
  },
  "Plaja Provatas Milos": {
    scurt: "Provatas beach is a charming, extremely welcoming destination, set in a wide bay on the island's south coast. It's known on Milos as \"Golden Beach\", due to its fine sand with an unusually warm reddish-golden colour. The sea here is clean, calm, sheltered from the big waves that come from the north, and very shallow for a generous distance out. It's considered the most accessible, comfortable beach on the island for families with young children.",
    cumAjungi: "Provatas is about 13 km south of the main port, Adamas. The main road crossing the island south is fully paved, modern and very fast to drive. A rental car gives you full comfort, sparing you the rigid schedule of the seasonal buses. Parking down below is public, spacious, laid out on dirt right behind the beach and completely free, offering very easy car access, just a one-minute walk from the sunbeds.",
    echipament: [{ titlu: "Sand toys for kids", text: "The reddish-golden sand is very fine, clean and mouldable, ideal for little ones." }, { titlu: "No special footwear needed", text: "The bay's seabed is one continuous stretch of fine, soft sand, completely free of stones or sea urchins." }, { titlu: "Strong sunscreen", text: "With the water shallow and warm, kids will tend to spend hours in the sea without feeling the heat." }],
    preturi: "The beach is very well organised. Renting a set of two sunbeds with an umbrella costs around €12-15 a day. Right above the beach, on the hill, there are a few excellent traditional taverns. A frappe costs €3.50, and a full lunch of Cretan/Cycladic dishes or fresh fish costs around €12-15 per person.",
    turisti: [{ titlu: "The safest beach for kids", text: "All families praise in reviews that the sea stays shallow and warm like a natural pool for a long way out." }, { titlu: "Extremely simple access", text: "Unlike Tsigrado or Sarakiniko, tourists appreciate that here you don't have to climb down stairs or difficult rocks, with everything at road level." }],
    tips: [{ titlu: "Best time to go", text: "Arrive around 9:30 AM to pick the best front-row sunbeds. With the bay facing south, it's an excellent strategic stop on days when the north wind (Meltemi) blows strongly on the island and creates big waves on the northern beaches (like Sarakiniko), while in Provatas the sea stays completely calm." }],
  },
  "Plaja Pollonia Milos": {
    scurt: "Pollonia beach is the town beach of the charming fishing village in the north-east corner of Milos island. It's a quiet, crescent-shaped bay, covered in fine golden sand, naturally shaded by a generous row of tamarisk trees. The sea is warm, extremely clean and very shallow near shore, sheltered from big waves by a rocky peninsula. The atmosphere here is typically Cycladic, relaxed and bohemian, with wooden boats slowly swaying at anchor.",
    cumAjungi: "Pollonia is about 10 km from the main port, Adamas. Although there's a local bus line, a rental car gives you extra comfort and the freedom of not depending on a rigid evening schedule. The road is fully paved, modern and very simple. A huge advantage is parking: there's an immense public space, laid out for free on dirt right at the village entrance, just a two-minute walk from the sand. From Pollonia harbour you can take a short ferry to visit the neighbouring island, Kimolos.",
    echipament: [{ titlu: "No aqua shoes needed", text: "The seabed inside the bay is entirely made of fine, clean, extremely soft sand." }, { titlu: "Mat or large towel", text: "The tamarisk forest on the beach offers dense, free natural shade, perfect for sitting right on the ground." }, { titlu: "Sand toys", text: "It's an ideal spot for children, with the sand perfect for activities at the water's edge." }],
    preturi: "The beach has a small area organised with sunbeds, where a set costs around €12-15 a day. The village is known for some of the best fish taverns on the island, set right along the seafront. A frappe costs €3.50, a portion of grilled octopus is around €14-16, and a full meal for two comes to €40.",
    turisti: [{ titlu: "Everything within reach", text: "Visitors greatly appreciate the proximity to bakeries, supermarkets, playgrounds and excellent restaurants." }, { titlu: "Peace and safety", text: "All families praise the lack of big waves and the fact that you can enjoy dinner while the kids play on the sand, just a few metres away." }],
    tips: [{ titlu: "Best time to go", text: "Stay in Pollonia for dinner. The bay has an incredibly warm, picturesque atmosphere at sunset, when the tavern lights come on along the shore, reflecting in the calm sea." }],
  },
  "Plaja Achivadolimni Milos": {
    scurt: "Achivadolimni is the longest sandy beach on the island, set right inside Milos's huge natural bay. Its name comes from \"clams\" and \"lake\", after a small nearby lake full of shells. It's an immense strip of light-coloured fine sand, caressed by a clean sea ranging from light blue to turquoise. Thanks to its impressive size, the beach offers a rare feeling of open space and total freedom, spared from the noise of major commercial crowds.",
    cumAjungi: "The beach is about 6 km south of Adamas, on the road to the airport. Public transport has stops on the main road above the dunes, but a rental car is much more comfortable for carrying umbrellas and cool boxes. The road is fully paved and very fast. Parking is huge, free and open right along the secondary road that follows the beach line, just a one-minute walk from the water.",
    echipament: [{ titlu: "Your own umbrella and a beach tent", text: "Most of this immense beach is completely wild and unorganised, and pines are rare in the dune area." }, { titlu: "Windsurfing or kitesurfing gear", text: "On days when the north wind picks up, the open bay at Achivadolimni offers excellent conditions on the island for these sports." }, { titlu: "No aqua shoes needed", text: "Sea entry is very gentle, exclusively over soft, clean sand, free of stones." }],
    preturi: "Access to the beach and parking are free. In season, there's a small area organised by a nearby campsite, where a set of sunbeds costs around €10-12. A mobile canteen sells cold water and frappes for €3-4. For a full hot meal, it's best to drive 5 minutes back towards Adamas harbour.",
    turisti: [{ titlu: "Unlimited space", text: "Tourists are delighted they don't have to sit close to others, the beach being ideal for long walks along the water's edge." }, { titlu: "Gentle entry", text: "Praised by families for the shallow water depth over a good distance from shore." }],
    tips: [{ titlu: "Best time to go", text: "Come in the morning on days when the forecast calls for light wind. The bay will be calm, flat as a mirror, and the water will have a gorgeous turquoise colour. The northern part of the beach is fairly popular with windsurfing fans thanks to the steady afternoon breeze." }],
  },
};
